<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__conditionalfinding_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#findingStatement> "Where wind components are close to Gaussian shape and without too much anisotropy, all fits are quite close and rather accurate, except on the tail where only the non-Gaussian distribution does not underestimate the strong-wind probability." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__conditionalfinding_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#findingScope> "most stations in north-western France" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__conditionalfinding_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportedInStudy> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__study_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__conditionalfinding_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#findingOutcome> "does not underestimate strong-wind probability in the distribution tail" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__conditionalfinding_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#underCondition> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__condition_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__conditionalfinding_002> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#ConditionalFinding> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__conditionalfinding_002> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#findingStatement> "In complex mountain regions with anisotropy and/or departure from Gaussian wind-component shape, either the elliptical or the non-Gaussian distribution can be better suited than Weibull to represent wind statistics." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__conditionalfinding_002> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#findingScope> "southern and eastern France" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__conditionalfinding_002> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportedInStudy> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__study_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__conditionalfinding_002> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#findingOutcome> "can be better suited than Weibull" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__conditionalfinding_002> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#underCondition> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__condition_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__conditionalfinding_003> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#ConditionalFinding> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__conditionalfinding_003> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#findingStatement> "The Rayleigh–Rice distribution gives excellent results especially at weather stations in the Rhône or Aude valleys, where channelled flows create shouldered distributions that Weibull and other two-parameter distributions are not able to reproduce." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__conditionalfinding_003> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#findingScope> "Rhône and Aude valleys" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__conditionalfinding_003> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportedInStudy> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__study_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__conditionalfinding_003> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#findingOutcome> "gives excellent results and reproduces shouldered distributions" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__conditionalfinding_003> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#underCondition> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__condition_004> .
