<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__conditionalfinding_004> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#findingStatement> "The Rayleigh–Rice distribution generally performs better during winter, which the authors explain by a higher probability of persistent strong winds producing a secondary peak or shoulder at higher wind speeds." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__conditionalfinding_004> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#findingScope> "France" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__conditionalfinding_004> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportedInStudy> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__study_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__conditionalfinding_004> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#findingOutcome> "generally performs better during winter" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__conditionalfinding_004> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#underCondition> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__condition_003> .
