<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1378024__problem_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#researchProblemStatement> "An objective and accurate method is needed to describe the nonlinear transfer from 10 m wind speed to 100 m wind speed over large regions because constant-exponent extrapolation ignores spatiotemporal variability, atmospheric stability, and surface roughness." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1378028__problem_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#ResearchProblem> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1378028__problem_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#ResourceUnderexploration> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1378028__problem_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#researchProblemStatement> "Machine-learning methods have seen limited use for predicting wind speed at turbine hub height from measurements at lower heights, while most vertical wind-speed extrapolation studies have used classical methods." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689577__problem_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#ResearchProblem> .
