<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689600__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Studies comparing different methods for estimating Weibull parameters in Nigeria are very scarce, and the accuracy of the available estimation methods has received little attention." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689600__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689600__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689600__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "ChiSquareStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689600__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study compared five statistical distribution methods for estimating Weibull parameters at twelve Nigerian stations and evaluated their accuracy with three goodness-of-fit tests." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689600__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Use more estimation methods and more goodness-of-fit tests in future studies to identify the estimation method with the best effectiveness." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689600__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The performance of Weibull-parameter estimation methods varied from station to station and depended on the goodness-of-fit measure used." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689605__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689605__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689605__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Hourly wind data for 2008–2010 at Catalca were measured at 10 m and extrapolated to 30, 60, and 80 m. A two-parameter Weibull distribution was fitted using graphical, method of moments, energy pattern factor, mean standard deviation, power density, and genetic algorithm methods. Performance was compared using MAE, RMSE, NMAE, Chi-square error, R2, and Net Fitness." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689605__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "All six estimation methods almost fitted the measured data, although the 2010 Weibull PDF and CDF curves deviated considerably from the real-data curve." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689605__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "GA and GM were respectively the first- and second-best methods in terms of MAE, RMSE, and R2, whereas EPF outperformed the other methods in terms of NMAE and Chi-square error." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689605__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Based on the aggregate Net Fitness ranking, the methods ranked from best to worst as GA, PD, GM, MOM, MSD, and EPF." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689605__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "No method ranked best for all cases, and the suitability of an estimation method depends on factors including data size, data shape, and the selected goodness-of-fit measures." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689605__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The reported annual average power densities indicated that the Catalca site is suitable for wind power generation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689605__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689605__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689605__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689605__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689605__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689605__objective_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689605__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689605__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689605__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689605__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689605__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R689605__analysis_002> .
