<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R702341__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Further investigation of the wind regime and diurnal wind patterns should be carried out because only 1 year of data was available." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R702341__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The available data covered only 1 year, so the authors stated that no conclusive results should safely be drawn and that further investigation was needed." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703000__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703000__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703000__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Three-hour wind-speed data from 2003–2007 at 10 m for five sites in Semnan province were analyzed, with wind speeds at 30 m and 40 m obtained by Power Law extrapolation. Ten-minute wind-speed and wind-direction data collected during 2007 at Moalleman, Haddadeh, and Kahak were also statistically characterized. Weibull distributions, wind power density, wind roses, turbulence, and annual energy capture by five wind-turbine models were evaluated." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703000__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Damghan had the best wind conditions among the five towns, and Moalleman was the best of the subsequently examined sites. At Moalleman, reported power-density ranges were 172–177 W/m2 at 10 m, 257–277 W/m2 at 30 m, and 303–329 W/m2 at 40 m. Prevailing winds were generally from the southwest. The larger turbine considered could produce more than 2000 MWh during 2007. Moalleman was explicitly classified as a class 3 wind-power site and considered suitable for grid-connected and stand-alone applications." .
