<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703000__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Assessment of wind-energy potential and wind-turbine feasibility in Semnan province." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703000__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The detailed Moalleman assessment and turbine-energy calculation were based on data for the year 2007." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703000__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703000__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703003__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703003__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703003__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Five years of three-hourly wind-speed data for Zahedan (2003–2007), measured at 10 m, were statistically analysed using a two-parameter Weibull distribution. Weibull parameters were estimated with the standard deviation method" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703003__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "wind speeds were extrapolated to 20 m and 30 m" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703003__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "four small wind turbines were simulated using Windographer" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703003__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "and costs of electricity were estimated." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703003__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For the 2003–2007 period, the average Weibull shape parameter, scale parameter, wind power density, and wind energy density were 1.155, 3.401 m/s, 89.184 W/m2, and 781.252 kWh/m2, respectively. Zahedan falls into PNL wind power class 1 overall, and the potential for wind-energy development is limited, although it may be appropriate for low-capacity wind turbines in rural and small communities. Proven 2.5 kW was the most economical of the four assessed turbine models, while Bergey Excel-R produced the highest annual electricity output." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703003__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703003__objective_001> .
