<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703003__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703003__energysystem_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Measured wind-speed data from three Taiwanese wind farms for 2006–2008 were converted from 10-min measurements to hourly data and averaged over 3 years. Conventional Weibull, Gamma–Weibull, Normal–Normal, Normal–Weibull, Weibull–Weibull, and maximum-entropy-principle probability density functions were compared using Kolmogorov–Smirnov maximum error, RMSE, Chi-square error, and relative percent error of wind potential energy." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For the unimodal wind-speed distribution at station A, superiority of the four mixture probability density functions and the maximum-entropy-principle function relative to the conventional Weibull function was not significant. For the bimodal distributions at stations B and C, all mixture functions and the maximum-entropy-principle function described wind characterizations better than the conventional Weibull function for both wind-speed and wind-power-density analyses. The proposed Gamma–Weibull probability density function performed best in the Kolmogorov–Smirnov test for wind-speed analyses, while the maximum-entropy-principle and Gamma–Weibull functions performed best for wind-power-density analyses." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__location_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__problem_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Systematical analysis about the suitability of mixture probability functions and maximum-entropy-principle functions together with conventional Weibull function in a single study had rarely been found in the literature." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "ChiSquareStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RelativePercentError" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study compared four mixture probability density functions and a maximum-entropy-principle function with the conventional Weibull function using wind-speed data from three wind farms with different climatic environments." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703006__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The maximum-entropy-principle probability density function has a more complex mathematical expression for computer programming, requires more computation time to determine parameters, and its cumulative distribution function could not be expressed in a closed form." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703009__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703009__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703009__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Monthly mean wind-speed data measured at 10 m for Enugu, Owerri and Onitsha were analysed using a two-parameter Weibull distribution. Weibull parameters were calculated using the standard deviation method, wind speed was extrapolated to turbine hub heights, and selected wind turbines and a rotodynamic wind-powered pump were simulated." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703009__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Among the three locations considered, Enugu had the highest annual mean wind speed and annual mean power density. Based on capacity factor, POLARIS 15-50, POLARIS 62-1000 and WWD-1-60 models, or turbines with similar characteristics, were identified as best suited for electricity generation in Enugu. The three sites were also reported to have strong potential for wind-powered water pumping." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703009__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703009__objective_001> .
