<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study statistically assessed offshore wind characteristics and wind energy potential using wind observations from three offshore-island meteorological stations in Hong Kong. Wind speeds were adjusted to an 80 m hub height using a power-law model, and Weibull distributions were fitted using the moment method" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "the maximum likelihood method was also used to revisit Weibull-model validity." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Waglan Island had the highest reported whole-period annual mean wind speed and wind power density among the three stations. The Weibull distribution gave an adequate description of the offshore wind-speed data, with no significant discrepancy between the moment-method and maximum-likelihood Weibull prediction curves. The southeastern waters near Waglan Island were identified as the most promising location for offshore wind-farm development among the locations assessed." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__location_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__characterization_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__characterization_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__characterization_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__characterization_005> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Inadequate understanding of offshore wind characteristics had limited the harvesting and utilization of offshore wind energy potential in Hong Kong." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703013__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Because the measurements were collected from meteorological masts on offshore islands, surrounding topographic effects may introduce measurement errors and may influence the representativeness and veracity of the offshore wind characteristics. Measurements from offshore platforms or remote-sensing techniques would be preferable, but such data were not readily available." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703026__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703026__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703026__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study develops probability models for air density, wind velocity, Weibull parameters, surface roughness exponent, MCP long-term wind-speed prediction residuals, and turbine power performance, then combines them in a crude Monte-Carlo based simulation to assess annual energy production uncertainty at Kwangyang Bay." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703026__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For the Kwangyang Bay case study, the Monte-Carlo approach produced a long-term AEP of 4.550 GWh, compared with 4.713 GWh from the conventional approach. The standard deviation of generated AEP normalized by its average value was 11%." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703026__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703026__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703026__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703026__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703026__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703026__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703026__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703026__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703026__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "The IEC method does not allow complicated relationships between different uncertainty sources, and a more sophisticated stochastic method is needed to simulate the behavior of a physical system." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703026__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703026__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "A framework for uncertainty analysis of wind energy potential at a specific site based on probability models for each parameter." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703026__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Further research will include additional improvement of probability models for meteorological variables developed from limited data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703026__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The orographic directional effect and the stability of the boundary layer are not considered in this study. Topographical effects cannot be generalized because they are too local and are beyond the scope of this study." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703026__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703026__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703029__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703029__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703029__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Wind-speed data measured at 10 m at five locations in southern Algeria were analysed using Weibull probability density functions. Weibull parameters were extrapolated to turbine hub heights, turbine output was estimated by cubic-spline interpolation of manufacturer power-curve data, and annual energy output, capacity factor, and unit electricity cost were calculated for four commercial wind turbines." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703029__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The sites in southern Algeria, except Tamanrasset, have important wind-energy potential. Adrar was the best location among the sites considered for energy production and capacity factor, while Ghardaia was second. The maximum annual energy output was 9429.8 MW h for the Fuhrlander FL 2500 at Adrar. The Suzlon S82/1.5MW had the highest capacity factor among the considered models and was identified as the most attractive model in terms of cost per kW h for the same hub height of 70 m." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703029__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703029__objective_001> .
