<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703032__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Hourly wind-speed data measured at 10 m were obtained for six north-central Nigerian locations. The authors used a two-parameter Weibull probability density function to analyse wind data, extrapolated wind characteristics to turbine hub heights, assessed annual energy output and capacity factor for five commercial Polaris America wind turbines, and performed an LCOE-based economic analysis." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Among the locations considered, Minna was the most promising site in terms of energy production and capacity factor, followed by Makurdi and Ilorin" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "based on unit electricity cost, Minna was the most viable site." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The capacity factor ranged from 2.86% for the P17-50 model in Bida to 36.10% for the P50-500 model in Minna." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Average LCOE ranged from 0.0660 $/kWh for the P50-500 model in Minna to 1.2872 $/kWh for the P17-50 model in Bida." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For the P15-50, P19-100, and P50-500 models in Minna, increasing the operating-and-maintenance escalation rate from 0% to 10% increased estimated LCOE by about 7%, while increasing the inflation escalation rate from 0% to 5% decreased LCOE by about 29% and decreased return on investment from 11.54% to 6.23%." .
