<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703043__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703043__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703043__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Measured wind-speed data from 2007 at 10 m, 30 m, and 40 m were statistically analysed for four sites in North and South Khorasan. The study calculated mean wind speed, fitted Weibull wind-speed distributions, evaluated wind direction and wind roses, calculated turbulence intensity and surface roughness, and evaluated wind power density." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703043__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Esfarayen and Fadashk had the highest annual mean wind speeds at the three measured heights among the four studied sites. The authors reported that Weibull distributions gave a good fit to the experimental data and that annual power-density results from measured data and the Weibull distribution had little difference. Bojnourd was evaluated as a class 2 wind-power site, while Esfarayen, Nehbandan, and Fadashk were evaluated as class 3 sites." .
