<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "sustainability" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Daily wind-speed data measured from January 2006 to December 2010 at Katsina, Warri, and Calabar were fitted using Gumbel and Weibull probability distributions. Model fitting performance was evaluated using correlation coefficient and Nash-Sutcliffe coefficient of efficiency. Weibull-model results were used to simulate wind-turbine electric-power output at hub heights from 10 m to 110 m and to evaluate present value cost and cost per kWh." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Katsina was identified by raw-data, Gumbel, and Weibull wind-speed and power-density models as a higher wind-speed-class site, whereas Warri and Calabar were identified as low wind-speed sites. For Katsina, the simulated least electricity-generation cost per kWh occurred at a 50 m turbine hub height. For Warri and Calabar, modeled cost per kWh decreased with increasing hub height up to 110 m. The authors stated that modeled electricity-generation costs could support off-grid rural electrification, although initial procurement and installation costs could still be cost intensive for the rural populace." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__location_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__characterization_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__characterization_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "While many studies have deliberated on wind characteristics and energy potential from different parts of Nigeria, none have undertaken such study for establishing how wind energy could have been applicable as a solution for rural-electrification problems in the country." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "NashSutcliffeEfficiency" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study assessed wind-energy potential at selected Nigerian sites to gain insights into the usage of wind-energy systems for sustainable rural electrification." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703046__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Continuous wind-speed and wind-direction records from five meteorological stations in Hong Kong were statistically analysed. Wind speeds were transformed to an 80 m turbine hub height using a power-law exponent of 0.14. A two-parameter Weibull distribution was used to characterize wind speed, estimate wind-power density, and calculate wind-turbine operating probabilities. Moment, maximum-likelihood, and power-density methods were compared for Weibull-parameter estimation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Across the five stations for the 2005–2010 study period, Tai Mo Shan had the highest whole-period mean wind speed (9.04 m/s) and Hong Kong Observatory had the lowest (2.55 m/s)." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The annual Weibull scale parameter ranged from 2.85 m/s to 10.19 m/s, while the annual shape parameter ranged from 1.65 to 1.99." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Tai Mo Shan had the highest reported average wind-power density, reported as 915.53 W/m2 in the Results section and 915.23 W/m2 in the Conclusion" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "these values conflict." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Hong Kong Observatory had the lowest reported mean wind-power density, 24.20 W/m2." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Hilltops and offshore islands were concluded to be the most promising locations for wind-energy exploitation in Hong Kong, whereas available wind-power potential in urban areas was relatively rare." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The Weibull distribution function was found to give a good representation of the measured wind data, and little difference was observed among the moment, maximum-likelihood, and power-density methods for Weibull-parameter estimation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__location_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__location_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__location_005> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__characterization_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__characterization_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__characterization_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__characterization_005> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Wind energy exploitation in Hong Kong is still rare." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Statistical assessment of wind characteristics and potential wind energy at five typical weather stations with different terrain conditions in Hong Kong." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Extend the analysis to more weather stations across Hong Kong, particularly offshore areas, and integrate statistical analysis of field measurements with Computational Fluid Dynamics simulations for spatial wind-speed distributions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Long-period wind measurements are often unavailable" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "the study introduced relative error to account for possible bias originating from insufficient wind data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703052__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703052__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703052__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study analyzed wind-speed data from Kudat and Labuan for 2006–2008. Wind speeds recorded at 10 m were converted to 100 m using the wind profile power law, and a 2-parameter Weibull distribution was used to assess wind characteristics, wind power density, wind energy density, most probable wind speed, and wind speed carrying maximum energy. WRPLOT software was used to show wind direction." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703052__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The maximum wind power density was 67.40 W/m2 at Kudat in 2008, while the maximum wind energy density was 590.40 kWh/m2/year at Kudat in 2008." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703052__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The highest most probable wind speed was 2.44 m/s at Labuan in 2007, and the highest wind speed carrying maximum energy was 6.02 m/s at Kudat in 2007." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703052__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For wind speeds greater than 2 m/s, the maximum deviation between observed and Weibull frequency distributions was about 5%" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703052__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "at wind speeds below 2 m/s, the maximum percentage error was 25%." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703052__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The most probable wind directions were 190 degrees at Kudat and 269 degrees at Labuan through the study years." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703052__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The authors concluded that the sites are unsuitable for large-scale wind-energy generation, but that small-scale wind energy can be generated at a turbine height of 100 m." .
