<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703052__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "There is very limited research on the assessment of wind energy potentiality in Malaysia." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703052__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study estimated wind energy potential at two Malaysian sites using more recent wind-speed data for 2006–2008." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703052__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The Weibull distribution function is unable to represent the probabilities of observing zero or very low wind speed." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703052__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The analysis used three years of data, and the paper notes that wind data from periods shorter than 30 years may inherit variations from the long-term average." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703055__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703055__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703055__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Wind-speed data from Jhampir-FFC were preprocessed into hourly averages and analyzed at monthly, seasonal, and yearly scales. A two-parameter Weibull distribution was fitted using Maximum Likelihood Method, Modified Maximum Likelihood Method, and Energy Pattern Factor Method. Their performance was evaluated using RMSE, R2, Chi-Square tests, and Monte Carlo simulation. Directional wind-power densities and wind-energy production using a selected wind turbine were also estimated." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703055__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Maximum Likelihood Method was found to perform better than Modified Maximum Likelihood Method and Energy Pattern Factor Method based on the reported performance evaluation and Monte Carlo results. The annual mean measured wind speed at 80 m was 7.77 m/s and the annual mean measured wind power density was 287.48 W/m2. The annual actual wind energy extracted using the selected turbine was 10054.27 kWh. The authors concluded that Jhampir is suitable for setting up wind farms for green and clean energy utilization." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703055__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703055__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703055__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703055__objective_002> .
