<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703064__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703064__energysystem_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703064__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703064__energysystem_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study fitted a two-parameter Weibull distribution to wind-speed data from four Northern Tigray locations and compared the energy pattern factor, least-squares regression, method of moments, and mean standard deviation methods for estimating Weibull parameters. Performance was assessed using relative percentage error, RMSE, mean percentage error, mean absolute percentage error, Chi-square error, and R2." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Least-squares regression method (LSRM) presented better performance than the other selected methods for the four selected locations. EPFM, MOM, and MSDM were reported as less efficient for fitting Weibull distribution curves at these locations. The authors reported poor-class wind power at all selected locations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__location_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__location_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__characterization_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__characterization_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__characterization_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Very few studies had investigated wind-speed characteristics and patterns across Ethiopia, with less attention given to sites principally in Northern Ethiopia." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RelativePercentError" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "MAPE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "ChiSquareStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study evaluated four methods for estimating Weibull parameters for wind-energy applications at Chercher, Maychew, Mekele, and Senkata in Northern Tigray, Ethiopia." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703068__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Using monthly mean wind speed can lose extremely high or low wind speeds within a month and does not allow observation of diurnal wind-speed variations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703072__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703072__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703072__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study analyzed 10-min wind-speed data from 2011 at 10 m, 30 m and 40 m at four Bushehr Province locations. Weibull probability distributions were fitted using the standard deviation method, wind power and energy densities were calculated, wind direction was analyzed using wind rose diagrams, surface roughness and power-law exponents were estimated, and twelve wind turbines were evaluated using annual capacity factor and annual energy output." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703072__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Bordkhun had the highest annual mean wind speed among the four sites, at 5.93 m/s at 40 m, and an annual mean wind power density of about 265 W/m2 at 40 m. The Weibull distribution matched the experimental data considerably well. Bordkhun was considered the best site for wind-energy development in Bushehr Province, whereas Asaluyeh, Delvar and Haft-Chah were not particularly suitable for large-scale turbines" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703072__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "small-scale wind turbines could be a good alternative for those sites. Proven 15 had the highest capacity factor at all sites, while Northern Power 100-24 produced the highest annual energy output." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703072__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703072__objective_001> .
