<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703072__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703072__characterization_020> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703075__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study statistically analysed hourly wind-speed and wind-direction data for six Moroccan coastal sites over 2011–2015. Weibull distributions were fitted using least squares, maximum likelihood, and WAsP methods" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "R2 was used to assess goodness of fit. Wind power density, turbine capacity factor, and annual output energy were evaluated for selected turbines." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The Weibull model provided an accurate description of actual wind-data frequencies independently of the parameter-estimation algorithm used, with R2 values ranging from 0.899 to 0.996 at 50 m." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Dakhla had the highest annual mean wind speed and Weibull scale parameter among the best-fitting results, while Tetouane had the lowest." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Dakhla and Laayoune had the highest annual wind power densities and were concluded to be suitable for grid-connected wind-power systems." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Assila and Essouira were concluded to be suitable only for stand-alone wind-power applications, although their reported annual power densities are below 200 W/m2 and Table 3 classifies 0–200 W/m2 as \"Not Suitable\"." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703075__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703075__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703075__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703075__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703075__location_003> .
