<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703102__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703102__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703102__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Wind data from 25 Eritrean sites in the Wind and Solar Monitoring Network were analysed. Mean wind speed, standard deviation, Weibull parameters, prevailing wind direction, and wind power density recalculated for 100 m above ground were assessed. Measured values were also compared with Global Wind Atlas values." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703102__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The coastal region sites typically have the highest wind power density, followed by the central highlands." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703102__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Assab Airport and Gahro, situated in the far southern part of Eritrea near the mouth of the Red Sea, have the highest mean wind speeds and wind power density among the studied sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703102__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Some central highland sites, including Gizgiza and Dekemhare, also show potential for wind power, while Kerkebet is the only western-lowland site deemed to have potential." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703102__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For good sites, seasonal variations are most prominent in the coastal region, with a peak during November–March, while year-to-year variations are generally small." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703102__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Measured mean wind speeds and wind power densities are typically higher than Global Wind Atlas values" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703102__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "the difference is especially large for complex-terrain central-highland sites where Global Wind Atlas results are more uncertain." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703102__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703102__objective_001> .
