<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703105__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703105__characterization_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703105__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703105__characterization_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703105__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703105__characterization_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703105__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Although wind characteristics and energy potential had been studied for other Nigerian sites, the authors stated that no such study was available in the literature for Akure, Nigeria. The authors also identified that prior Nigerian assessments commonly used monthly data rather than daily or hourly data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703105__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703105__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study used 11 years of daily average wind-speed data to investigate wind characteristics, energy potential, and econometric modelling for Akure metropolis." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703105__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R703105__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R704955__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R704955__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R704955__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study introduced the method of multi-objective moments (MUOM) for estimating Weibull-distribution parameters and compared it with MLM, MMLM, MM, GM, and EPFM using actual hourly averaged wind-speed data from four Turkish stations, including annual, long-term, and selected monthly data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R704955__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For all considered wind sample cases, MUOM gave smaller power-density error than the other considered methods. It also showed comparable good performance for most considered data with regard to criteria other than PDE." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R704955__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R704955__objective_001> .
