<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705188__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705188__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705188__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study fitted a Weibull distribution to hourly 2016 wind-speed data from Agadir Al Massira station using seven numerical parameter-estimation methods: graphical method, maximum likelihood method, empirical method of Justus, empirical method of Lysen, energy pattern factor method, Mabchour's method, and method of moments. The methods were compared using R2, RMSE, chi-square error, and error in annual wind-power-density estimation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705188__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For five months (May to September), the maximum likelihood method was the most effective, while the empirical method of Justus was ranked first for January, October, November and December and ranked second for February. For annual wind-power-density estimation, the maximum likelihood method had an error of -0.51 per cent, compared with -4.56 per cent for the empirical method of Justus" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705188__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "the authors concluded that the maximum likelihood method was the most effective and accurate method at Agadir." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705188__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705188__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705188__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705188__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705188__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705188__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705188__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705188__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705188__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705188__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705188__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "ChiSquareStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705188__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RelativePercentError" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study developed the PWMBP method for estimating two-parameter Weibull distribution parameters and compared it with MLM, MMLM, MOM, GM, PDM and PWMM using monthly, seasonal and yearly hourly wind-speed data from Cide and Keban, Turkey. Suitability and accuracy were evaluated using R2, RMSE, KS, PDE, graphical comparison, and estimated wind-turbine energy output using Weibull distributions and power curves." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "PWMBP apparently outperformed the other methods for power-density estimation for all considered data according to PDE. PWMBP had the highest efficiency for most considered data with respect to R2, RMSE and KS. For energy-production estimation, PWMBP yielded the best performance for 5 time periods of Keban wind-speed data and for 6 of 16 considered time periods for Cide according to EPE." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__characterization_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "The literature contains studies focusing on Weibull parameters for accurate wind-resource prediction, yet there is no consensus on the most accurate estimation method." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "Power density error" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "Energy production error" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Development and evaluation of the PWMBP method to estimate Weibull parameters more accurately for wind-energy applications." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The analyses used wind-speed data from two Turkish regions, Cide in 2006 and Keban in 2007, and considered the selected seven Weibull-parameter estimation methods." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705198__energysystem_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705211__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705211__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705211__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study compared Maximum Likelihood Method (MLM), Modified Maximum Likelihood Method (MMLM), and the newly developed Wind Energy Intensification Method (WEIM) for estimating Weibull shape and scale parameters using hourly wind data measured at 50 m mast height for sixty locations in Pakistan. The methods were evaluated using Wind Energy Error (WEE), RMSE, and R2, and wind energy density estimates were compared with values based on the actual wind-data distribution." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705211__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "WEIM was found to be the most accurate method in the overall ranking, while MLM was the least accurate. WEIM was found better than MLM with respect to WEE, RMSE, and R2" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705211__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "it was found better than MMLM with respect to WEE and R2, while WEIM and MMLM were comparable with respect to RMSE. Wind energy density values estimated by WEIM were closest to actual energy density values among the three methods. Chaghi, DI Khan, Rahim Yar Khan, and Thatta were identified as the amplest sites in Balochistan, KPK, Punjab, and Sindh, respectively." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705211__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705211__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705211__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705211__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705211__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705211__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705211__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705211__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705211__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "R705211__problem_001" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705211__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705211__performance_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705211__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705211__performance_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705211__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705211__performance_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705211__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "R705211__problem_001" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study fitted a Weibull distribution to wind-speed data from Imphal, Guwahati, Shillong, and Kolkata. It compared the method of moments, empirical method, power density method, maximum likelihood method, and the proposed non-iterative energy variance method using R2, RMSE, and power density error." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The proposed energy variance method provided the least error for Guwahati and Kolkata stations, while the maximum likelihood method and power density method showed the least error for Shillong and Imphal stations, respectively." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Across the four stations, Kolkata had the highest reported wind-speed and wind-power potential, whereas Shillong had the lowest reported potential." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The authors identified the energy variance method as the superior estimation method based on the overall ranking analysis and comparison with the existing methods." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__objective_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__location_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__location_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Previous wind-energy assessment studies in various areas of India were limited, and existing works used only one or two methods to estimate Weibull parameters. The authors also identified the time consumption of iterative estimation methods as a limitation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "Power density error (PDE)" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705221__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study introduced and evaluated a non-iterative energy variance method alongside four conventional methods for estimating Weibull parameters in four cities in Northeast and East India." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705236__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705236__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705236__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Meteorological wind-speed data for Jeddah were assessed using a two-parameter Weibull distribution. Monthly, annual and hourly wind-speed characteristics, Weibull shape and scale parameters, wind direction, and wind power and energy densities were evaluated." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705236__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The reported annual Weibull shape parameter ranged from 1.398 to 1.763 and the scale parameter ranged from 3.146 to 4.329 m/sec. The authors reported that average wind speeds were not sufficient for large-size wind turbines and suggested small wind turbines instead. The paper reports that wind power density was maximum in March and minimum in February. Reported annual wind-power-density values are inconsistent across the paper: Table 4 reports a meteorological maximum of 83.78 W/m2 in 2006, whereas the text reports a highest value of 77.99 W/m2 in 2003." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705236__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705236__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705236__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705236__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705236__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705236__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705236__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705236__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705236__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705236__analysis_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705236__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705236__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705236__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Future work is indicated as identifying Weibull parameters after the initial wind assessment stages." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705236__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The current study covers initial stages of wind assessment to find the best location to identify Weibull parameters." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705566__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705566__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705566__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Wind-speed data from nine offshore buoys in the Ionian and Aegean Sea were fitted with a two-parameter Weibull distribution and a two-component Weibull-mixture distribution. Parameters were estimated by maximum likelihood using a Newton–Raphson numerical method implemented in MATLAB, and fits were evaluated using R2 and RMSE against experimental cumulative frequencies." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705566__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For most of the selected sites (six stations with either unimodal or bimodal frequency distributions), the two-component mixed-Weibull distribution provided the highest degree of fit. At Athos, Kalamata and Santorini, p = 0, so the mixed-Weibull distribution was transformed to the simple Weibull distribution. The authors conclude that the two-Weibull mixture is more suitable for such wind conditions and could offer less relative errors in determining annual mean wind power density." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705566__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705566__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705566__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705566__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705566__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705566__location_002> .
