<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705566__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705566__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705566__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Because all samples were offshore, the utility of some findings for onshore data may be limited." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705585__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705585__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705585__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study compared maximum likelihood, modified maximum likelihood, and least-squares estimators for Inverse Weibull distribution parameters through Monte-Carlo simulation, then fitted Inverse Weibull and Weibull distributions using ML and MML estimates to seasonal hourly wind-speed data from Bursa and Sakarya, Turkey." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705585__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "In the simulation study, the ML estimator was overall the most efficient, while the MML estimators had similar bias and MSE performance to ML for large sample sizes and were explicit functions of sample observations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705585__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The LS estimator showed the worst joint performance according to the Def criterion and was not included in the wind-speed-data modeling stage." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705585__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For Bursa, Inverse Weibull fitted winter and autumn wind-speed data better, whereas Weibull performed better for spring and summer." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705585__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For Sakarya, Inverse Weibull fitted the wind-speed data better than Weibull for all seasons according to RMSE and R2." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705585__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "MML-based RMSE values were lower, and MML-based R2 values higher, than the corresponding ML-based values for both data sets." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705585__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705585__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705585__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705585__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705585__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705585__objective_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705585__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705585__location_001> .
