<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705585__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705610__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705610__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705610__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Eight probability distribution functions—Exponential, Weibull, Gamma, Lognormal, Inverse Gaussian, Log-Logistic, Generalized Extreme Value, and Nakagami—were fitted to wind-speed data from five stations in east and southeast Iran. Maximum-likelihood estimation was used to calculate distribution parameters, and fitting performance was assessed using R2, RMSE, AIC, and BIC." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705610__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "No single distribution function was suitable for all examined stations. Nakagami provided the best fits at Chabahar and Khaf" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705610__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Gamma, Generalized Extreme Value, and Inverse Gaussian provided the best fits at Lutak, Rafsanjan, and Zabol, respectively. Nakagami ranked first at two stations and third to fifth at the other three stations. Skewness may be an important parameter affecting Nakagami accuracy, but the influence of the identified parameters requires further investigation for conclusive conclusions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705610__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705610__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705610__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705610__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705610__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705610__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705610__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705610__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705610__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705610__location_003> .
