<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705610__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "There is a lack of detailed study about determining the suitable probability distribution models for estimating wind speed distribution in windy locations of Iran." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705610__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705610__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705610__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "AIC" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705610__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "BIC" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705610__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study appraised the capability of different probability distribution functions to fit wind-speed data at five stations in east and southeast Iran and applied Nakagami distribution for the first time in the selected case studies." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R705610__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "More examinations of Nakagami effectiveness should be conducted using more case studies with different wind-speed characteristics." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R706033__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R706033__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R706033__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Five numerical methods were used to estimate the shape and scale parameters of a two-parameter Weibull distribution fitted to synoptic wind-speed observations from Maroua: maximum likelihood, modified maximum likelihood, energy pattern factor, graphical, and empirical methods. Performance was compared using RMSE and R²." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R706033__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Based on the collected data in the district of Maroua, the maximum likelihood method was the most accurate method overall, followed by the energy pattern factor method and the graphical method. The empirical method followed by the modified maximum likelihood method were the least precise. RMSE and R² values had very close magnitudes for all numerical methods used for the collected data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R706033__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R706033__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R706033__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R706033__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R706033__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R706033__analysis_001> .
