<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R706049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R706049__energysystem_005> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707161__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707161__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707161__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Measured hourly wind-speed data from Garoua for 2007–2012 were fitted with a two-parameter Weibull probability density function using six parameter-estimation methods. The methods were evaluated with chi-square, R2, RMSE, and Kolmogorov-Smirnov goodness-of-fit tests." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707161__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The Energy Pattern Factor method ranked first and the Moment Method second for estimating the Weibull scale and shape parameters. Globally, the Empirical Method, Maximum Likelihood Method, and Modified Maximum Likelihood Method ranked third, fourth, and fifth, respectively, while the Graphical Method was inadequate. Garoua's wind-energy potential was concluded to be not fitted for generating electricity" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707161__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "the authors stated that windmills for community water supply, livestock watering, and farm irrigation could produce a fruitful result." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707161__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707161__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707161__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707161__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707161__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707161__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707161__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707161__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707161__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707161__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707161__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Due to the absence of a reliable and accurate Cameroonian wind atlas, wind-resource evaluation had received limited attention in Cameroon and further wind-energy assessment studies were necessary." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707161__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "ChiSquareStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707161__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707161__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707161__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707161__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study assessed the wind-speed distribution and compared six two-parameter Weibull parameter-estimation methods for wind data collected in Garoua." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study introduced the upper-truncated Weibull distribution (TWD) for wind-speed modeling, estimated TWD and Weibull-distribution parameters using maximum likelihood, compared fitting results using AIC, RMSE, KS and R2, and compared wind-power-density errors using hourly wind-speed data from three Turkish stations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Maximum likelihood among the considered methods seems to be a more efficient estimator for TWD parameters in terms of MSE." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "TWD outperforms WD for most of the wind-speed data measured in the considered regions of Turkey." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "TWD yields less mean power error than WD for most of the considered wind-speed data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "TWD can alternatively be used to evaluate the wind-energy potential of a specified region." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__location_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__characterization_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__characterization_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "The Weibull distribution is unable to model all wind structures encountered in nature, and selecting the most appropriate distribution is necessary to minimize errors in wind-power estimation for a specific area." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "AIC" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "MSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "power density error" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707402__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Different model-selection criteria may provide inconsistent ranking orders of fit performance among candidate distributions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Wind-speed time series from four urban weather stations in Palermo were divided into monthly and seasonal subsets. Preliminary statistics were calculated, and Weibull, Rayleigh, Lognormal, Gamma, Inverse Gaussian, Pearson type V, and Burr probability density functions were fitted using maximum likelihood estimators. Goodness of fit was ranked using the Kolmogorov-Smirnov test." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The authors state that the Burr PDF achieved better agreement with the empirical wind-speed data. However, the total-period Kolmogorov-Smirnov ranking table ranks Burr first for Merlino and Cassandra, while Gamma ranks first for Morgana and Pizia." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__location_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__location_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__location_005> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__characterization_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__characterization_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__characterization_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Urban wind conditions can be strongly influenced by natural or artificial obstacles, making accurate assessment of wind-energy plant performance more difficult and requiring better local anemometric information." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707412__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study tested seven probability density functions, including the Burr PDF, for fitting wind-speed data recorded in an urban environment." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study fitted Weibull, elliptical, non-Gaussian, and Rayleigh–Rice wind-speed distributions to NOAA ISD-Lite observations from 89 French weather stations for 2010–2013. Fits were obtained by minimizing the right-tail Anderson–Darling statistic, and compared using Cramer–von Mises and right-tail Anderson–Darling of second degree scores." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The Weibull distribution was generally accurate near the centre of wind-speed distributions in northern France but tended to underestimate distribution tails and performed less accurately in complex southern terrain. The Rayleigh–Rice distribution generally outperformed the other tested distributions, especially in valleys and at stations affected by persistent channelled flows. Where wind components were close to Gaussian and without much anisotropy, all fits were relatively close, except that only the non-Gaussian distribution did not underestimate strong-wind probability in the tail." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__objective_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "The widespread use of the Weibull distribution to model wind-speed statistics is empirical rather than physically justified, and the distribution may fit poorly when wind components are non-isotropic or non-Gaussian or when multiple wind regimes occur." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "Cramer–von Mises statistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "right-tail Anderson–Darling of second degree statistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The non-Gaussian wind-speed distribution assumes statistically independent wind components with similar parameters b and c" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707435__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "the authors state that this assumption is debatable and not generically true. The Rayleigh–Rice distribution has four parameters and is not easily fitted." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707456__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707456__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707456__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study constructed and compared seven bivariate joint-distribution models for wind speed and wind direction: angular-linear (AL), Farlie-Gumbel-Morgenstern (FGM), and anisotropic lognormal approaches. AL and FGM models used either truncated-below-Normal and Weibull (TNW) or inverse-Gaussian and lognormal (IGL) wind-speed mixtures and mixtures of von Mises distributions for wind direction. Fit was compared using adjusted R2 and RMSE." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707456__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Across the North Dakota sites considered, the anisotropic approach generally provided poorer adjusted R2 and RMSE results than AL and FGM approaches, although it could produce close joint-distribution results for some sites. AL- and FGM-based distributions had similar performance, and the simpler FGM approach could be used instead of AL models for representing wind characteristics. IGL and TNW models had comparable performance for representing wind speed and for joint distributions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707456__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707456__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707456__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707456__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707456__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707456__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707456__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707456__location_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707456__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707456__location_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707456__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707456__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707456__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "Adjusted R2" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707456__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707456__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Future research may develop more efficient anisotropic-model construction procedures, use multiple directional sectors and prevailing directions, investigate independence between longitudinal and lateral wind-speed components, consider statistical dependency using concepts from FGM models, and incorporate meteorological approaches, seasonality, and spatial effects for uncertainty assessment." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707456__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Only Green R had an additional complete record for 2005 for cross-validation. The cross-validation discrepancies were not significant, but they indicated the existence of a potential over-fitting issue when parameters and goodness-of-fit metrics are determined from the same dataset." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study fitted nine parametric wind-speed distributions to hourly wind-speed data from 67 Malaysian stations using maximum likelihood estimation, derived wind-power distributions using a transformation technique, computed theoretical mean wind power using raw moments or Monte Carlo integration, assessed spatial dependence using semivariograms, and produced inverse-distance-weighting maps." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Gamma, Burr, Weibull, Erlang, and Inverse Gamma distributions were selected as the most appropriate distributions across stations. The semivariogram analysis indicated a lack of spatial correlation of wind power in Malaysia. The maps indicated comparatively higher wind-power potential in northeast, northwest, and southeast Peninsular Malaysia and in southern Sabah, while the authors stated that more comprehensive analysis with more stations is needed." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__location_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__analysis_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "The authors observed that wind-energy research in Malaysia was not widespread and stated that more in-depth studies were needed to explore the opportunity." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "Akaike's Information Criterion (AIC)" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "Bayesian Information Criterion (BIC)" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "mean square error (MSE)" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "A nationwide rough spatial assessment of wind-power density based on suitable wind-speed probability distributions and geostatistical mapping." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707478__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "A more comprehensive analysis with more stations is needed to obtain a better map of wind-power potential in Malaysia and to identify specific areas with good wind regimes." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study derived theoretical wind-power-density functions from Weibull, Gamma, and Inverse Gamma wind-speed probability density functions using a transformation method. Maximum likelihood estimation and Kolmogorov-Smirnov goodness-of-fit statistics were used for wind-speed distribution fitting, and Monte Carlo integration was used to determine power-density statistical properties for Gamma and Inverse Gamma cases." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The wind-power-density function derived from the Weibull probability density function follows a modified Weibull probability density function, allowing its mean, standard deviation, skewness, and kurtosis to be obtained from Weibull properties." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For power density derived from Gamma and Inverse Gamma probability density functions, the resulting equations are difficult to match with existing statistical models" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Monte Carlo integration was proposed as an efficient and reliable flexible solution for determining their statistical properties." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Among the stations considered, Weibull was the best wind-speed model at Cameron Highlands, Kudat, and Putrajaya, while Gamma was better at Mersing, Malacca, and Sandakan." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The theoretical wind-power-density functions fitted the histograms of empirical wind-power data well under the reported assumptions of unit airstream area and constant air density." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__location_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__location_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__location_005> .
