<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__analysis_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Difficulty in obtaining statistical properties of wind power density from wind-speed probability density functions, particularly for Gamma and Inverse Gamma distributions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "A transformation method and Monte Carlo integration approach were presented to derive and evaluate wind-power-density statistical properties." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The study does not involve real wind turbines" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "therefore, the airstream area was assumed to be 1 m2." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study fitted eight parametric wind-speed distribution models to hourly data from two Malaysian meteorological stations. Parameters were estimated by maximum likelihood, with the Nelder–Mead optimization technique used for selected distributions. Goodness-of-fit information from the Kolmogorov–Smirnov statistic, Akaike’s information criterion, deviation in skewness/kurtosis, and 1-R2 was standardized through a standard normal CDF transformation and combined through multiplicative aggregation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The multiplicative aggregation of standardized goodness-of-fit scores selected the Gamma distribution as the best statistical distribution model for wind-speed data collected at both Kuantan and Balok Baru." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For Kuantan, graphical representations indicated that Gamma, Weibull, and Burr models fit the data better than the other distributions, although the differences among Gamma, Weibull, and Burr were relatively small" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "the probability difference graph indicated that Gamma was more precise than Weibull and Burr." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The graphical representations agreed with the analytical results obtained through multiplicative aggregation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Different goodness-of-fit criteria can provide inconsistent answers for the selection of a wind-speed distribution model, causing confusion and a lack of consensus on the best selected model." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "Akaike information criterion" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "deviation in skewness/kurtosis (DSK)" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707519__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "An integrated multi-criterion approach using standardized scores and multiplicative aggregation was proposed to obtain a conclusive distribution-model selection." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707531__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707531__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707531__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study fitted a mixture of two truncated normal distributions (MTTND) and six conventional probability density functions to experimental wind-speed distributions from six locations. Parameters were estimated using non-linear least-squares regression with a trust-region algorithm. Goodness of fit was evaluated for PDFs and CDFs using R2 and RMSE, and estimated characteristic wind-speed quantities were compared with experimental values using relative percentage errors." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707531__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Across the six locations considered, the MTTND provided the greatest accuracy for representing the experimental discrete PDF and CDF. For the PDF, its R2 was not less than 0.980 and its RMSE was not greater than 0.011" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707531__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "for the CDF, its R2 was not less than 0.996 and its RMSE was not greater than 0.050. The MTTND also gave lower average and maximum relative errors for the characteristic mean wind speeds than the conventional distributions considered." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707531__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707531__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707531__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707531__objective_002> .
