<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707542__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study developed a mixture kernel density model that combines kernel densities with optimal weight coefficients determined by minimizing asymptotic integrated mean squared error using a Lagrangian multiplier method. The model was evaluated against six conventional models using Chi-square and Kolmogorov–Smirnov goodness-of-fit tests on hourly wind-speed samples from eight North Dakota sites, and was applied to six wind turbine generator types and three wind-energy assessment indices." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The MKD model passed almost all goodness-of-fit tests and had smaller average test statistics than the other tested models. The authors conclude that it provides a better match to the observed wind profile than the compared models and can facilitate identification of a preferable wind turbine generator and a wind site containing richer wind-energy resources among the sites considered." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707542__objective_001> .
