<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707587__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707587__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707587__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study reviewed goodness-of-fit criteria used to compare probability density functions for wind speed data, represented 11 selected probability distributions in conventional moment-ratio and L-moment-ratio diagrams, and applied the diagrams and goodness-of-fit criteria to hourly wind-speed series from seven stations in the United Arab Emirates." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707587__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For the United Arab Emirates stations, Kappa, Log-Pearson type III and Generalized Gamma distributions covered all station samples in the diagram regions. Among distributions with one shape parameter, Weibull distributions had the most central position relative to the sample coordinates. Conclusions from goodness-of-fit criteria agreed better with the L-moment-ratio diagram than with the conventional moment-ratio diagram." .
