<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707587__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Despite its advantages, the moment-ratio-diagram approach had never been used for the assessment of wind-speed distributions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707587__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707587__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "ChiSquareStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707587__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707587__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "AndersonDarlingStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707587__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study developed and applied moment-ratio and L-moment-ratio diagram approaches for wind-speed-data analysis in the United Arab Emirates." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707587__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Future work should focus on non-stationary frequency-analysis techniques for modelling wind-speed series in various regions around the globe. Moment-ratio diagrams could be adapted to analyse temporal evolution of wind-speed characteristics using a moving window through the data series." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707587__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Classical frequency-analysis tools used in wind-speed modelling are based on the temporal-stationarity hypothesis, but this assumption is not always met." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Observed hourly wind-speed data from 83 meteorological stations in Québec were fitted with one-component and two-component mixture probability distributions. L-moment ratio diagrams were used to assess one-component distributions, and mixture-model parameters were estimated using least-squares and maximum-likelihood methods optimized with a genetic algorithm. Goodness of fit was evaluated using chi-square, R2, RMSE, and Kolmogorov-Smirnov statistics." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Among the probability distributions having one shape parameter and represented as curves in the L-moment ratio diagram, Weibull provided the best fit." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Mixture models provided better goodness of fit than the one-component Weibull and Kappa distributions according to the performance criteria used." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The maximum-likelihood method outperformed the least-squares method according to all criteria." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The mixture of two Gumbel distributions estimated using maximum likelihood was the overall best model." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Mixture distributions can efficiently model both bimodal and unimodal wind-speed behaviors." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Wind-energy assessment and mapping studies remain relatively limited in Nordic environments. Very few studies had evaluated wind-energy potential in Québec, and previous Québec assessments had primarily relied on the Weibull distribution." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "ChiSquareStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study evaluated homogeneous and heterogeneous two-component mixture distributions, alongside one-component distributions, for fitting wind-speed data from a large network of stations across Québec." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Extend the moment ratio diagram approach to bimodal and mixture distributions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Analyze non-stationarity in wind-speed data in Québec, including trends, jumps, and cycles." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Extend homogeneous and heterogeneous mixture models to the non-stationary case using covariates such as time, climate indices, and low-frequency climate oscillation indices." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "L-moment ratio diagrams cannot represent mixture distributions presenting bimodal behaviors." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Mixture models have additional complexity compared with one-component Weibull models and require advanced optimization methods such as the genetic algorithm used in this study." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707596__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The genetic-algorithm parameter-estimation method takes more processing time when mixture models are applied to a large number of stations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707661__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Hourly wind-speed and wind-direction observations from six stations in the greater Chania area were used for regional and seasonal wind-characteristic assessment, wind-power-density estimation, and comparison of Weibull, Rayleigh, Lognormal, Gamma, and Inverse Gaussian distributions for overall and monthly wind-speed frequency distributions. Distribution parameters were estimated using maximum likelihood estimation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Mean wind speed varied from 2.1 m/s at Souda to 6.034 m/s at Pedio Volis. The study identified two regions for onshore wind-energy applications: the Chania valley and southern Akrotiri area, suitable only for small-scale applications, and the elevated northern Akrotiri area, proposed as a potential site for larger-scale applications. Gamma was suggested as an alternative to Weibull and, at elevated sites, Gamma outperformed Weibull. Although the chi-square null hypothesis was accepted in very few cases, high coefficient-of-determination values and visual inspection indicated that Gamma and Weibull reasonably modelled the experimental wind-speed distributions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707661__objective_001> .
