<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "ChiSquareStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707672__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707672__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707672__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study proposed non-parametric kernel density estimation for wind-speed probability distributions, developed a wind-speed-sample-based technique to calculate an optimal bandwidth, and compared it with ten conventional parametric distributions using hourly wind-speed data from ten Chinese wind-farm sites over 2004–2006. Goodness-of-fit was assessed using Chi-Square and Kolmogorov–Smirnov tests, posteriori histogram comparisons, mean-square-root errors, and visualized distribution matches." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707672__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For the ten wind-farm sites and the 3-year datasets considered, the statistical and posteriori comparisons indicated that the proposed non-parametric kernel estimation was more accurate and had better adaptability than any of the ten conventional parametric distribution models. The kernel model could fit bimodal probability-density distributions, whereas the conventional parametric distributions considered were unimodal." .
