<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707682__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707682__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707682__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Long-term hourly observed wind-speed and wind-direction data from four Rwandan meteorological observatories were analyzed for periods with monthly hourly mean wind speed greater than or equal to 2 m s−1. Weibull, Rayleigh, lognormal, normal, and Gamma probability density distributions were fitted and compared using graphical comparisons, residual analysis, RMSE, MBE, and a χ2 goodness-of-fit test." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707682__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The paper concludes that Gisenyi has suitable wind-energy potential for electricity generation, whereas Kigali, Butare, and Kamembe have sufficient potential for windmills or water pumping. The reported rankings of best-fitting wind-speed distributions are internally conflicting for Gisenyi, Kigali, and Kamembe between Section 3.2 and the conclusion." .
