<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707709__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Johnson SB distribution is used for the first time in this work and further results need to be sought." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707902__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707902__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707902__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study extrapolated long-term daily near-surface wind-speed series from 58 DWD stations to 100 m AGL using the Hellman power law, fitted 67 theoretical cumulative distribution functions, selected the five-parameter Wakeby distribution, modeled Wakeby targets using least squares boosting and spatial predictors, and calculated modeled annual wind energy yield using a standard wind-turbine power curve." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707902__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The five-parameter Wakeby distribution was the best-fitting distribution on average and was concluded to be a universal wind-speed distribution for the study area. Relative elevation and topographic exposure in the main wind direction were important predictors. Modeled annual wind energy yield varied strongly over short distances in complex terrain" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707902__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "highest and lowest values occurred within distances below 500 m." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707902__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707902__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707902__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707902__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707902__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707902__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707902__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707902__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707902__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707902__analysis_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707902__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R707902__analysis_003> .
