<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708241__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "AIC" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708241__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study proposed and evaluated SGED and STD as flexible alternative families for describing wind-speed distributions and estimating wind-power-density distributions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708252__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708252__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708252__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study modeled 23-year offshore wind-speed records using Weibull, Rayleigh and Lognormal distributions optimized by Cuckoo Search (CS) and Chaotic Particle Swarm Optimization (CPSO). Monthly and quarterly maxima were re-analyzed using a GH model, then Gumbel and GEV distributions were fitted to estimate extreme wind speeds for specified return periods." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708252__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For the four Bohai Rim study sites, Weibull was the most suitable distribution for observed wind-speed frequencies. GEV performed better than Gumbel for monthly and quarterly offshore extreme wind-speed modeling. CS–GEV was selected in seven of eight extreme-wind cases" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708252__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "CPSO–GEV was selected for quarterly extremes at site D. The study area had estimated extreme wind speeds below 45 m/s for the evaluated return periods." .
