<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708252__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Little work had been performed to estimate offshore wind energy together with extreme wind speeds in China, and the availability of long-term extreme wind-speed data was limited." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708252__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708252__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "Proper Error (PE)" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708252__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708252__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study proposed GH statistical calibration optimized by artificial-intelligence algorithms to re-analyze extreme wind speeds under data shortage." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708252__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "More detailed work needs to be carried out for each candidate site to gain precise predictions prior to wind farm construction." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708252__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The main challenge for extreme wind-speed estimation was insufficient extreme-wind data" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708252__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "the extracted monthly and quarterly extreme-wind samples had sizes of 276 and 92, respectively." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708260__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708260__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708260__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study analyzed wind-speed data from four sites in central China, tested long-term wind-speed-distribution stability using Mann–Whitney U and two-sample Kolmogorov–Smirnov tests, compared parametric and non-parametric probability-density models, compared parameter-estimation methods including the cuckoo search algorithm, and assessed wind energy and wind-turbine selection using six output-power curves and consideration of wake-related power loss." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708260__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The mutation tests indicate that the wind speed distributions at all of the sites do not change." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708260__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For sites 1 and 2, the Weibull distribution was superior to the other selected parametric distributions according to the reported comparison criteria" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708260__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "for sites 3 and 4, the normal distribution outperformed the other selected parametric distributions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708260__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The non-parametric kernel estimation provided more accurate and realistic wind-speed-distribution features at all four observation sites than any conventional parametric model according to the reported comparisons." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708260__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "In the overwhelming majority of cases, the cuckoo search algorithm was superior to the other reported parameter-estimation methods for the parametric models." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708260__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The selection of output-power curves significantly affects wind-turbine selection" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708260__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "the JW1500 turbine had the highest reported average capacity factor and modified average capacity factor at all four sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708260__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Considering wake effects and power loss can lead to better wind-energy evaluation and wind-farm design." .
