<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708270__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "There was still no consistent conclusion on which method can obtain the most accurate results to estimate the parameters of the Weibull distribution." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708270__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708270__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708270__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RRMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708270__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "Index of Agreement" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study proposed a diffusion-based kernel density method (DKDM) for estimating wind-speed probability distributions. The method uses a diffusion partial differential equation on a finite domain for bandwidth selection and boundary correction, and uses discrete cosine transformation and inverse discrete cosine transformation to reduce computational complexity. It was tested using simulated parametric distributions and wind-speed data from six observation stations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "DKDM accounts for both bandwidth selection and boundary correction of kernel density estimation and does a satisfactory job in fitting commonly used parametric models." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For the six wind observation stations, DKDM produced non-negative probability-density domains, whereas SJPI estimates extended to negative wind-speed values near zero." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The preprocessing random-number procedure eliminated repeated data values and produced continuous probability densities for stations with relatively low recording frequencies and resolutions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "In Chi-squared and Kolmogorov-Smirnov tests, DKDM and SJPI statistics were smaller than the corresponding critical values, whereas most Weibull-distribution statistics were larger than the critical values." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The authors caution that smaller goodness-of-fit statistics for KDE can indicate smaller bandwidths and closer agreement with the empirical distribution function rather than closer agreement with the true probability distribution function." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__location_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__location_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__location_005> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__location_006> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Most kernel density estimation papers concentrate on mathematical theory, while only a few actually model wind-speed probability distributions. Parametric distribution selection may not work well across different wind farms, and conventional KDE has bandwidth-selection and finite-boundary problems." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "ChiSquareStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "An improved non-parametric diffusion-based kernel density method was developed to address KDE bandwidth selection and boundary correction when estimating wind-speed probability distributions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Extend DKDM to model multivariate wind distributions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Compared with parametric methods, DKDM may be trapped in situations where no wind speed is available." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708294__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "It is inappropriate to compare wind resources between different stations because of different measuring conditions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708307__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708307__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708307__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study developed a Multivariate and Multimodal Wind Distribution (MMWD) model based on multivariate kernel density estimation, applied it to univariate, bivariate, and trivariate wind-condition distributions, compared its univariate wind-speed fit with five standard distributions using R2 from Q-Q plots, and estimated wind power density using Monte Carlo integration." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708307__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The MMWD model had the largest R2 values among the compared distributions at both Baker and Station 44013 for univariate wind-speed fitting. The onshore Baker wind distribution was found to be multimodal, whereas the offshore Station 44013 distribution was treated practically as unimodal. Strong correlation among wind speed, wind direction, and air density was observed. For the examined nine-turbine farm, MMWD produced a higher WPD estimate but a 5% lower farm-power estimate than Weibull because wind speeds above the turbine cut-out speed do not contribute to farm generation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708307__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708307__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708307__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708307__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708307__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708307__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708307__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708307__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708307__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708307__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708307__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Existing wind-distribution approaches make limiting assumptions regarding wind-variable correlation and distribution modality, and a robust multivariate probability distribution of wind speed, wind direction, and air density was reported as absent from the literature to the authors' knowledge." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708307__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708307__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study developed an MMWD model capable of representing multimodal data and joint variations of wind speed, wind direction, and air density." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708307__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Further research is necessary to allow the MMWD model to better represent the periodic nature of wind-direction data. Explicit consideration and characterization of uncertainties in wind conditions and their propagation into overall wind-farm power output is identified as a direction for future research. Implementation of the MMWD model in optimal planning of commercial-scale wind farms is proposed." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708307__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The KDE-based model does not account for the frequency of calms." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708307__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The periodic equivalence of wind directions 0° and 360° is not captured in the KDE-based model." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708307__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "KDE can often lead to overfitting of probability distributions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708307__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Prediction of long-term 20-year wind conditions using 10 years of data might introduce greater uncertainties." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708327__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708327__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708327__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Wind-speed data from five representative North Dakota sites were fitted with eight conventional probability distributions and maximum-entropy-principle-derived PDFs. Six goodness-of-fit statistics and a proposed comprehensive ranking metric were used to compare distribution-fit performance." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708327__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "No particular distribution outperformed the others for all five sites. Multiple distributions provided good fits for Alfred and Ray/Wheelock" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708327__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Green River and Olga had lower goodness-of-fit" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708327__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "no tested distribution provided an acceptable fit for Benedict. MEP-derived PDFs outperformed conventional distributions for Benedict's multimodal wind-speed histogram, whereas one or more conventional distributions outperformed MEP-derived PDFs at the other sites with unimodal histograms. Different goodness-of-fit statistics produced different preference orders among tested distributions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708327__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708327__objective_001> .
