<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708327__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "A comprehensive and fair comparison of wind-speed probability density functions was missing" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708327__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "many common PDFs had not been studied as potential candidates, and existing studies often used only one to three evaluation metrics." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708327__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "ChiSquareStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708327__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708327__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708327__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "Log-LH" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708327__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708327__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "Index_A" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708327__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study fitted eight conventional PDFs and eight MEP-derived PDFs to data from each of five North Dakota sites and evaluated them using six goodness-of-fit statistics and a proposed comprehensive metric." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708327__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "More research is needed regarding approaches that may serve the purpose of fair comparison of statistical distributions better." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708327__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The proposed comprehensive metric is described as a first step for fair comparison of statistical distributions" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708327__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "other approaches might serve the purpose better." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study fitted 24 one-component probability density functions and 21 two-component mixture probability density functions to empirical wind-speed probability density functions derived from global ERA-Interim reanalysis data. Sixty-nine distribution-parameter-estimation-method combinations were evaluated using eight goodness-of-fit metrics related to probability-probability plots, quantile-quantile plots, and mean wind power density." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Mixture probability density functions, including Burr-Generalized Extreme Value, Dagum-Generalized Extreme Value, Dagum-Weibull and Generalized Extreme Value-Weibull, generally provided superior fits to one-component distributions for probability-probability-plot goodness-of-fit metrics. The Wakeby distribution was suitable for estimating the upper tail of the majority of onshore empirical distributions, whereas the Kappa distribution was appropriate for many offshore regimes. The Johnson system of distributions and Wakeby distributions were very appropriate choices for estimating mean wind power density according to x3 error. The widely used two-parameter Weibull distribution provided similarly good fits only in a few cases." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "The diversity of conceptual frameworks, samples and results in previous studies makes it difficult to identify the most suitable probability density function or mixture probability density function, parameter estimation method and reliable goodness-of-fit metric for optimal empirical probability density function fitting of wind speed data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__performance_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__performance_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__performance_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__performance_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__performance_005> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__performance_006> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__performance_007> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__performance_008> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The investigation provided a comprehensive global-scale performance assessment of numerous commonly used probability density functions and compared them with newly introduced mixture probability density functions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "In future studies it might be sufficient to fit the majority of empirical probability density functions with a few of the presented distribution-parameter-estimation-method combinations. It is preferable using few distributions defined by a larger number of parameters than searching for a two-parameter distribution suitable only in the specific case." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study developed a system of wind speed distributions comprising Kappa, Wakeby, and Burr-Generalized Extreme Value distributions. It used 10,016 globally distributed hourly wind speed time series, fitted distributions to empirical wind speed distributions, trained a random forests classifier using L-moment ratios, evaluated goodness-of-fit using eleven metrics combined into a comprehensive metric, and assessed average wind turbine power-output estimation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The system of wind speed distributions had significantly better goodness-of-fit than the individual evaluated distributions and provided high-accuracy average wind turbine power-output estimates for stations with capacity factor at or above 0.20. The random forests classifier correctly predicted the distribution with the highest comprehensive goodness-of-fit metric at 73.6% of stations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__analysis_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__analysis_003> .
