<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__characterization_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__characterization_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__characterization_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__characterization_005> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "None of the previous studies incorporated the best of the well-fitting wind speed probability density functions into a single system of probability density functions for harmonized modeling of existing wind speed regimes." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "MAE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "A single system of wind speed distributions was developed to reproduce the large majority of existing near-surface wind speed regimes." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "In future wind resource studies, the system of wind speed distributions can be applied to assess the wind resource from local to global scale." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708940__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708940__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708940__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study introduced the Extended Generalized Lindley Distribution (EGLD) for wind-speed distribution modelling and compared EGLD, Weibull, Rayleigh, Lognormal and Gamma distributions using hourly averaged wind-speed data from four stations in Turkey. Parameters of all considered distributions were estimated using maximum likelihood estimation, and fitting and wind-power-estimation capability were assessed using RMSE, R2, Chi-square, Kolmogorov-Smirnov, AIC and power density error criteria." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R708940__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "EGLD provided a better fit than the other considered distributions for all stations considered in Table 4. The conclusions state that EGLD outperformed Weibull and other well-known distributions for most wind-speed data measured in different regions of Turkey, and that its power density error results showed superiority in estimating wind power. EGLD showed significant improvement in fit for most considered annual and long-term wind-speed data." .
