<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709006__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The Power Density Method and L-Moments Method, previously used only for Weibull-parameter estimation in wind-energy literature, were developed and applied to the other distributions used in this study where applicable." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709006__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Given the low wind speed values at the four studied sites, where the mean wind speed does not exceed 3.7 m/s, the results of this study may change for sites with high wind potential." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709022__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709022__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709022__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Four parametric wind-speed distribution functions (Gamma, Lognormal, Rayleigh, and Weibull) were fitted to actual and rounded/truncated wind-speed data from five stations in Kerman Province, Iran. Maximum likelihood estimation and method of moments were compared using nine goodness-of-fit indices." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709022__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For actual wind-speed data, the lognormal distribution yielded the best fit across the five studied stations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709022__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For truncated wind-speed data, Weibull distribution fitted using maximum likelihood estimation performed best for Bam, Arzuiyeh, and Shahrbabak, while lognormal distribution remained best for Bardsir and Rafsanjan." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709022__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The Rayleigh distribution gave the least accurate results for both actual and truncated wind-speed data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709022__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The authors recommend Weibull distribution with maximum likelihood estimation when there is uncertainty about wind-speed-data accuracy." .
