<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709039__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "power density error (PDE)" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709039__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study proposes Generalized Lindley and Power Lindley distributions as alternatives to Weibull for wind-speed modeling." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709075__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study compared Weibull, Rayleigh and lognormal distributions for 10-min average wind-speed time series from ten South African sites, using RMSE and R2 for goodness of fit. Weibull parameters were estimated using the maximum likelihood method, wind speeds were extrapolated to turbine hub heights using a power-law relationship, and capacity factors for 20 commercially available turbines were estimated analytically." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The wind distribution at all sites was best modelled by the Weibull distribution, with the Rayleigh distribution a close competitor." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Among the ten sites considered, WM05 had the highest capacity factors and WM02 had the lowest capacity factors." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Turbine K was reported as the most appropriate choice among the turbines considered for the coastal region of South Africa based on capacity-factor estimation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709075__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709075__objective_002> .
