<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709075__location_008> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709075__location_009> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709075__location_010> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709075__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Reliable knowledge of wind distributions and appropriate turbine selection based on local wind regimes is needed for different sites in South Africa." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709075__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study determined the best-fitting wind-speed distribution for ten sites and estimated capacity factors for commercially available turbines using local wind regimes." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709086__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study fitted two-parameter Weibull, Rayleigh, two-parameter Gamma, and Lognormal distributions to daily wind-speed data from four Yangtze River Delta cities. Wind speeds measured at 10 m were extrapolated to a 90 m hub height using empirical extrapolation. Method of moments, maximum likelihood estimation, least-squares method, bat algorithm, cuckoo search, and particle swarm optimization were compared for parameter estimation. Goodness of fit was evaluated using R2, RMSE, and the Kolmogorov-Smirnov test." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "In this case, metaheuristic optimization algorithm-based distribution models performed better than numerical-method-based models. Weibull was the best-fitting distribution, followed by Gamma, while Rayleigh and Lognormal had the worst performance. No one metaheuristic optimization algorithm dominated the others in this case. The selected optimal models were PSO-Weibull for Shanghai and BA-Weibull for Hangzhou, Taizhou, and Chuzhou." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709086__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709086__objective_002> .
