<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709086__characterization_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709086__characterization_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Applications of metaheuristic optimization algorithms to estimate parameters of wind-speed distribution models were relatively few." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study compared bat algorithm, cuckoo search, and particle swarm optimization with conventional numerical methods for estimating parameters of wind-speed probability distributions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Future work should compare more wind-speed distributions and parameter-estimation methods, model wind speeds at different temporal scales, and explore and model seasonal wind-speed data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Only four commonly used wind-speed distributions and three numerical methods and three metaheuristic optimization algorithms were considered. The analysis used daily wind-speed data sampled at 10 m with a temporal resolution of 24 h" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "hourly and 10-minute wind speeds were not considered. Seasonal wind-speed trends were not considered." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study compared single parametric distributions, four mixture distributions, and a proposed hierarchical mixture of multiple distributions (HMMD) for fitting one-year wind-speed records at four Chinese wind farms. Parameters for mixture models were estimated using EM, HMMD parameters were estimated using nested EM, and wind-energy potential and wind-energy conversion-system performance were assessed using the fitted distributions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The proposed HMMD model had the best goodness-of-fit among the considered models for the four observed regions. Mixture models generally outperformed single distributions, but no single mixture model always produced the best fit under different wind regimes. HMMD-based wind power densities classified Jilin and Ningxia as Class 3 and Gansu and Dongshan as Class 6" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "the study described wind-energy potential as moderate in Jilin and Ningxia and excellent in Gansu and Dongshan. The WECS using Nordex N131/3000 Delta at 99 m hub height was selected as optimal for Jilin and Ningxia, while the WECS using eno e.n.o. 126 at 117 m hub height was selected as best for Gansu and Dongshan." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__objective_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__objective_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__location_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__location_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__analysis_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__problem_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__characterization_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__characterization_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__characterization_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Existing mixture models assume that each component is a unimodal single distribution" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "this assumption may be inadequate when a component itself has a bimodal or multimodal distribution." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "ChiSquareStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "MAPE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The paper develops HMMD, in which each outer component is approximated by a mixture model, and introduces a nested EM algorithm for parameter estimation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "The authors state that reliability evaluation of power systems will be analyzed if wind-speed frequency distribution obeys the HMMD model, and that they will try to estimate all HMMD parameters within a Bayesian framework." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709096__energysystem_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709107__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709107__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709107__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study compared Weibull, Rayleigh, and multi-peak Gaussian fits to observed percentage wind-speed frequency distributions from 208 sites across India using R2 as a goodness-of-fit measure. The authors also described annual energy output computation using fitted wind-speed distributions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709107__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For the 208 Indian measurement sites analysed, the authors found multi-peak Gaussian functions to provide a better fit to wind-speed distributions than Weibull and Rayleigh functions, particularly for bi-modal and multi-modal distributions. For uni-modal distributions, the three fits had approximately similar R2 values from 0.95 to 0.99, although Gaussian fit was closer to 1.0." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709107__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709107__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709107__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709107__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709107__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709107__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709107__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709107__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709107__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "The two-parameter Weibull distribution is widely accepted for representing wind-speed distributions, although wind-speed distributions are often bi-modal or multi-modal and can present difficulties for fitting to a single Weibull distribution." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709107__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709107__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The suitability of multi-peak Gaussian functions as an alternative to Weibull and Rayleigh functions for representing wind-speed distributions was assessed using data from a large set of Indian sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709107__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "The authors recommend carrying out the exercise for wind-speed data in other parts of the world and establishing additional formulations for wind-speed analysis, height extrapolation, wind-turbine design considerations, and energy assessments." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "sustainability" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study used measured Edinburgh driving-cycle data for route 1 and a Microsoft Excel VBA calculation program to estimate the energy and fuel-saving potential of an ultracapacitor-based kinetic energy recovery system for a Mitsubishi Galant and six additional automobile models." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For the seven vehicles modelled on Edinburgh route 1, the reported average reduction in energy and fuel consumption was 35%." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For the Mitsubishi Galant, up to 37% of energy could be recovered on the route considered" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "the calculated value decreased to 23% when flat terrain was assumed." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The authors note that the route's descending and braking conditions may lead to more optimistic kinetic-energy-recovery results for the sampled vehicles." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The calculated payback period was reported as not commercially promising, although reduced fuel use and carbon footprint were considered beneficial at a wider scale." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__characterization_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "The authors recommend future research on the impact of driver style on regenerative-braking effectiveness." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The Edinburgh driving-cycle data were collected during part of 1999–2000 and may have changed because of additional automobiles, changes to traffic lights, crosswalks, and other traffic-pattern changes." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Exact altitude values for each time sample were not available" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "the rate of rise between street-area altitude readings was assumed to be gradual." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Driver operation of the brake pedal and accelerator and driver style can affect overall kinetic-energy-recovery performance." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "A significant proportion of the calculated reduction was attributed to the route's descending and braking conditions, which could lead to optimistic results." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R709120__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710275__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710275__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710275__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study maps wind-energy potential in the Far North Region of Cameroon using wind-speed data, Weibull distribution fitting, vertical wind-speed extrapolation, wind-power-density estimation, and an energy-cost analysis." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710275__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710275__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710275__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710275__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710275__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710275__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710275__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710275__analysis_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710275__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "The lack of reliable local wind-energy information for the Far North Region of Cameroon." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710275__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study provides a wind-energy potential mapping and assessment for the Far North Region of Cameroon." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710637__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study fitted Gamma, Weibull, Rayleigh, Normal, and Lognormal probability distribution functions to wind-speed data from Abong Mbang and discriminated them using Chi-square, R2, and RMSE goodness-of-fit tests. Self-written Matlab R2013b codes were used for computational work." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For the Abong Mbang weather station, the Gamma distribution was the best representative of the wind-speed regime and was closely followed by the Weibull distribution. Wind speeds and power densities were very low" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "the authors concluded that the site is not technically feasible for installation of even small wind turbines." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710637__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710637__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710637__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710637__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "The paper states that no such wind-energy study had so far been carried out in some other parts of Cameroon, including Abong Mbang." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "ChiSquareStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study assessed wind-energy potential and probability density functions for the Abong Mbang weather station." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "The authors advise revisiting the site in the future after accumulating a much longer duration of data and measurements at higher heights for a more valid assessment" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "the best representative PDF may be different at the same site for different heights." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The study used low-frequency daily data and a limited period of data of only two years." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study statistically analysed 28 years of 10 m AGL wind-speed data from Maroua using a Weibull probability density function with the energy pattern factor method. It extrapolated wind characteristics to hilltops from 50 to 350 m AGL using an empirical power-law correlation, assessed six wind turbines, and estimated costs of wind-generated electricity in Microsoft Excel." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "At 10 m AGL, Maroua was classified as wind-power class 1 and deemed unsuitable for electricity generation. The paper reports that hilltops at 100 m AGL are suitable using taller wind towers, that hilltops at 150 m AGL are most suitable, and that hilltops above 200 m AGL are excellent for wind-turbine applications. YDF-1500-87 had the lowest reported electricity costs among the selected turbines. The paper reports conflicting claims regarding the turbine with the highest capacity factor: the results text and tables identify P-15-50 as having the highest capacity factors, whereas the conclusion states that YDF-1500-87 followed by E82-2000 provide the highest capacity factors." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__analysis_001> .
