<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__characterization_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__characterization_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__characterization_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__characterization_005> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__characterization_006> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__characterization_007> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "No feasibility studies had been carried out on potential mountainous wind-farm projects in Maroua." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "No measurement stations were installed at the selected hilltops" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "therefore, 10 m AGL wind characteristics were extrapolated to hilltops." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__energysystem_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__energysystem_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__energysystem_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__energysystem_005> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R710647__energysystem_006> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711154__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711154__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711154__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study used monthly mean wind-speed data from 2007 to 2012 at Garoua International Airport, fitted a two-parameter Weibull probability density function using maximum likelihood estimation, extrapolated Weibull parameters and mean wind speed to 15 m and 20 m above ground level, and estimated water-pumping performance for hypothetical windmills." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711154__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The Weibull distribution proved to be a useful tool to predict the wind regime relevant to wind power generating systems." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711154__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The wind energy potential in the north region of Cameroon is not fitted for generating electricity." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711154__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The authors conclude that the results encourage the use of water-pumping windmills in rural areas for household water use, small-scale irrigation, and livestock." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711154__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711154__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711154__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711154__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711154__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711154__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711154__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Studies on wind characteristics in the north region of Cameroon are limited, and there appear to be limited interests and limited previous research on wind energy for mechanical water pumping." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711154__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Further wind characterization studies at different heights above ground level are required." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711154__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711154__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711159__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711159__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711159__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "sustainability" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711159__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Hourly wind-speed data collected at a 10-m meteorological station in Ambam from November 2012 to October 2014 were fitted with a Weibull distribution. Weibull shape and scale parameters were estimated using graphical, empirical, energy pattern factor, and moment methods, whose performance was compared using RMSE, chi-square, and R2. Wind power density and wind-energy density were estimated from the collected time-series data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711159__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The empirical method had the best overall performance because it ranked first, second, and third across the three years of analysis. Ambam was characterized as unfavorable for effective wind-energy generation considering the mean monthly and yearly wind speed and wind power density. Nevertheless, at 10 m height, the reported potential was described as not negligible in the Cameroonian rural-electrification context for localities far from the national electrical network." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711159__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711159__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711159__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711159__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711159__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711159__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711159__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711159__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711159__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711159__characterization_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711159__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711159__characterization_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711159__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711159__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "ChiSquareStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711159__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711159__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Ambam is not favorable for an effective energy generation system at the assessed 10-m height." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study used NASA satellite daily average wind-speed data for Debuncha, partitioned the data into monthly minimum, monthly average, monthly maximum, wet-season, and dry-season datasets, and fitted Weibull, Gumbel, and Frechet distributions using maximum likelihood estimation. The fitted distributions were compared using P values of the Kolmogorov-Smirnov statistic and standard-error analysis." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The authors report that the Frechet distribution best fitted the monthly minimum, monthly average, and monthly maximum wind-speed data relative to the Gumbel and Weibull distributions. They also report that monthly average wind speeds fitted the Weibull distribution better than monthly minimum and monthly maximum wind speeds. Wind speed and wind power density were higher during the wet season than during the dry season. Average wind speeds were relatively low compared with the reported 6–10 m/s cut-in wind speeds of most modern wind turbines." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__objective_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__analysis_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__characterization_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__characterization_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "The study notes that Weibull distribution is commonly considered the best distribution for mathematically modelling wind-energy potential, and investigates whether other distributions in the generalized extreme value family, specifically Gumbel and Frechet distributions, may better describe wind-energy potential at a site." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "P values of the Kolmogorov-Smirnov statistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "standard error" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study compares Weibull, Gumbel, and Frechet distributions for monthly minimum, monthly average, and monthly maximum wind-speed data from Debuncha." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "The authors state that they intend to obtain high-resolution or Cameroon meteorological-department ground-station data for Debuncha and to design more adaptive small wind turbines for low wind speeds by considering aerodynamic structure, reduced load, and high-lift, low-Reynolds-number air-foil design." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711419__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "High-resolution wind-resource data at 10-minute to 1-hour intervals and ground-station data for the site were not available for analysis." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study used ERA-5 daily zonal and meridional wind data at 10 m above ground level from January 2000 to December 2017 on a 0.25° × 0.25° grid of 2745 sites. Weibull, Normal, and Lognormal probability density functions were fitted by the maximum likelihood method, assessed using RMSE, chi-square, and R2, and used to evaluate wind power densities. Wind speeds and power densities were extrapolated from 10 m to 50 m with a power-law exponent of 1/7." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Weibull and Normal probability density functions were found to be more appropriate than the Lognormal distribution for modelling wind speed in the study area" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "the Lognormal PDF slightly overestimated wind power density. Wind resources across most of the study area were classified mostly as class 1 and, at a few locations, class 2, and were not suitable for large-scale electricity generation. The highest seasonal wind variability occurred in the Gulf of Guinea during the rainy season and in the Lake Chad Basin during the dry season. Annual/interannual wind-speed and power-density patterns were either decreasing at windier sites or relatively constant at less windy sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__objective_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__characterization_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Previous Cameroon wind-energy studies targeted specific locations and did not simultaneously address the use of Normal and Lognormal PDFs for a large number of sites across Cameroon." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "ChiSquareStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711460__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study used data covering the whole Cameroonian territory and compared Weibull, Normal, and Lognormal PDFs across 2745 sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Three-hourly wind-speed data measured five times per day from 6am to 6pm at 10 m were analyzed using Weibull and Rayleigh probability-density models, goodness-of-fit tests, power-density calculations, and wind-rose plots." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The Weibull model was a better fit to the Bafoussam wind regime than the Rayleigh model. Mean wind speeds varied between 1.9 and 3.1 m/s in the cases considered, and Bafoussam was assessed as a poor wind-energy-potential site. Winds were predominantly from the NE first quadrant, mainly at 10 degrees, while most calms occurred at 6am and the highest wind speeds were measured at 3pm." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__objective_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "ChiSquareStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Evaluate wind energy at higher heights using power laws accounting for surface roughness" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "collect a longer-duration dataset after a considerable number of years" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "compare Weibull with a broader spectrum of probability density functions" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "and use a higher sampling rate with newly installed airport instruments." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The three-hourly time steps diminish the stochastic nature of wind speeds and directions at shorter sampling times" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "the Beaufort scale is subjective and less accurate" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711507__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "and the energy-potential evaluation assumes zero surface roughness." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711568__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711568__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711568__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study compared thirteen numerical methods for estimating Weibull parameters using 38 years of average daily wind-speed data for representative towns in the 10 regions of Cameroon. Method effectiveness was assessed through R2, RMSE, chi-square test and relative power density error, including quantitative comparison of Weibull cumulative distribution functions with cumulative data frequencies." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711568__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The energy density method was the best method for estimating wind power density at all selected sites, followed by the novel energy pattern factor method. The graphical method was best for the cumulative distribution function at all sites except Ebolowa, where the empirical method of Justus was best. The selected sites were reported as wind power class 1" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711568__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Maroua had the highest reported wind power density, 33.4806 W/m2, and Ebolowa the lowest, 0.1126 W/m2. The authors suggested that low-start-up wind turbines may be suitable for small applications, while Maroua, Garoua and Ngaoundere were more suitable for wind-power generation systems than the other cities considered." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711568__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711568__objective_001> .
