<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711568__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "For Ebolowa, only two wind-speed bins were observed in the data" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R711568__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "the authors associated this limited number of bins with poor performance of several methods." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study compared measured and satellite-derived wind-speed data at Garoua using MBE, RMSE, RRMSE, R2 and IOA" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "used a two-parameter Weibull probability distribution function for wind-speed characterization" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "extrapolated wind characteristics to a 30 m hub height" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "simulated four 20 kW wind turbines using a parabolic power-curve law" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "and estimated costs of energy and water with the present value of costs method." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Satellite-derived data were found sufficiently accurate to provide a reasonable wind-resource assessment during the initial phase of wind-project planning before higher-accuracy in situ measurements are available. The North Region was classified as wind power class 1 at 10 m height above ground level and was deemed unsuitable for large-scale wind-turbine applications. Figuil showed the best combination of capacity factor, cost of energy, cost of water and flow-rate capacity among the sites considered, whereas Poli showed the worst values independently of the wind turbine used. The turbine with the lowest cut-in and rated wind speeds had the highest capacity factors and the lowest costs of energy and water produced." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__objective_002> .
