<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__location_008> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__location_009> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__analysis_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Satellite-based wind-resource data are valuable in Cameroon because very few meteorological stations are available, while studies on wind power remain very limited." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "MBE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RRMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "IOA" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study explored long-term satellite-derived wind data and statistical accuracy indexes to assess wind resource and electric wind pumping potential in the North Region of Cameroon before higher-accuracy local measurements are accessible." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The satellite-derived-data assessment against ground measurements was performed for Garoua, the only site with measured ground-level data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712261__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712275__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712275__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712275__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Twenty-eight years of up to three-times-a-day synoptic wind-speed observations from Kousseri were analyzed. A two-parameter Weibull distribution was fitted using maximum likelihood, modified maximum likelihood, graphical, empirical, and energy pattern factor methods. The methods were compared using RMSE and R²." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712275__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The five methods were effective for the available Kousseri data, with RMSE and R² values very close across methods. The energy pattern factor method had the lowest yearly-average RMSE and highest R², followed by the maximum likelihood and graphical methods. The maximum likelihood method had the smaller average relative error for predicted wind-speed standard deviation than the energy pattern factor and graphical methods." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712275__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712275__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712275__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712275__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712275__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712275__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712275__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712275__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712275__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "A more appropriate Weibull estimation method is needed to provide accurate and efficient evaluation of wind energy potential because the suitability of each method depends on the sample data distribution and is location specific." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712275__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712275__performance_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712275__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712275__performance_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712275__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712275__performance_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712275__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The suitability of five numerical Weibull-parameter estimation methods was compared for Kousseri, Cameroon." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712275__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Extension of this study to other locations in the Northern region of Cameroon and over similar study periods is required for a sound conclusion." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712288__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712288__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712288__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Five numerical parameter-estimation methods for a two-parameter Weibull distribution—maximum likelihood, modified maximum likelihood, energy pattern factor, graphical, and empirical methods—were compared using measured wind-speed data from Maroua, Cameroon, for 1985–2013. RMSE, chi-square, and R² were used for performance assessment, and predicted mean wind speeds and standard deviations were compared with measured data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712288__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The five Weibull methods had RMSE, chi-square, and R² values with magnitudes very close to each other. The paper identifies the energy pattern factor method as the most accurate method based on the statistical tests, but it reports that this method produced the highest standard-deviation errors compared with measured standard deviations. The paper contains conflicting rankings of the graphical and maximum likelihood methods: the abstract ranks the graphical method second and maximum likelihood third, whereas the discussion ranks maximum likelihood second and graphical third. The conclusions recommend the energy pattern factor method for estimating Weibull parameters and state that the maximum likelihood method could be an alternative." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712288__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712288__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712288__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712288__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712288__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712288__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712288__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712288__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712288__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712288__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "ChiSquareStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712288__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712288__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RelativePercentError" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712532__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712532__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712532__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Measured 10-minute wind-speed data from Alasaba meteorological station in 2007 were statistically analyzed using a Weibull distribution model. The study compared measured and Weibull-estimated monthly wind-speed frequency and cumulative distributions, used R2 goodness-of-fit testing, extrapolated wind speed and Weibull parameters to different heights, and estimated wind power and energy density." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712532__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The authors report that Weibull distributions generally fitted the actual monthly wind-speed data well, although November showed a significant difference between actual and estimated monthly cumulative density functions. The reported monthly R2 values include 98.2% for July, 97.7% for September, 96.8% for December, 72% for November, and 85.1% for May. The study concludes that the site wind-speed and energy-intensity values indicate that present technology allows cost-effective wind-power generation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712532__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712532__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712532__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712532__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712532__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712532__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712532__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712549__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712549__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712549__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study assessed wind energy potential at Kırklareli University Kayalı Campus using measured wind data, Weibull and Rayleigh statistical distributions estimated by Moment and Maximum Likelihood methods, goodness-of-fit tests, WRPLOT wind-direction analysis, and WAsP-based turbine energy-production and micrositing analyses." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712549__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For the examined statistical distributions, the Rayleigh MLE method was estimated to be the most suitable model based on goodness-of-fit tests. At 100 m, annual mean results estimated using Rayleigh MLE reported a scale parameter of 7.15 m/s, wind speed of 6.34 m/s, standard deviation of 3.31 m/s, and power density of 322 W=m2. The annual dominant wind direction was Northeast (NE), with 1407 blowing hours. The GE103 model was suggested as the most suitable turbine and was estimated to generate 7.270 GWh annually." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712549__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712549__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712549__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712549__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712549__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712549__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712549__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712549__analysis_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712549__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
