<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712552__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712552__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712552__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Hourly wind-speed data measured between 2000 and 2006 at six Turkish meteorological stations were analyzed. Weibull distributions were fitted using the mean wind speed-standard deviation method, wind speeds were extrapolated using a power-law formula, and annual energy output and capacity factor were calculated for four commercial wind turbines." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712552__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The annual mean wind speeds at Erzurum, Elazıg˘, Bingöl, Kars, Manisa and Nig˘de were reported as 8.7, 8.5, 5.9, 6.9, 7.4 and 8.0 m/s, respectively, at 10 m. Erzurum and Elazıg˘ were concluded to be the best regions among the six studied locations for harnessing wind power. The locations investigated can be evaluated as marginal areas for economical electrical energy generation. The conclusion states that annual highest Weibull k and c values occur at Elazıg˘ and Erzurum, respectively, although the yearly k row in Table 3 reports the largest listed k value, 1.96, for Bingöl." .
