<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712552__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Wind power potential was calculated for Manisa, Nig˘de, Elazıg˘, Bingöl, Erzurum and Kars in Turkey." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Five years (2014–2018) of wind-speed data recorded every 10 min at 10 m at the Djibouti-city weather station were statistically analysed using Weibull shape and scale parameters. Wind characteristics, wind direction, power density, energy density, and the performance of five selected commercial micro wind turbines were evaluated." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The annual mean wind speed was 1.652 m/s at 10 m. The monthly mean wind speed was lowest in June (1.247 m/s) and highest in February (2.329 m/s). Eastern winds were the dominant direction (61.3%), followed by western winds (36.05%). Among the five turbines considered, the Polaris P12-25 yielded the highest reported capacity factor (9.629%) and annual energy output (2.1 × 10^4 MWh), although the conclusion describes this energy output as occurring in August. The authors conclude that Djibouti-city has potential for small-scale wind-turbine applications and that turbines with hub heights greater than 30.5 m should be installed for efficient harvesting." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__objective_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__characterization_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__characterization_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "A wind-energy-potential study in this urban area was not feasible before because of lack of data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study provides one of the first evaluations of wind potential in the Republic of Djibouti using five years of wind-speed data for Djibouti-city." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "An extensive power-feasibility study should be conducted in larger geographical areas of Djibouti-city to choose the best possible options for different scales of wind-power generation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The available wind potential for Djibouti-city could not be estimated for other areas because of lack of data. A few days from the 9th to the 30th of September 2015 were missing because of a technical problem of the cup-anemometer." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712555__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712559__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712559__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712559__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Eight probability density functions were fitted to measured wind-speed data from two urban and two rural stations in Djibouti. Their goodness of fit was assessed using RMSE, R2, and the index of agreement for monthly, seasonal, and yearly periods." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712559__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Based on yearly, monthly, and seasonal analyses, Weibull, Rayleigh, Gamma, and Gumbel were the top four ranked distribution functions for all stations. For the rural stations, Nakagami ranked 1st for Ghoubet and 3rd for Bada Wein in the yearly analysis." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712559__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712559__objective_001> .
