<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712626__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Contribution to the update of the wind map in Algeria through wind-resource analysis in two regions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712630__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712630__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712630__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study processed meteorological and wind-speed data from Laayoune over 369 days, fitted a Weibull distribution using least-squares, standard-deviation, and Mabchour's methods, and compared WES 18-100KW, XANT M-21 100KW, and Northem Power NPS 21-100KW turbines using Excel, ALWIN, and HOMER." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712630__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For the Laayoune site, the authors conclude that the XANT M-21 100KW turbine has generally good annual energy production compared with the other turbines and has a low total cost" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712630__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "they identify it as the most efficient, most profitable, and best suited turbine among those compared." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712630__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712630__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712630__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712630__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712630__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712630__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712630__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712630__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712630__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712630__analysis_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712630__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712630__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712630__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712630__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study combined 10 m surface-station observations, TerraClimate and ERA5 gridded data, and CORDEX-Africa regional climate-model simulations to assess historical and projected wind speed and wind power density across Zambia. ERA5 was selected for subsequent analysis, three better-performing RCMs were combined into an ensemble, outputs were bias-corrected using linear scaling, ERA5 wind speed was extrapolated from 10 m to 100 m using a power law, and wind power density was calculated." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Observed 10 m winds across Zambia averaged 2.8 m/s and were rarely strong. Extrapolating ERA5 wind speed from 10 m to 100 m increased the mean from 2.5 to 3.4 m/s for 1981–2000. Wind speed generally increased across much of the country, although lowland terrain in Eastern Province bordering Malawi showed negative projected anomalies. Projected annual average wind power density was about 46.6 W/m2, which the study concluded is generally too weak for large-scale wind-power generation. Small-scale turbines accommodating a cut-in wind speed of 3.8 m/s were concluded to be more suitable, particularly in rural and suburban areas where obstructions are few." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__analysis_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__analysis_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Assessment of wind-speed variables relevant to wind-energy generation across southern Africa, particularly Zambia, has been ignored, and literature on future spatiotemporal wind-speed variations is especially lacking." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "PearsonCorrelation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RelativeBias" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study provides a comprehensive assessment of wind-speed projections across Zambia using high-resolution CORDEX-Africa models." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Station data covered only 2006–2021" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712633__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "the study used ERA5 in subsequent analyses because of this limited station-data period. Country-level spatial averages could potentially obscure maximum wind power densities across some regions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712637__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Wind data from the Ngaoundere meteorological airport station were processed using a Weibull distribution with parameters estimated by the modified maximum likelihood method. Wind speed was vertically extrapolated with the Hellmann exponential law, and WAsP together with generated topographic data was used for wind-resource extrapolation and mapping. A hypothetical wind farm of four 1.65 MW Vestas V82 turbines was simulated in a selected high-wind-resource area." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The Weibull parameters calculated by the modified maximum likelihood method were very close to those obtained by WAsP, and agreement was observed for the mean wind speed and energy density calculated at 10 m. A hypothetical wind farm of four 1.65 MW turbines in the selected high-resource area had a computed annual energy production of 5,985 MWh and could enable a reduction of 1200 tons of CO2 emissions per year." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712637__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712637__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712637__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712637__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712637__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Wind energy remains unexploited in Cameroon despite its theoretical potential in the North of the country, and research in this area is still in its starting phase in Cameroon." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study carried out wind characterization for Ngaoundere and provided a wind resource map intended to support selection of suitable areas for wind park installation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712637__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712637__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712641__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712641__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712641__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study evaluated Taïba Ndiaye wind-farm production data at annual, monthly, daily, hourly, and intra-day scales and compared production with ERA5 wind conditions at 100 m above ground level." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712641__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Production peaked between December and May and was lowest between July and November. Night-time production was 43.1% higher than daytime production overall. Farm production showed a strong positive correlation with 100 m wind speed" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712641__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "winter and spring production maxima were associated with strong winds, while low summer production was attributable to meteorological conditions characterized by weak winds." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712641__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712641__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712641__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712641__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712641__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712641__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712641__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712641__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712641__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712641__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study used ERA5 reanalysis and in situ data from the Ziguinchor meteorological station to characterize wind spatio-temporal variability and available wind power density at 10 m and 100 m. Weibull distribution analysis, wind-rose analysis, turbulence-index analysis, wind-occurrence analysis, and wind-turbine capacity-factor calculations were performed. The abstract specifies five named Basse Casamance sites, whereas the methods and results specify six sites, additionally including Oussouye." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Wind potential was stronger on the coast and in the north-western part of Senegal. At the seasonal scale, wind was higher in winter and spring than in fall and summer. In Basse Casamance, Diembering, Kabrousse, and Kafountine had higher wind power density at 100 m than inland sites. At Ziguinchor and 10 m for 2016–2018, ERA5 gave slightly higher annual mean wind speed and wind power density than station data. Nordex acciona N-100 and EolSénégal/500 W/24 V were identified as more suitable at Ziguinchor at 100 m and 10 m, respectively." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__analysis_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__analysis_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__characterization_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Previous wind-potential studies had not covered the whole country, especially the Basse Casamance area in southern Senegal." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study assessed wind spatial and temporal distributions and wind power density across Senegal, with a case study focused on Basse Casamance." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712644__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "A technical and economic analysis of a wind system for electricity production for Ziguinchor and other Basse Casamance sites would be interesting. The authors also state that the impact of global warming at 1.5 and 2°C on wind power density in Senegal should be studied." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712648__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712648__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712648__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study used monthly mean wind-speed data measured at 10 m at the NIMET meteorological station in Kano. A two-parameter Weibull distribution was fitted using the standard deviation method, wind speeds were extrapolated to different hub heights using a power-law expression, and wind power density, energy density, and energy efficiency index were calculated." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712648__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For the reported 2000–2014 analysis period, the overall monthly average wind speed was 9.13 m/s" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712648__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "June had the highest monthly wind speed of 10.6 m/s and November had the lowest of 6.7 m/s. The maximum monthly power density and corresponding energy density were estimated as 735.925 W/m2 and 529.866 kWh/m2, respectively, in June. The authors concluded that Kano falls under wind power density Class 7 and could be considered for wind-turbine application." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712648__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712648__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712648__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712648__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712648__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712648__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712648__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712648__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712648__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712648__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712648__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712648__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712648__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Kano State has no wind power project currently due to lack of research that could reveal its potentials and benefits" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712648__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "previous studies did not include energy efficiency index formulation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R712648__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study assessed wind power potential and energy efficiency index for Kano using monthly mean wind-speed data and Weibull analysis." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713394__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713394__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713394__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study used daily wind-speed climatic data for Accra from the Tutiempo Network, averaged the daily data into monthly data and the monthly data into yearly data, and applied a two-parameter Weibull distribution function. Weibull shape and scale parameters were calculated using the empirical method or Standard Deviation Method." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713394__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For Accra during 2002–2016, monthly mean wind speed ranged from 3.5944 ms−1 to 5.4167 ms−1. The highest reported wind power density was 157.5603 Wm−2 in September 2006. Periods with mean power density greater than 100 Wm−2 were reported as suitable for large-scale electric wind application, while small-scale wind turbines could be a good option during the remaining periods. The monthly mean wind-power-density and mean-wind-speed relationship had a coefficient of correlation of 99.3 %." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713394__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713394__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713394__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713394__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713394__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713394__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713394__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713394__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713394__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "The availability of wind resources necessary for exploitation is still a big limitation in Ghana, and wind-data coverage by the Energy Commission is limited to a few regions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713394__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "PearsonCorrelation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713394__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study employed more wind-speed data for Accra than studies found in the literature and distinguished mean power density for large-scale electric wind application for each month and year during the study period." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Wind-speed and wind-direction records collected approximately every 10 minutes during 1998–1999 at five northern Senegalese sites were analysed. The selected-station data were fitted using a two-parameter Weibull probability distribution, with Weibull parameters estimated through linear regression." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The annual average wind speed in the northern coastal region was reported as 3.8 m/s, based on data from five locations, and an annual energy of 158 kWh/m2 could be extracted." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The reported average wind speed is below the 6.0 m/s minimum speed stated for wind-electric generation, whereas wind-powered water pumping appears to be a viable option." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Wind availability was higher during the dry but cold season" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "the maximum monthly mean wind speed of 5.3 m/s occurred in March, while September and October had the lowest monthly mean wind speeds of around 3.0 m/s." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The Weibull distribution was reported to be well suited for the particular study area and useful for calculating parameters relevant to wind-power-generating systems." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__objective_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__location_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__location_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__location_005> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__location_006> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "A reliable and accurate Senegalese Wind Atlas was absent, and further studies assessing wind energy in Senegal were considered necessary." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study evaluated wind-energy potential at five northern coastal Senegalese locations as an attempt to contribute to a prospective Senegalese Wind Atlas." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Conduct additional long-term measurements for the region." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Perform more detailed studies separately at each site before construction and installation of wind energy conversion systems." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The work is described as a preliminary study based on approximately two years of data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713398__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The authors state that more detailed site-specific studies are needed before construction and installation of wind energy conversion systems." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713401__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713401__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713401__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Wind-speed data for Abeche, Mongo, and N'Djamena were assessed using the Weibull distribution. Wind speeds and Weibull parameters were extrapolated from 10 m to turbine hub heights, and five wind turbines were assessed using capacity-factor, energy-output, and present-value-cost calculations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713401__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "N'Djamena had the highest reported wind speeds from 10 m to 105 m, but the Enercon-82 turbine had the highest reported capacity factor among the evaluated turbines at Abeche and Mongo. The authors conclude that Enercon-82 is applicable for Abeche and Mongo, while future work should examine other adaptable turbines for N'Djamena." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713401__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713401__objective_001> .
