<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713405__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713405__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713405__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study applied ten numerical methods to estimate the shape parameter k and scale parameter c of a two-parameter Weibull distribution using daily wind-speed data from Kano, Maiduguri, Jos, Abuja, and Akure, Nigeria, for 2002–2012. The methods were evaluated using RMSE, R2, chi-square error, MAPE, and MABE, and wind characteristics including mean wind speed, most probable wind speed, wind speed at highest energy, and wind power density were calculated." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713405__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The best overall numerical methods for estimating Weibull parameters were MMLM for Kano and Maiduguri, MQM for Jos and Abuja, and EMJ, EML, and AMM jointly for Akure." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713405__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "MOMAB was the least-performing numerical method for all five studied locations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713405__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Among the locations considered, Jos had the highest reported mean wind speed and wind power density, while Akure had the lowest reported mean wind speed and wind power density." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713405__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The authors concluded that Jos was the best location for installing wind turbines, Kano was an excellent location for grid integration, Maiduguri was suitable for a stand-alone application, and Abuja and Akure were unsuitable for wind-energy applications." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713405__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713405__objective_001> .
