<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713405__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "MAPE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713405__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "MABE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713405__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study estimated Weibull parameters for wind-speed data from five Nigerian locations using ten standard and rare numerical methods and compared their performance." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713411__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713411__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713411__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study assessed 30 years of monthly mean wind-speed and wind-direction data at 10 m for 1984–2013 and five years of daily wind-speed data for 2009–2013. It used a two-parameter Weibull probability density function, estimated wind power density, extrapolated wind speed to 80 m, and evaluated six practical wind turbines." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713411__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Monthly mean wind speed peaked at 4.62 m/s in August and was lowest at 3.60 m/s in November. Mean wind speed was 4.05 m/s during dry DJF months and 4.32 m/s during wet JJAS months. Maximum estimated wind power density was 145.48 W/m2 in August. AV 928 had the highest reported monthly average power output among the turbines considered, but capacity factors were relatively low, approximately 10% or less, raising concern about the economic viability of a large-scale wind-power project at the study site." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713411__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713411__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713411__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713411__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713411__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713411__objective_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713411__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713411__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713411__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713411__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713411__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713411__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713411__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713411__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713411__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713411__characterization_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713411__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "There exists limited evidence of wind-energy assessment studies in Nigeria, where electricity supply is still below demand." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713411__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713411__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713416__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713416__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713416__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Hourly wind-speed time-series data for 2002–2011 from three Nigerian offshore locations were averaged to daily and monthly values. Weibull, Rayleigh and Exponential probability distributions were fitted and compared using RMSE, R2 and chi-square. Wind power density, characteristic wind speeds, turbine power output and capacity factor were estimated." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713416__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Weibull distribution provided a better fit to the collected wind data than Rayleigh and Exponential distributions based on the reported goodness-of-fit results. The paper concludes that the three considered locations have potential for wind power generation and recommends DeWind D6 and Polaris P62-1000 turbines, or turbines with similar design characteristics, for the three locations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713416__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713416__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713416__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713416__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713416__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713416__objective_003> .
