<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713420__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study explored wind resources and energy potential for sixteen regions covering almost all the territory of Algeria." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713420__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Other power systems may be integrated in the future." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713424__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713424__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713424__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Hourly wind-speed data from six coastal Ghanaian locations were analysed using two-parameter Weibull distributions. Weibull parameters were estimated using the standard deviation method, wind characteristics were extrapolated to turbine hub heights using Weibull-based height expressions, and performance and LCOE were calculated for four commercial wind turbines." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713424__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The coastal Ghana wind resource was classified as Class 2 or less and was considered marginally suitable for large-scale wind-energy development, suitable for small-scale applications, and potentially useful as part of a hybrid energy system. The CF-100 turbine was considered the most economically viable option across all selected sites. Turbines with cut-in wind speed below 3 m/s and rated wind speed between 9 and 11 m/s were considered suitable for the coastal region." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713424__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713424__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713424__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713424__objective_002> .
