<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713430__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713430__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713430__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study assessed offshore wind-energy technical potential in the Lagos coastal region using bathymetry data from GEBCO, wind-speed data analysed from existing literature, wind-speed scaling to a 135 m hub height using the log law, turbine-layout calculations, and output and annual-energy-generation calculations for the Aerodyn SCD 8.0/168 turbine." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713430__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The paper reports that Lagos annual electricity demand of about 96.36 TWh can be met by annual generation of about 191.2 TWh for a wind farm at the shore and 200 TWh for waters with depth less than 50 m. It concludes that the most efficient depth for the current target energy demand would be between the shore and 50 m deep offshore." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713430__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713430__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713430__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713430__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713430__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713430__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713430__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713430__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713430__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713430__analysis_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713430__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713430__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713430__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Onshore wind-energy resources have been fairly explored, whereas offshore wind energy in the Lagos region had not been explored." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713430__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study provides a technical assessment of offshore wind resources around Lagos, Nigeria, including a technical turbine layout and potential output." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713430__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Further work can be done on losses during transmission of power to the system operation unit and the cost of carrying out the proposed work." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713430__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Economic and market factors were outside the scope of the study. Exclusive economic zones, Marine Protection Zones, commercial fishing, and other restrictions were not implemented because no such data was obtained." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713430__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713430__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study analysed 5-min average wind-speed time series collected during 2005–2009 at 10 m in Johannesburg" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "compared Weibull, Rayleigh, lognormal, and logistic distributions using R2 and RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "estimated Weibull parameters and wind power density using the standard deviation method" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "and evaluated annual energy output, capacity factor, and levelised electricity cost for small commercially available wind turbines." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Weibull distribution provided the best fit among the distributions considered. Johannesburg had a whole-period mean wind speed of 4.15 m/s and a wind power density of 62.72 W/m2, and was classified as class 1, which is poor for grid application. However, because monthly minimum wind speeds were greater than 3 m/s, the site can be used for small wind-power applications. Turbine F was reported as the most preferable turbine, with an LEC of 0.25–0.33 $/kWh, although Table 9 reports a lower 2005 LEC for turbine H than for turbine F." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__objective_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__objective_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Very little had been reported on South Africa regarding assessment of wind distribution and wind power potential." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The paper determined the statistical distribution describing Johannesburg wind speeds, evaluated wind power potential, and performed cost analysis of selected small commercially available wind turbines based on the local wind regime." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The authors note that weather-service data observed at lower mast heights are not reliable for large-scale wind-turbine assessment, because instrument positioning information is usually unavailable and existing standards may be applied less strictly. They state that these data can be adequate for small-scale wind turbines operating at lower height." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713445__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713445__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713445__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Daily average wind speeds from 15 Nigerian sites were fitted with a two-parameter Weibull distribution using an empirical method. Wind power density was estimated and classified using the NREL standard, commercially available wind turbines were evaluated using capacity factor, and unit electricity costs were calculated using the present value cost method." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713445__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Sites S2 (Jos) and S3 (Kano) had class-7 wind resources and were reported to be economically viable for wind-power grid integration. S8 (Iseyin), a class-5 site, may also be considered for grid application but may require a turbine with lower cut-in and rated wind speeds. S7, S9, and S15 were not considered viable for grid application but were reported as suitable for standalone applications." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713445__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R713445__objective_001> .
