<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R716871__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R716871__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R716871__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Monthly average wind-speed data for one year at 20 m and 60 m were assessed for Msallata, Espiaa, Alqatrun, and Adirsiyah in Libya. Weibull parameters were estimated using the Empirical Method of Justus, Graphical Method, and Maximum Likelihood Method, and fitted distributions were compared with actual data using R2, RMSE, MBE, and MAE." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R716871__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "At 20 m, GM gave the best distribution performance for Adirsiyah and Espiaa, MLM for Alqatrun, and EMJ for Msallata. At 60 m, EMJ gave the best modeling performance for Adirsiyah and Msallata, while MLM gave the best performance for Alqatrun and Espiaa. Msallata had the maximum wind-power potential and Adirsiyah the minimum among the four sites considered." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R716871__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R716871__objective_001> .
