<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717690__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717690__performance_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717690__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717690__performance_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study applied and compared five wind-energy-potential estimation methods—ANFIS, MLP, SVR, EMJ, and MLM—to wind data from Lomé and Cotonou. It fitted wind-speed probability density functions, calculated available energy, recoverable energy, and wind-turbine energy output, and evaluated method performance using RMSE and R2." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "ANFIS and MLP outperformed EMJ, MLM, and SVR for wind-speed characterization and wind-energy-potential estimation at the Lomé and Cotonou sites. ANFIS was reported as the most accurate approach and MLP as the second most accurate. SVR ranked third but was unstable across estimation types and sites and was less recommendable for Cotonou. Weibull distribution-based EMJ and MLM were reported as the least accurate, especially for recoverable energy and wind-turbine energy output." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__characterization_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study compared five promising wind-energy-potential estimation methods in the regional context of Togo and Benin and recommended methods for future wind-resource assessment projects in the region." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__energysystem_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717710__energysystem_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717717__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717717__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717717__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Wind-speed data collected at 10, 20 and 30 m during 2008 and 2009 at Borj-Cedria were used to estimate seasonal mean wind speed, wind-speed distribution and wind-power density. The seasonal net energy production of seven commercialized 1.5 MW wind turbines assumed to be installed at 80 m above ground level was evaluated using manufacturer power curves, air-density correction and a power-loss factor." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717717__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The authors report that Borj-Cedria presents a promising wind potential and that the simulation of seven commercialized wind turbines shows about 3.57% difference in annual net energy production. They conclude that the Vensys70 wind turbine is the best type adapted to the site conditions among the turbines studied." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717717__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717717__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717717__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717717__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717717__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717717__location_001> .
