<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717721__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717721__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717721__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Monthly mean wind-speed data for 2013-2017 from NiMet were evaluated at 10 m using a two-parameter Weibull probability distribution function to determine monthly and annual wind-resource potentials for power generation at Yenagoa, Calabar and Port Harcourt." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717721__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Computed annual mean wind speeds were 1.74 m/s for Yenagoa, 2.85 m/s for Calabar and 1.38 m/s for Port Harcourt. Computed annual mean power densities were 4.64 W/m2, 7.06 W/m2 and 3.08 W/m2, respectively. The paper concludes that the investigated coastal south-south Nigerian locations have a low wind-energy resource classified as Class 1 and that higher wind speed, power density and wind-energy resource may be achieved if data were collected above the 10 m height used in the study." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717721__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R717721__objective_001> .
