<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R718237__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "The authors state that their work is among the first studies conducted for these Moroccan coastal regions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R718237__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R718237__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R718237__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "ChiSquareStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R718237__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study determined wind-speed distributions at different heights using historical wind-speed data, calculated wind power and energy density, and selected wind-turbine models for the sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R718237__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R718237__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719349__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719349__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719349__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study analysed 24 years of wind-speed data from ten South West Nigerian stations using a two-parameter Weibull distribution, assessed Weibull goodness of fit, extrapolated wind characteristics from 10 m to turbine hub heights, simulated outputs of five wind-turbine models, and conducted a cost-benefit analysis." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719349__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Average wind speeds between 1.9 and 5.3 m/s were reported across the stations. Lagos Island, Ikeja and Ibadan were ranked as the top three stations based on Weibull results. GE 1.5xle produced the highest simulated output among the five turbine models. The authors concluded that, apart from Lagos, Oyo and mountainous locations, lower-wind-speed-rated turbines would be more appropriate and that turbines with cut-in speeds of 2.0–3.0 m/s and rated speeds of 10–12.0 m/s would be excellent for the sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719349__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719349__objective_001> .
