<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719349__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "NashSutcliffeEfficiency" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719358__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719358__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719358__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study used average daily meteorological wind data from National Agency of Meteorology stations at 10 m, fitted a Weibull distribution using the standard deviation method, calculated available and recoverable wind power, extrapolated Medea wind speed to 20, 40, and 60 m, and evaluated four wind turbines for wind pumping." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719358__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "At 10 m, the selected locations were reported to have relatively low wind characteristics. Tiaret, Batna, and Meliana were identified as having more significant wind power potential among the selected North Algerian sites. The authors concluded that wind power can nevertheless be considered in northern Algeria for pumping at modest drills, despite rather low wind speed." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719358__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719358__objective_001> .
