<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "solar" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hybrid" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study analyzed a decade-long on-site wind dataset from Naama using Weibull and Rayleigh distribution fitting, Pearson correlation analysis, principal component analysis, wind-turbine simulation in ASHES, and solar simulation using PVGIS-SARAH. Linear regression models were used to predict wind power generation from global irradiance, with an enhanced version additionally incorporating temperature and humidity." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Wind speed and solar irradiation showed statistically significant negative monthly correlations from January to May and from September to December, whereas the correlations during June to August were not statistically significant in the reported monthly correlation analysis. The Weibull distribution provided a slightly better fit to the Naama wind-speed dataset than the Rayleigh distribution. Simulated wind output was generally higher during early morning and late-afternoon-to-evening periods, when solar output was lower or absent." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__objective_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__analysis_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Solar photovoltaic generation is intermittent and unavailable at night, creating a need for complementary renewable resources capable of reducing supply shortfalls." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "ChiSquareStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "PearsonCorrelation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study evaluates whether Naama wind resources can supplement declining solar photovoltaic output, particularly during evening and low-solar-irradiance periods." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Future research should explore longer-term climatic data, technological advancements, broader geographical coverage, complex summer atmospheric dynamics, and advanced predictive models incorporating additional relevant parameters." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Seasonal discrepancies, particularly weaker correlations during summer, suggest the need for more comprehensive environmental analyses. The decade-long data may not fully capture long-term climatic trends, findings based on current technology could evolve as technology advances, and the focus on Naama may limit generalizability to other regions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719366__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719520__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719520__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719520__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study used monthly wind-speed data for 2008-2016 measured at 10 m, fitted a two-parameter Weibull distribution using the energy pattern factor method, extrapolated wind speed and Weibull parameters to hub heights using a power-law model, estimated turbine energy output and capacity factor, and evaluated electricity-generated cost using the present value of costs method." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719520__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The reported mean monthly wind speeds were within 4.31-6.04 m/s at 10 m height." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R719520__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The study reported monthly wind power density values from 61.864 W/m2 in November to 184.792 W/m2 in December." .
