<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720066__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720066__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "ChiSquareStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720066__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720066__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study proposed Pdf analysis using Weibull and Rayleigh distributions, evaluated the models with R2, Chi-square, and RMSE, and calculated wind-energy potential." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720167__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720167__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720167__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Eight probability density functions—Weibull, Gamma, Rayleigh, Gumbel, Lognormal, Inverse Gaussian, Nakagami and Exponential—were fitted to measured wind-speed data from two urban and two rural stations in Djibouti. Their fitting accuracies were evaluated using RMSE, R2 and the index of agreement over monthly, seasonal and yearly periods." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720167__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Based on yearly, monthly and seasonal analyses, Weibull, Rayleigh, Gamma and Gumbel were the top four ranked distribution functions and provided the best fits for all stations. For the rural stations, Nakagami ranked first for Ghoubet and third for Bada Wein" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720167__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "it was also ranked first at Bada Wein during the cold season." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720167__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720167__objective_001> .
