<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720167__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "The Nakagami distribution should be conducted and evaluated for more rural sites that have high wind speed." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720167__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "For Ghoubet, approximately 21 days of data between October and November 2015 are missing" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720167__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "the paper states that data losses during these months are often due to violent wind at the Ghoubet site." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720348__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720348__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720348__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Monthly wind-speed data for 2008-2016 measured at 10 m were statistically analysed. A two-parameter Weibull distribution fitted using the Energy Pattern Factor method was used to characterize wind speed and wind potential. A power-law model was used to extrapolate wind speed and Weibull parameters to other hub heights. Candidate wind turbines were evaluated for energy production, capacity factor, and electricity-generated cost using the present value of costs method." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720348__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The mean monthly wind speeds were reported to range from 4.31 to 6.04 m/s at 10 m height." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720348__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Monthly wind power density was reported to range from 61.864 W/m2 in November to 184.792 W/m2 in December." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720348__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The paper concluded that the wind potential at the selected area could be considered marginal (class 2) according to wind-power classification." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720348__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "YDF-1500-87 was reported to have the lowest electricity-generated cost per kWh and maximum energy power compared with the other evaluated models." .
