<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720760__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720760__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720760__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Wind-speed measurements from Bangui M’Poko Airport were analysed using a Weibull distribution fitted by the modified maximum likelihood method. WAsP was used with topography, roughness, and obstacle information to generate a wind atlas, wind-resource maps, and annual-energy-production estimates for a hypothetical wind farm." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720760__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The Weibull parameters, mean wind speed, and mean energy density calculated using the modified maximum likelihood method were very close to the WAsP results. The authors reported that the deviation in wind speed extrapolated to 70 m and in annual energy production was relatively small and may be due to determination of surface-roughness height. The estimated annual energy production of the hypothetical ten-turbine wind farm was 42.626 GWh." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720760__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720760__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720760__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720760__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720760__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720760__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720760__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720760__location_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720760__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "PearsonCorrelation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720760__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Future work is intended to account for interactions between wind turbines, also called wake effects, in numerical simulations and to evaluate turbine-output energy with an economic analysis of the produced kWh." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720760__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720760__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720773__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720773__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720773__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study used 25 years of daily average wind-speed data at 10 m meteorological height for Enugu, Onitsha, and Owerri. Weibull distributions were fitted using double-logarithmic plots and one-dimensional regression to obtain shape and scale parameters, and predicted probability densities were compared with observed distributions using Pearson correlation and root-mean-square error." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720773__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Annual mean wind speeds were 5.5 ± 0.6 m/s for Enugu, 3.6 ± 0.4 m/s for Onitsha, and 3.3 ± 0.3 m/s for Owerri." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720773__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The fitted Weibull shape factors were 2.0, 1.5, and 1.9 and the corresponding scale factors were 6.4, 5.6, and 5.1 m/s for Enugu, Onitsha, and Owerri, respectively." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720773__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "All reported correlations between measured and predicted probability densities were statistically significant at the 5% level" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720773__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "within the region of overlap, the Weibull distribution can be used with acceptable accuracy to predict wind potentials for the studied locations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720773__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Within the region of overlap, the theoretical model appears to underestimate the probability density of every speed bin for each location, and the authors associate the large root-mean-square errors with coarse approximations arising from daily averages." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720773__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720773__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720773__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720773__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720773__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720773__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720773__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R720773__location_002> .
