<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R723171__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R723171__energysystem_005> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R723300__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R723300__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R723300__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Measured wind-speed data at 10 m above ground level for 2011–2016 were analyzed for thirteen Nigerian sites. A two-parameter Weibull distribution was used for wind-power assessment" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R723300__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "average wind-power density and corresponding wind-energy density were estimated. Wind speeds were extrapolated from 10 m to the 25 m turbine hub height using a power-law relationship, and annual electric energy output was calculated for a selected 20 kW wind turbine." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R723300__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Wind-power densities at the investigated sites were generally poor and class 1, except Jos, which was class 2. Jos had an average wind speed of 5.34 m/s and wind-power density of 133 W/m2. Kano had a wind-power density of 79.96 W/m2. Small stand-alone wind-energy systems in Jos, Sokoto, Kano, and Maiduguri were assessed as quite promising" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R723300__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Jos had the largest reported annual electricity generation, followed by Kano, Sokoto, and Maiduguri." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R723300__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R723300__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R723300__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R723300__objective_002> .
