<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R723373__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R723373__characterization_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R723373__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "In contrast to earlier studies focused on identifying suitable locations, selecting turbines and determining unit energy cost, this study also determined the effect of varying hub height on unit energy cost." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R723373__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R723373__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724371__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724371__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724371__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Four groups of 10-minute wind-speed data measured during 2014 at two coastal Zhejiang wind farms and at four heights were fitted with Weibull, Rayleigh, Gamma, logarithmic normal, and Inverse Gaussian distributions. The study compared goodness-of-fit indicators and wind-power-density relative errors, then compared six Weibull parameter-estimation methods." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724371__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The four wind-speed datasets were right-skewed and unimodal, with positive skewness and peakedness values." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724371__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Weibull and Rayleigh distributions had better fitting performance than logarithmic normal, Gamma, and Inverse Gaussian distributions at the four sites" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724371__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "after wind-power-density analysis, Weibull was concluded to be the best model for the studied Zhejiang coastal regions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724371__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "AMLM and GM had the worst Weibull fitting performance, EMJ performance was unstable, and MLE, PD, and MM achieved highly similar goodness-of-fit results and better accorded with the actual wind-speed distribution than the other methods." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724371__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724371__objective_001> .
