<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724404__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "A unified model for assessing wind speed at all regions of Inner Mongolia had not been proposed." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724404__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724404__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724404__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724404__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "AIC" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724404__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "BIC" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724404__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "PDE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724404__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The paper constructed a new probability distribution to fit wind-speed data in Inner Mongolia, China." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724501__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724501__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724501__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study applied maximum likelihood estimation of two-parameter Weibull distributions to hourly mean wind-speed data. It proposed an iterative sampling-interval procedure using a Box-Cox transformation, Anderson-Darling normality testing, autocorrelation coefficients, and the Ljung-Box test to select an independent wind-speed sample for estimating parameter standard errors." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724501__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For hourly mean wind speeds recorded at Amagro station, the selected data-acquisition interval for accepting independence at a significance level of 0.05 was 174 h, slightly more than one week." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724501__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Autocorrelated successive hourly mean wind speeds invalidated the usual statistical tests but had no significant effect on the shape of the estimated Weibull probability density distribution in this case study." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724501__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The calculated uncertainties for commonly used wind-energy statistic functions obtained from dependent wind-speed data were over-optimistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724501__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "the paper recommends using an independent wind-speed sample to estimate these uncertainties." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724501__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The root mean square error was 0.029 for both Weibull distributions compared in the study." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724501__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724501__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724501__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724501__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724501__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724501__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724501__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724501__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724501__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724501__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study fitted Lognormal, Gumbel, and Generalized Extreme Value probability distributions to monthly wind-speed data for Brasília, Campo Grande, Cuiabá, and Goiânia. Distribution parameters were estimated using maximum likelihood, and goodness of fit was assessed using KS, R2, RMSE, AIC, BIC, and AICc indicators." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For the four cities considered, the GEV distribution was reported as the best overall representation of wind-speed data when compared with LN and GUM distributions. For Campo Grande, GEV demonstrated a better fit for most months, except January, when LN performed better" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "GEV and LN were tied in July according to the combined ranking." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__location_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__location_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__location_005> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "The authors state that no detailed statistical analysis of wind-speed characteristics in the Brazilian Midwest area had been carried out to date." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "ChiSquareStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "AIC" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "BIC" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "AICc" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study evaluated the goodness of fit of probability distributions for wind speed at four central-western Brazilian cities." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R724505__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "The estimated distribution parameters and methodology can be implemented in studies concerning renewable-energy-source location, module reliability, power quality, protection systems, harmonics, and noise treatment." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725713__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725713__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725713__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study analyzed 1 Hz wind-speed measurements from FINO-1 at 100 m over three years. It compared Weibull, Gaussian, Nakagami, Rician, Gamma, inverse-Gamma, and log-normal distribution models across time windows from 10 min to 1 month using next-point probability, Kullback–Leibler divergence, and square-velocity relative deviation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725713__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For large time windows, including 1 month, Weibull fitted wind-speed distributions better than Gaussian. For shorter windows, Gaussian, Nakagami, and sometimes Rice models performed better than Weibull depending on the metric. Gaussian produced the least errors in energy predictions independently of window size among the compared models." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725713__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725713__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725713__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725713__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725713__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725713__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725713__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725713__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725713__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "How the Weibull model holds for shorter time periods remained an open question." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725713__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725713__performance_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725713__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725713__performance_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725713__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725713__performance_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725713__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The paper systematically investigated two-parameter wind-speed distribution models over time windows spanning from 10 min to 1 month." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725713__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Future research could study the process across scales, including how standard deviation scales with time-window scale and analyses of correlations and Hurst exponents, to clarify limitations of assigning a particular statistical distribution to wind speed." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725713__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "One percent of data points that were NaNs were discarded" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725713__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "windows with more than 40% NaNs were discarded. Empirical distributions with two local maxima, representing less than 2% of windows, were discarded for histogram fitting and energy-prediction analyses. For inverse-Gamma fitting, windows producing infinite values below computational resolution, about 0.1% of windows, were discarded." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725792__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725792__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725792__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Three-hourly measured wind-speed data from January 2006 to December 2016 at ten Burkina Faso sites were fitted with Weibull, Hybrid Weibull, Rayleigh, Gamma, and inverse Gaussian distributions using the maximum likelihood method. Model fit was assessed using R2 and RMSE, and annual wind-power-density estimation was compared using relative percentage error." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725792__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Based on R2 and RMSE, Weibull was the most suitable distribution at Bobo, Dédougou, Ouaga, and Ouahigouya" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725792__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Hybrid Weibull was most suitable at Bogandé, Fada, and Po" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725792__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "and inverse Gaussian was most suitable at Boromo, Dori, and Gaoua. For annual wind-power-density estimation, Hybrid Weibull had the minimum error at seven sites, whereas Rayleigh had the minimum error at Ouaga and Ouahigouya and Weibull had the minimum error at Dédougou." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725792__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725792__objective_001> .
