<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725792__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "There is a lack of extensive research on determination of appropriate frequency-distribution models for estimating wind-speed distribution across different regions of Burkina Faso." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725792__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725792__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725792__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RelativePercentError" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725792__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study evaluated the capacity of five distribution functions to fit wind-speed data at ten sites throughout Burkina Faso." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725875__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725875__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725875__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Historical wind-speed data for Medan City from 2017 to 2019 were used to estimate and compare Weibull, gamma, and exponential distribution functions. Scale and shape parameters were calculated, and the models' PDF and CDF results were compared with observed cumulative probability." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725875__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For the Medan City wind site and the 2017–2019 wind data, the exponential distribution was found to be the best model for determining CDF, followed by Weibull and gamma distributions. The Weibull distribution was found to be the best model for determining PDF. The gamma model gave the worst performance in determining both CDF and PDF values. The observed cumulative probability using the exponential model did not fit the expected values." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725875__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725875__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725875__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725875__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725875__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725875__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725875__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "There was not enough information available about which model among the Weibull, gamma, and exponential distributions is suitable to estimate PDF and CDF of wind speed." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725875__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study compared Weibull, gamma, and exponential distribution models to identify suitable distribution functions for wind-speed characteristics in Medan City." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725964__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725964__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725964__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Wind-speed data from 10 Tamil Nadu stations for 1980–2018 were fitted with nine probability distribution models. Model fit was ranked using the Anderson-Darling statistical test." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725964__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "A single probability distribution did not provide the best fit for all 10 stations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725964__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The generalised extreme value distribution provided the best fit for six stations, whereas the Kumaraswamy distribution provided the best fit for four stations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725964__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The Kumaraswamy distribution ranked between 1 and 3 for 9 of the 10 stations and was therefore reported as more consistent than the other distributions within this study." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725964__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The Kumaraswamy distribution provided the best fit even when the wind-speed distribution was negatively skewed, whereas Nakagami performed satisfactorily only for slightly positively skewed distributions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725964__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "All stations analysed in this study had platykurtic wind-speed distributions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725964__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725964__objective_001> .
