<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725964__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Studies related to the prediction of wind energy potential in Tamil Nadu are limited, though the state has high potential for renewable energy extraction in India." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725964__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "AndersonDarlingStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R725964__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Further study should assess the performance of the Kumaraswamy distribution for mesokurtic and leptokurtic wind-speed distributions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Average hourly wind-speed data from the Poprad meteorological station for 2005–2021 were analysed as a whole and split into seasonal and monthly datasets. Two-parameter Weibull, three-parameter Weibull, and exponentiated Weibull distributions were fitted using the maximum likelihood method and compared using KS, AD, AIC, BIC, RMSE, and R2 criteria. Wind direction was also analysed using wind roses." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The exponentiated Weibull distribution provided a better fit than W2 and W3 for the entire period and seasonal wind-speed data. It performed best for monthly data except in February and March, when W3 performed better and EW was second best. The authors conclude that EW is a suitable alternative for wind-speed data with high positive skewness and kurtosis." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "The authors state that no published paper had focused on applying the exponentiated Weibull distribution to model wind speed at a higher-altitude inland location." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "AndersonDarlingStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "Akaike’s information criterion" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "Bayesian information criterion" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726086__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Hourly wind-speed data from the Poprad-Tatry airport meteorological station in Northern Slovakia were modelled using W2, W3, and EW distributions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726125__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726125__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726125__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Hourly wind-speed data from Bozcaada, Gökçeada, and Bilecik between October 2015 and September 2016 were converted to frequency distributions. A Finsler geometry-based distribution approach was compared with two-parameter Weibull and Rayleigh distributions using RMSE and wind power-density-error analyses." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726125__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The authors report that the Finsler geometry model had a better fit with measured probability-density distributions than the Weibull and Rayleigh models in the monthly analysis. The Finsler geometry method had small errors for power-density estimation over 12 months, whereas the Rayleigh distribution had high error rates in both monthly wind-speed modeling and power-density estimation. Weibull provided results similar to Finsler in some months." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726125__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726125__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726125__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726125__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726125__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726125__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726125__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726125__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726125__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726125__location_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726125__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726125__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726125__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726125__analysis_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726125__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726125__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726125__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "The performance of the Finsler geometry method at low and high wind speeds had not been compared and had not been investigated in terms of power density." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726125__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R726125__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study compares the Finsler geometry method with Weibull and Rayleigh models for low- and high-wind-speed regions and evaluates power-density errors." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study analyzed time series of hourly daily measured wind-speed data from five Rwandan meteorological stations for 1974–1993, averaged the data monthly, fitted Weibull and Rayleigh probability density functions, estimated Weibull parameters using the Maximum Likelihood method, extrapolated wind characteristics to higher altitudes, calculated wind power density, and plotted wind roses." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The Weibull probability density distribution was found to be the best-fitting model for the empirical distribution of measured monthly average wind speeds. At 60 m, Gisenyi had the greatest reported mean monthly wind speed and mean power density among the stations considered. On average, the windy season coincides with the rainy season in most parts of Rwanda, except in the western part where it coincides with the dry season." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__location_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__location_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__location_005> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__location_006> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "In Rwanda, wind energy had been unexplored and no study had been conducted to explore that resource." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "MBE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study investigated wind-energy-resource potential in Rwanda and provided a database intended for users of wind power." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727032__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "The authors recommend more detailed and systematic analyses of wind-speed patterns using continuous wind-speed data for at least one year, with seasonal, monthly, daily, and hourly analyses compared with the present results to obtain more reliable long-term averages." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727428__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727428__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727428__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study fits an inverse Weibull distribution to wind-speed data using a modified maximum likelihood approach, compares estimation approaches, evaluates goodness of fit using MAPE, RMSE, and R2, and describes sensitivity, calibration, and validation procedures." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727428__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The authors report that the proposed method produced d = 2.0082 and z = 6.1962, with RMSE = 0.0002 and R2 = 0.9999 in the reported parameter-estimation computation. They conclude that the inverse Weibull distribution with the modified maximum likelihood function provides a framework for wind-speed evaluation and renewable-energy resource assessment." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727428__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727428__objective_001> .
