<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727428__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Further research can explore additional statistical techniques and models, validate and refine the approach using larger and more diverse datasets from different geographical regions and wind sites, and incorporate machine-learning and artificial-intelligence algorithms for more precise wind-speed predictions and forecasts." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727440__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study fitted three original probability distribution functions, six two-component mixture probability distribution functions, and one three-component mixture Weibull distribution to hourly mean wind speed data from a wind farm in Texas. Parameters were estimated using the Aquila Optimizer method with RMSE as the objective function, and distributions were compared using RMSE, R2, and chi-square error." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For the utilized wind speed data, Gamma gave the best fit among the three original distributions. The two-component mixture Weibull distribution gave the best fit among the original and two-component mixture distributions, and the three-component mixture Weibull distribution gave the best fit among all distributions proposed in the study." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727440__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727440__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727440__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727440__performance_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727440__performance_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727440__performance_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727440__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "More three-component mixture distributions can be investigated and compared with the three-component mixture Weibull distribution." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study analyzed wind-speed and wind-direction data collected at 10 m in the Arzew region, fitted a Weibull distribution, used WAsP for wind-resource assessment, mapping and wind-farm simulations, compared four wind-turbine technologies under one-row and two-row layouts, and used HOMER for economic and environmental evaluation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The Arzew study site had a mean wind speed of 4.46 m/s at 10 m height, with annual mean wind-speed variation between 3.9 m/s and 4.79 m/s during the stated 10-year study period." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The Weibull shape parameter k varied from 1.38 to 2.12, and estimated power density varied from 100 W/m2 to 132 W/m2." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The single-row structure produced more energy for all wind-turbine models than the two-row structure." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Among the technologies evaluated, the Power Wind wind farm had the lowest reported cost of energy, $0.068/kWh, and the lowest reported carbon-dioxide quantity, 3,892,065 kg/year." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__objective_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__analysis_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727445__energysystem_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727542__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study used a bottom-up GIS-based offshore-wind resource-assessment approach. ERA5 monthly-average wind speeds were processed, extrapolated from 10 m to 100 m using the logarithmic wind profile law, and used with a Rayleigh wind-speed distribution, the Vestas V164–8 MW power curve, capacity-factor estimation, array-density assumptions, and scenario-specific spatial exclusions to estimate annual energy production. A GIS-based multi-criteria evaluation using capacity factor, bathymetry, distance to the Eskom transmission grid, and distance to commercial harbours identified suitable development regions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "With the minimum wind-quality limitation applied, Scenario 1 was estimated to have 44.52 TWh of annual energy production and Scenario 2 was estimated to have 2 387.08 TWh of annual energy production." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The study identified Richards Bay, Kwa Dukuza, Durban, and Struis Bay as suitable offshore-wind development regions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The estimated annual energy production for Scenario 1 could theoretically meet 14.9% of South Africa’s annual electricity demand, while Scenario 2 could theoretically satisfy annual electricity demand eight times over." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727542__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727542__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727542__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727542__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "The study states that it was the first offshore-wind resource assessment to focus exclusively on the South African context and to identify the most suitable wind-farm development regions within the South African EEZ." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Quantification of offshore-wind energy resources under four development scenarios and GIS-based identification of suitable offshore-wind development regions in the South African exclusive economic zone." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The ERA5 dataset resolution of 0.25° × 0.25° created small data gaps at points where the dataset met study-area borders, including EEZ and terrestrial boundaries." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The study did not consider the effect of shipping lanes on resource potential and site selection." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727542__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727583__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727583__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727583__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study fitted two-parameter Weibull and three-parameter Inverted Kumaraswamy (IKum) distributions to hourly wind-speed data from six stations around Lake Van. IKum parameters were estimated using maximum likelihood, least squares, and maximum product of spacing methods" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727583__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "a Monte-Carlo simulation compared the estimators. Final wind-speed fitting performance was evaluated using RMSE, R2, KS, and power density error criteria." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727583__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The IKum distribution was preferable to the Weibull distribution in terms of RMSE, R2, and KS criteria for four of six stations, and had lower power density error at five of six stations. Weibull had better goodness-of-fit performance at Tatvan and Muradiye" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727583__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "at Muradiye, IKum nevertheless had a smaller power density error. The authors state that IKum can be considered an alternative to Weibull, particularly when data have a high peak or outlying observations in the right tail." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727583__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727583__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727583__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727583__objective_002> .
