<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727583__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727583__characterization_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727583__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727583__characterization_005> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727583__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727583__characterization_006> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727583__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "The authors state that, to their knowledge, no study concerning IKum parameter-estimation methods other than maximum likelihood and Bayesian methods existed in the related literature." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727583__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727583__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727583__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727583__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "power density error (PDE)" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727583__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study used the IKum distribution for the first time to model wind-speed data and compared ML, MPS, and LS estimation methods for its parameters." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727583__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "The behavior of the ML, MPS, and LS estimators should be investigated for small sample sizes, for example n = 30, 50, and 100." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727587__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727587__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727587__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study fitted Weibull, Normal, and generalized extreme value distributions to wind data from Adrar, extrapolated wind speeds from 10 m to the 55 m hub height, calculated expected wind-farm performance using the PDFs and the manufacturer power curve, and compared the predicted outputs with SCADA operating data from the Kaberten wind farm." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727587__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For the studied case, the three distributions gave comparable estimates of average wind speed, while the GEV distribution was more appropriate for assessing wind-turbine annual energy production. The results may change for other sites with different wind regimes and climates and for other wind-turbine types." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727587__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727587__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727587__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727587__objective_002> .
