<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727592__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727592__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727592__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Wind-speed data recorded at 10 m during 2017–2019 were analysed using Weibull graphical and standard deviation methods. Wind characteristics were extrapolated to 70 m, the methods were evaluated using RMSE, Chi-square error and R2, and five commercial wind turbines were simulated using capacity factor." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727592__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Both numerical methods were found appropriate for Weibull-parameter estimation in the study area" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727592__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "however, the standard deviation method gave higher Weibull parameter estimates and higher average monthly wind power density than the graphical method. The Polaris P50-500 had the highest capacity factor among the five simulated commercial turbines for all three years." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727592__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727592__objective_001> .
