<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727661__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Wind-speed data collected at meteorological stations in N'Djamena and Faya Airport over five years were processed using Weibull wind-speed distribution modelling, WAsP-based wind-resource mapping, SRTM topographic data, obstacle and roughness modelling, and vertical extrapolation of wind speed to 100 m using a variable coefficient power law." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "At 10 m from the ground, the reported mean wind speed and energy density were 3.8 m/s and 99 W/m2 in N'Djamena, respectively, and 5.54 m/s and 246 W/m2 in Faya, respectively. The authors conclude that the Faya site offers the greatest wind potential among the two sites considered. At 100 m, mapped low-potential-zone average wind speeds were reported as 6.95 m/s for N'Djamena and 15 m/s for Faya" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "high-potential-zone wind speeds were 7.12 m/s in the North-East direction for N'Djamena and 16.4 m/s in the North-North-East direction for Faya." .
