<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727673__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727673__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727673__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study analysed hourly wind speed, temperature, and air-density measurements at 80 m, fitted a Weibull distribution using the likelihood method, calculated wind-turbine operating hours for five temperature and wind-speed cases, and estimated monthly, seasonal, and annual energy production for one Gamesa G52 wind turbine using a logical temperature equation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727673__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The annual Weibull scale parameter was 6.9 m/s and annual wind velocity was 6.2 m/s. The turbine was most productive in May, with average wind energy of 185.95 MWh. Estimated annual energy production was 1644.75 MWh. Low winds were reported as the principal reason preventing production, while temperature affected production only during summer for limited hours." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727673__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727673__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727673__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727673__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727673__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727673__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727673__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727673__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727673__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727673__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727673__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727673__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727673__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727673__energysystem_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727676__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727676__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727676__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study analysed hourly wind-speed data measured at 10 m above ground level for 2010–2014 at 12 South African locations. Weibull distributions were fitted to site wind characteristics, and annual energy outputs for two Kestrel small wind turbines were calculated by combining site wind probability distributions with turbine power curves. Economic performance was evaluated using simple payback period, net present value, and levelised cost of energy." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727676__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Port Elizabeth had the highest annual energy production for both evaluated turbines, whereas Oudtshoorn, Potchefstroom, and Nelspruit had the lowest annual energy outputs. Cape Peninsula and South Eastern locations had higher probabilities of high wind speeds than the Central and Northern regions. Under the present policies and assumptions considered, the two selected small wind turbines were not economically viable in the locations evaluated because NPVs were below zero and calculated LCOEs were higher than the stated electricity tariff." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727676__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727676__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727676__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727676__location_001> .
