<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727676__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727676__characterization_011> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727676__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727676__characterization_012> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727676__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Little or no known research had evaluated how energy and economic performance affected the growth of small wind generation in South Africa." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727676__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study established energy-productivity and economic-viability findings for small wind energy systems at locations in different South African regions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727676__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727676__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727676__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727676__energysystem_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Daily wind-speed data measured at 10 m at four Nigerian sites were analysed using a two-parameter Weibull Distribution Function. Weibull parameters, wind power density, most probable wind speed, wind speed carrying maximum energy, turbine energy outputs, and capacity factors were estimated." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Among the four investigated sites, Maiduguri was reported as having the best wind-energy potential. Ilorin, Makurdi, and Gombe were classified as wind power class 1 and described as unsuitable for wind power applications, while Maiduguri was classified as class 2 and may be considered for stand-alone applications. WT3 was reported as the most suitable turbine choice for the sites. The conclusion reports a Maiduguri wind power density of 1097.4 W/m2, which conflicts with Table 3, where the value is 107.485 W/m2." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__location_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__location_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__characterization_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__characterization_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__characterization_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Previous Nigerian wind-energy studies were concerned with adequately assessing site wind-power potential." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727714__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study additionally selected adequate wind turbines for the selected locations and determined the effect of wind-turbine parameters on capacity factor." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study statistically assessed wind potential at Adrar, In Salah, Illizi, and Tamanrasset using Weibull distributions fitted to wind data collected every 3 hours over 5 years at 10 m above ground. It evaluated CALORIUS 37 wind-turbine power and annual energy production while accounting for wind, temperature, latitude, longitude, and altitude data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The Weibull shape parameter ranged from 2.0 at Illizi and Tamanrasset to 2.48 at In Salah, while the scale parameter ranged from 4.6 m/s at Illizi to 6.3 m/s at Adrar. Mean wind speed ranged from 4.1 m/s at Illizi to 5.5 m/s at Adrar. Annual CALORIUS 37 energy production ranged from 4467.6 kWh at Illizi to 8409.6 kWh at Adrar. The authors state that the amount of CO2 that can be avoided ranged from 0.90 TE-CO2 for a natural-gas power plant in Illizi to 2.24 TE-CO2 for a gasoil power plant in Adrar." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__objective_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__location_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__location_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__location_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__characterization_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__characterization_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__characterization_004> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727799__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Hourly mean wind speed and wind direction data from 38 UK surface observation stations for 1981–2018 were quality controlled and averaged to daily mean wind speeds. Weibull scale and shape parameters were estimated using empirical, maximum-likelihood, and power-density approaches. Wind speeds were extrapolated from 10 m to 100 m using the 1/7th power law when directly applied to wind turbine functions. Weibull parameters were used to estimate wind power density, characteristic wind speeds, capacity factor, and operation probability for two wind turbines. Long-term trends were assessed using the Mann-Kendall test." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The Weibull distribution modeled daily mean wind-speed probability distributions satisfactorily, with correlation coefficients across the observation network between 0.90 and 0.96. Wind power density varied substantially among sites and regions. Statistically significant long-term changes in annual mean wind speed occurred at 15 of 38 stations but only in three of 11 regions. Wind power density was generally higher in winter than in summer, and 36 of 38 stations had at least twice as much wind power density in winter as in summer." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__analysis_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__characterization_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#reportsCharacterization> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__characterization_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Previous UK wind-speed studies did not clearly state which reported long-term trends were statistically significant, and available assessments did not extend the analysis to 2018." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "The study provides an updated assessment of long-term and seasonal wind-speed variation across the UK using 1981–2018 data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "No additional attempt was made to separate different windstorm types because of the nature of the study and the relatively low likelihood of extreme wind-speed occurrence. Data availability may be restricted because MIDAS data were used under license." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__energysystem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#assessesEnergySystem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R727821__energysystem_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study proposed two variational-Bayesian infinite mixtures of Gaussian distributions, IMoG-I and IMoG-II, based on stick-breaking construction. They were used to fit hourly wind-speed distributions at fourteen Puerto Rico stations and compared with fourteen single distributions, seven homogeneous finite-mixture distributions, and seven heterogeneous finite-mixture distributions using goodness-of-fit indicators." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "IMoG-I and IMoG-II generally outperformed the compared single, heterogeneous-mixture, and homogeneous-mixture distributions across the fourteen Puerto Rico datasets. IMoG-II and IMoG-I ranked first and second, respectively, among the compared models. The models automatically determined useful Gaussian components" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "the optimal number of components was less than 10 for all data considered in this study." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__objective_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__objective_003> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#conductedAt> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__location_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#employsAnalysis> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__analysis_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__problem_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#investigatesResearchProblem> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__problem_002> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "KolmogorovSmirnovStatistic" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R2> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "RMSE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#usesEvaluationMetric> "MAE" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R728960__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "The proposed models will be utilized to estimate wind-speed distributions at unknown locations. The authors also propose studying infinite mixture distributions whose components are Weibull, Gamma, Kappa, Wakeby, or other distributions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R732443__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R732443__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R732443__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Monthly averaged wind-speed data from thirteen meteorological stations in Chad, covering five consecutive years at 10 m above ground level, were statistically analyzed using a two-parameter Weibull distribution. Wind speed carrying maximum energy, wind power density, wind energy density, and wind-direction patterns were evaluated." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R732443__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Higher wind speeds occurred during generally dry weather conditions from November to May, while lower wind speeds occurred during wet conditions from June to October. Based on yearly averaged data, Abéché was the most recommended site for wind-energy generation, followed by N'Djamena, Pala, Mongo, and Faya-Largeau. The study concluded that most assessed sites are promising only for small-scale applications, whereas Am Timan, Bousso, Bokoro, and Ati were not feasible for wind-energy generation because of weak mean wind speeds of around 1 m/s." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R732443__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R732443__objective_001> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R732443__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#hasObjective> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R732443__objective_002> .
