<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563369__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "daily solar radiation estimation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563369__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Compared ERA-Interim reanalysis, eight empirical models and a support vector machine using 2007–2017 observations at Ahvaz, BandarAbbas and Kermanshah, Iran" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563369__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "assessed calibration and validation RMSE." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563369__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "SVM performed best at Ahvaz and Kermanshah" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563369__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "validation RMSE was 242 and 315 J cm-2 day-1 for best empirical comparators. ERA-Interim was a useful fallback but less accurate." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563369__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Sparse radiation measurements limit daily solar-radiation estimation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563369__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test additional machine-learning methods and denser station networks." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563369__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Only three Iranian stations and a limited observation period were used." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563372__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563372__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "short-term solar radiation forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563372__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Evaluated regressions in logs, ARIMA, unobserved-components, transfer functions, neural networks and hybrids on six global-horizontal-radiation datasets at 5, 15, 30 and 60 minute resolutions using true out-of-sample forecasts." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563372__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Log-ARIMA with time-varying coefficients performed best in most tests" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563372__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "cloud-cover transfer functions improved high-resolution forecasts, with occasional neural/hybrid gains at 5-minute resolution." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563372__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Few studies compare many time-series approaches across operational high resolutions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563372__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Systematic out-of-sample comparison across four temporal resolutions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563372__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Evaluate additional sites and probabilistic forecasts." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563372__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Performance depends on site, resolution and weather variability." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563524__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563524__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "environmental assessment of renewable energy" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563524__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Comprehensive literature review of environmental impacts from solar thermal/PV, wind, biomass, geothermal, hydroelectric, tidal, ocean, and osmotic power plants, supplemented by SWOT analysis." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563524__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Renewable plants reduce carbon emissions but can cause land-use, material, biodiversity, water, noise and marine impacts" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563524__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "impacts vary strongly by technology and site." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563524__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "RES technologies are often labeled clean while non-CO2 environmental effects receive less attention." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563524__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Synthesized impacts and opportunities/threats across major RES technologies." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563524__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Develop consistent comparative environmental indicators and mitigation strategies." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563524__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Review findings depend on published life-cycle and case-study evidence." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563613__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563613__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "solar irradiance and climate variability" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563613__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Applied autoregressive integrated moving average models to long-range total solar irradiance at the top of the atmosphere and surface air-temperature time series." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563613__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The same ARIMA model type represented both series" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563613__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "surface temperature closely imitated TSI variability, consistent with random-walk behavior linked to solar activity." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563613__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "The similarity of stochastic variability in solar irradiance and surface temperature needed time-series characterization." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563613__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Provided a common ARIMA representation for comparing the two series." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563613__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test additional climate forcings and longer observational records." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563613__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Analysis is based on selected long-term series and model assumptions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563618__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563618__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hourly solar irradiance prediction" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563618__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed and tested an adaptive alpha-model using measured sunshine duration, air temperature and relative humidity at Jeddah, Saudi Arabia" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563618__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "predicted global, direct and diffuse irradiance." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563618__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Predictions agreed well with measurements, achieving correlation coefficients above 97% and low mean bias error." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563618__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Conventional irradiance models have limited adaptability to local atmospheric conditions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563618__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test the adaptive model across climates and longer periods." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563618__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Validation focused on one site." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563621__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563621__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "short-term solar irradiance forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563621__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Tested three next-hour GHI forecasting methods at Miami and Orlando: direct GHI ARIMA, separate DHI/DNI ARIMA combined with an atmospheric model, and cloud-cover transient ARIMA with nonlinear regression lookup tables." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563621__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Including cloud-cover information improved forecast accuracy relative to irradiance-only approaches." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563621__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Short-term GHI forecasts often omit cloud-transient effects." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563621__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Validate cloud-cover models across more climates and forecast horizons." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563621__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Tests used two US weather stations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563639__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563639__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hybrid renewable-energy forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563639__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Applied non-seasonal Box-Jenkins ARIMA models to daily averages of wind speed, solar irradiance, ambient air temperature and PV-module temperature in Bahrain’s first hybrid system (4.0 kWp PV and 1.7 kWp wind)." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563639__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Different ARIMA specifications captured autocorrelation and provided forecasts for hybrid-system operation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563639__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Hybrid-system management requires forecasts of multiple weather and component variables." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563639__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test seasonal and multivariate models with longer operational records." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563639__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Study concerns one hybrid installation and local climate." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563642__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563642__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hourly global-radiation forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563642__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Combined numerical weather prediction inputs with stationary endogenous data, a multilayer perceptron and ARMA residual modeling" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563642__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "tested hourly forecasts at five Mediterranean sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563642__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Hybrid MLP/ARMA outperformed classical models at all sites, with nRMSE about 14.9%." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563642__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Classical radiation forecasts did not fully exploit NWP and nonlinear temporal structure." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563642__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Assess transferability to other climates and longer horizons." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563642__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Results are based on five Mediterranean locations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563654__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563654__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "day-ahead solar irradiation forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563654__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Tested two multilayer-perceptron architectures on a two-year hourly irradiation series, comparing endogenous/exogenous inputs against ARMA and persistence baselines." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563654__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "A multi-output MLP reduced nRMSE by 1.3 points versus ARMA and 7.8 points versus persistence." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563654__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Day-ahead PV forecasts need nonlinear models that use both historical and external information." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563654__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Validate across more sites and seasons." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563654__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Evaluation used one real-case time series." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563658__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563658__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "daily solar radiation forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563658__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Optimized a multilayer perceptron using pre-treated, stationary multivariate time series for daily global-radiation prediction and assessed alternative network configurations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563658__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The optimized MLP improved daily radiation prediction compared with conventional approaches." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563658__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "ANN forecasts require careful stationarity treatment and architecture selection." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563658__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test robust optimization across additional PV plants." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563658__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Performance depends on preprocessing and site-specific data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563661__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "solar-radiation time-series forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed seasonal ARIMA models using hourly solar-radiation observations from Seoul, South Korea, spanning 1981–2017, and evaluated daily and monthly forecasts." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "SARIMA represented long-term seasonal patterns and provided accurate daily and monthly global-radiation predictions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Few long-term studies jointly forecast daily and monthly radiation with seasonal ARIMA." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Validate with additional Korean stations and exogenous weather variables." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Single Seoul station and historical data period." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563678__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563678__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "small-scale solar-radiation forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563678__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Compared ARMA, nonlinear autoregressive neural network and hybrid ARMA-NAR models for multi-hour hourly and high-frequency solar-radiation forecasts at Ghardaia, Algeria" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563678__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "polynomial detrending was used to stationarize data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563678__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The hybrid ARMA-NAR model improved forecasts by combining linear and nonlinear dynamics." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563678__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Solar series are both nonstationary and nonlinear, limiting single-model forecasts." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563678__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Evaluate additional climates and horizons." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563678__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Validation focused on one Algerian site." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563682__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563682__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "spatial solar-radiation forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563682__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Applied seasonal ARIMA to 34 years of NASA POWER monthly insolation data for the Delhi region and generated four-year forecasts visualized with a marching-square contour algorithm." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563682__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Forecast accuracy reached R2 0.9293, RMSE 0.3529, MAE 0.2659 and MAPE 6.556." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563682__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Spatial solar forecasts are rarely presented as operational contour maps." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563682__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Validate forecasts with ground stations and other regions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563682__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Remote-sensing modeled data and one regional case study." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563685__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563685__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "monthly solar-radiation forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563685__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Applied ARMA and ARIMA models to stationary and non-stationary monthly mean daily global-radiation series for one-, two- and three-month-ahead forecasts." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563685__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Time-series models produced useful multi-month forecasts for large-scale solar-radiation data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563685__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Few studies address operational multi-month solar forecasts using both stationary and non-stationary formulations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563685__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test hybrid and exogenous-variable models." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563685__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Forecast performance depends on stationarity treatment and data source." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563694__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563694__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "multi-resolution irradiance forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563694__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Benchmarked autoregressive and machine-learning time-series models using endogenous global-irradiance data at 5-minute, hourly and daily horizons in Algeria." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563694__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Model performance varied with temporal resolution and forecast horizon" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563694__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "optimized models were especially effective for hourly forecasts." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563694__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Few benchmarks span sub-hourly, hourly and daily horizons in one study." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563694__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Add exogenous weather forecasts and more locations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563694__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Case study limited to Algerian sites and endogenous inputs." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563699__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563699__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hourly global solar forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563699__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Built supervised Support Vector Machine models combined with time-series inputs for one-hour-ahead global horizontal solar radiation at Ghardaia, Algeria" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563699__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "compared with persistence and published models using RMSE, NRMSE, NMBE, MAPE and correlation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563699__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The selected SVM produced accurate one-hour forecasts and outperformed several benchmark models." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563699__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Validate SVM forecasting across climates and horizons." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563699__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Single arid-site case study." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563704__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563704__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "daily global solar-radiation estimation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563704__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed a combined linear Box–Jenkins ARMA and nonlinear ANN model using two years of daily global-radiation observations (2012–2013) at two Algerian climate sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563704__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The combined model improved mean percentage error by 18.1% and 2.7% at one site and 27.26% and 1.39% at the other versus ARMA and ANN, respectively" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563704__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "RMSE reductions were also reported." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563704__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "ARMA and ANN alone do not fully handle both linear and nonlinear solar-radiation dynamics." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563704__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Combined the complementary ARMA and ANN processes for daily radiation estimation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563704__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Validate with longer records and more climates." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563704__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Only two years of data from two sites were analyzed." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563707__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563707__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "daily global solar-radiation modeling" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563707__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Trained, optimized, validated and independently tested MLP, ANFIS, SVM and decision-tree models in sunshine, temperature, meteorological and day-number input groups using five years of high-resolution measurements from Cairo, Egypt." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563707__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "MLP models were most accurate, with RMSE 4.75–31.69% lower than the corresponding best regression models" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563707__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "ANFIS and SVM followed, while decision trees demonstrated useful simple temperature/day-number models." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563707__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Comparative evidence for several machine-learning algorithms and input categories was limited." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563707__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Benchmarked four machine-learning approaches against regression models on independent data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563707__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Evaluate models across more climates and operational datasets." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563707__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "One five-year Cairo case study limits geographic transferability." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563717__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563717__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "daily diffuse solar-radiation estimation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563717__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Compared extreme learning machine, backpropagation neural-network, random-forest, generalized regression neural-network and Iqbal empirical models using daily diffuse radiation at Beijing and Zhengzhou stations in the North China Plain." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563717__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "AI models outperformed the Iqbal model at both stations" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563717__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "the GANN model had the best accuracy, followed by ELM, random forest and GRNN. All models underestimated diffuse radiation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563717__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Diffuse-radiation observations are scarce in the particulate-polluted North China Plain." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563717__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Benchmarked AI and empirical methods using measured daily diffuse radiation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563717__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Extend to more sites and pollution conditions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563717__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Only two stations with diffuse-radiation measurements were assessed." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563720__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563720__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "daily global solar-radiation estimation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563720__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Trained and tested SVM and XGBoost models with daily global radiation, maximum/minimum temperature, transformed precipitation, and extraterrestrial radiation at three humid-subtropical Chinese stations" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563720__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "compared against four empirical models." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563720__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Both machine-learning models outperformed empirical models. Adding precipitation improved RMSE by 5.9–12.2% in training and 8.0–11.5% in testing" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563720__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "XGBoost was generally more accurate, stable and faster than SVM." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563720__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Daily solar radiation is often unmeasured, while commonly available meteorological variables remain underused." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563720__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Evaluated precipitation-enhanced SVM and XGBoost against empirical estimators." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563720__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test across climates and additional weather predictors." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563720__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Only three humid-subtropical stations and selected input variables were examined." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563723__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563723__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hourly solar-irradiance forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563723__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed MLFFNN, RBFNN, SVR, FIS and ANFIS models for hourly irradiance in Abu Musa Island using either local time and meteorological inputs (N1) or past irradiance time-series values (N2)." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563723__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "For N1, SVR and MLFFNN achieved correlation coefficients of 0.9999 and 0.9795, respectively. For N2, SVR, MLFFNN and ANFIS exceeded 0.95 correlation on testing data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563723__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Grid integration requires accurate hourly irradiance forecasts from both weather and time-series inputs." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563723__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Compared five ML algorithms under meteorological and purely autoregressive input strategies." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563723__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Assess models at diverse climates and with additional predictors." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563723__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "One island site limits generalizability." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563728__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563728__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "daily global solar-radiation estimation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563728__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed support vector regression (SVM-R) to estimate daily global solar radiation on a horizontal surface using sunshine ratio alone, trained with 2005–2006 data and tested on 2007 data from Ghardaia, Algeria." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563728__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Testing yielded RMSE 1.59 MJ m-2, relative RMSE 8.46%, and correlation coefficient 97.4%, showing SVM-R is effective using only sunshine ratio." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563728__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Daily global-radiation data are often unavailable in isolated locations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563728__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Provided a simple sunshine-ratio SVM-R estimator for DGSR." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563728__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Validate simple-input SVM-R at other sites and climates." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563728__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Single site and three-year data record." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563732__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563732__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "global horizontal solar-radiation estimation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563732__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Used support vector regression with different combinations of ambient temperature, humidity, atmospheric pressure, day number and wind speed to estimate GHSR from 2009–2011 NISE data at Gurugram, India" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563732__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "compared with hidden Markov and ANN models using RMSE." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563732__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "SVR outperformed hidden Markov and ANN comparators" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563732__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "temperature was the most important input, together with pressure, humidity, day number and wind speed." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563732__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "PV planning requires GHSR estimates where direct measurements may be unavailable." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563732__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Evaluated SVR sensitivity to meteorological-input combinations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563732__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Validate meteorological-input SVR across Indian climates." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563732__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "One three-year site-specific dataset." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563736__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563736__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "two-day-ahead solar irradiance forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563736__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed an hourly naïve Bayes classifier for two-day-ahead GHI prediction using public weather forecasts of temperature, relative humidity, dew point and sky coverage, while representing daylight variation and the diurnal cycle." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563736__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The naïve Bayes model improved forecast results" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563736__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "over an eight-month test set it achieved RMBE 2.73% relative to mean GHI 333.04 Wh m-2." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563736__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Two-day-ahead GHI forecasting needs fast methods using readily available weather forecasts." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563736__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Applied a fast NB classifier that accounts for daylight and diurnal GHI characteristics." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563736__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Evaluate with additional regions and compare operational forecasts." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563736__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Results depend on public weather-forecast quality and tested data conditions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563739__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563739__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hourly solar-component forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563739__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Compared smart persistence, artificial neural networks and random forests for one- to six-hour forecasts of global horizontal, beam normal and diffuse horizontal irradiance measured at Odeillo, France." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563739__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Random forest was most efficient" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563739__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "GHI nRMSE ranged 19.65–27.78%, BNI 34.11–49.08%, and DHI 35.08–49.14% across h+1 to h+6 horizons." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563739__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Component-specific solar forecasts remain challenging under variable meteorological conditions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563739__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Benchmarked RF and ANN against smart persistence for three irradiance components." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563739__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Validate solar-component forecasts at additional climates." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563739__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Single highly variable meteorological site." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563742__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563742__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "multi-day hourly solar-radiation forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563742__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Compared multivariate adaptive regression splines (MARS), classification and regression trees (CART), M5 model trees and random forest for one- to six-day-ahead hourly solar-radiation forecasts using a Gorakhpur, India solar-resource dataset." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563742__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Random forest delivered the best forecasts while CART performed worst among the four tested models." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563742__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Utilities need reliable multi-day hourly solar forecasts for power planning and bidding." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563742__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Benchmarked four tree/regression machine-learning methods for horizons up to six days." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563742__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Assess models at other sites and incorporate weather forecasts." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563742__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Results are based on a single solar-resource site." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563745__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563745__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hourly solar-irradiance estimation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563745__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed and tested SVR, ANN and decision-tree base models and their boosting and bagging ensembles using five years of hourly meteorological data from five Turkish cities" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563745__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "evaluated R2 and RMSE." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563745__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Boosting and bagging ensembles improved base-model RMSE by 4.6–14.6% on average, demonstrating improved solar-irradiance estimation accuracy." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563745__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Ensemble learning beyond random forests had limited detailed evaluation for solar-irradiance prediction." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563745__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Compared boosting and bagging ensembles of three common regression learners." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563745__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Evaluate ensembles with other algorithms and climates." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563745__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Five-city national case study and selected ensemble configurations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563748__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563748__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "satellite-based global solar-radiation estimation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563748__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Evaluated neural-network, support-vector-regression and Gaussian-process regressors for hourly global solar radiation at Toledo, Spain using geostationary Meteosat inputs (cloud index and visible reflectivity), clear-sky radiation, and physical-model outputs" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563748__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "compared with Heliosat-2, CAMS and SolarGIS." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563748__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Machine-learning regressors provided reliable global-radiation estimates from satellite measurements" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563748__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "using physical-model outputs as post-processing inputs produced the best estimates." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563748__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Satellite physical approaches can benefit from data-driven post-processing for local solar-radiation estimation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563748__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Benchmarked regressors and physical models, including physical-model output as ML inputs." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563748__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Validate satellite/ML post-processing across regions and years." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563748__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "One year of data at a single radiometric station." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563751__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563751__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "monthly mean daily solar-radiation estimation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563751__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Compared Simple Membership Function and Fuzzy Rule Generating Technique (SMGRT), deep learning and ANFIS using sunshine duration, extraterrestrial radiation, relative humidity, cloudiness, air temperature and soil temperature at Isparta, Turkey (2007–2016 excluding 2010)." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563751__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "All methods performed well, but SMGRT was slightly better. Its Model 1 using H0, sunshine duration and air temperature had MBE 0.156, MSE 1.878, RMSE 1.371 and R2 0.960." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563751__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Reliable monthly solar-radiation prediction is needed with limited, commonly available meteorological data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563751__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Provided a comparative SMGRT, DL and ANFIS evaluation with multiple predictor combinations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563751__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Validate methods at other climates and stations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563751__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Single Turkish station and historical data record." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563754__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563754__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "solar-radiation forecasting for smart buildings" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563754__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed ANN and recurrent neural-network models from actual meteorological-year data at an Alabama weather station" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563754__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "compared sampling frequencies and moving-window scenarios for solar-radiation prediction." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563754__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "RNN improved NMBE by 47% and RMSE by 26% versus ANN. Increasing data frequency from one hour to ten minutes reduced CV(RMSE) from 30.9% to 9.41% for ANN and 9.83% to 7.64% for RNN" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563754__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "moving window improved RNN NMBE from 0.9% to 0.2%." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563754__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Higher solar-radiation forecast accuracy is needed to support smart-building model predictive control." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563754__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Compared ANN and RNN with data-granularity and moving-window enhancements." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563754__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test more climates, building-control settings, and cloud conditions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563754__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "One local weather station limits broader generalization." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563757__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563757__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "daily diffuse horizontal solar-radiation estimation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563757__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Evaluated SVM, M5 model tree, random forest, XGBoost and CatBoost using six input combinations of daily global radiation, sunshine hours, maximum/minimum temperature and relative humidity from 15 Chinese stations (1996–2015), under limited local and extrinsic-data scenarios." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563757__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Without global radiation, average RMSE increased 42.4% across China (68.3% in subtropical/tropical monsoon regions). SVM was most accurate/generalizable, but CatBoost was recommended based on close accuracy and far lower computation time, particularly for extrinsic data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563757__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Reliable diffuse-radiation prediction is difficult when target stations lack complete or historical local data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563757__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Compared local and extrinsic-data soft-computing models for 15 Chinese stations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563757__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test wider data-sharing configurations and future climates." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563757__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Station selection and historical data may constrain transferability." .
