<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563839__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "GRU was the best model across the comparison, with MAPE 19.28%." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563839__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Accurate solar-radiation forecasting systems using broad meteorological inputs are scarce in Bangladesh." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563839__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Compared three recurrent-network architectures across five cities." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563839__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test additional locations, weather inputs and longer forecast horizons." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563839__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Five cities and available meteorological data constrain wider generalization." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563842__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563842__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "temperature-based daily global solar-radiation prediction" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563842__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed a corrected-SVM approach using air temperature as the sole input: one SVM estimates horizontal global solar radiation, another estimates its error, and a weighted sum gives the corrected prediction. Evaluated at semi-arid Ghardaia, Algeria, using 2013–2015 measurements." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563842__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Corrected-SVM improved conventional SVM: MABE 1.623 vs 1.713, RMSE 2.286 vs 2.575 MJ m-2, relative error 11.35 vs 12.61%, and correlation 94.20 vs 93.06%." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563842__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Daily radiation prediction is needed where only air-temperature measurements are available." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563842__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Corrected conventional SVM estimates by modeling and weighting their residual errors." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563842__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Evaluate corrected SVM in other climates and with additional inputs." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563842__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Single semi-arid site and three-year record." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563845__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563845__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "daily solar-radiation estimation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563845__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Used a continuous-density Hidden Markov Model with Pearson R pattern-similarity clustering to select clusters of meteorological inputs, then a Generalized Fuzzy Model to estimate solar radiation. Tested 15 input combinations using 915 days at the Solar Energy Centre, Gurgaon" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563845__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "trained on 750 days and validated on 165." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563845__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Sunshine duration was the most important predictor" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563845__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "the best combination used all inputs except wind speed and achieved RMSE 7.9124, MAPE 3.0083 and R 0.9921." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563845__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Distance-based clustering and single models may not capture input-pattern similarities for solar-radiation estimation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563845__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Combined shape-based HMM clustering with nonlinear generalized fuzzy modeling." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563845__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test the HMM–fuzzy approach at diverse sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563845__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "One monitoring station and a three-year record." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563848__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563848__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "daily global solar-radiation prediction" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563848__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed a hybrid Coral Reefs Optimization–Extreme Learning Machine model using measured, radiosonde and meteorological-model data at Murcia’s radiometric station" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563848__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "ELM predicts daily global radiation while CRO evolves neural-network weights." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563848__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "CRO–ELM produced more accurate daily global-radiation predictions than classical ELM and support vector regression." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563848__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Daily solar-radiation predictors require improved nonlinear model optimization from heterogeneous meteorological data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563848__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Used Coral Reefs Optimization to evolve ELM weights for daily global-radiation prediction." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563848__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Validate the optimization–learning approach across sites and seasons." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563848__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Single southern-Spain station." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563851__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563851__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "daily solar-radiation time-series prediction" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563851__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Proposed a Genetic Approach Combining Multi-Model Framework: a genetic algorithm dynamically segments the solar series, subsequences are clustered, and a separate time-delay neural network is trained for each pattern. Used 2009 Singapore data for training/tuning and 2010 for validation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563851__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The pattern-specific genetic multi-model framework outperformed comparison algorithms for daily solar-radiation prediction." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563851__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Fixed-length segmentation can miss meaningful stochastic solar-radiation patterns." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563851__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Used genetic dynamic segmentation, cluster-specific models and pattern identification for forecasting." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563851__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test the adaptive segmentation and pattern identification at other sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563851__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Validated on a 24-month single-location series." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563854__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563854__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "clear- and real-sky global-horizontal-radiation forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563854__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed Cuckoo Search-Optimally Pruned Extreme Learning Machine (CS-OP-ELM) forecasting models using direct and direct-recursive strategies. MRSR and leave-one-out cross-validation rank and prune feed-forward-neural-network neurons, and Cuckoo Search optimizes weights. Compared with ARMA, back-propagation NN and OP-ELM using US hourly radiation data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563854__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "CS-OP-ELM achieved the best forecasting performance among the evaluated methods for clear- and real-sky global horizontal radiation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563854__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Solar-radiation forecasts require efficient nonlinear models with automatic neural-architecture optimization." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563854__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Combined neuron pruning, two forecasting strategies and Cuckoo Search weight optimization." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563854__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test the optimized hybrid model across additional climates and horizons." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563854__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Site count is inconsistently described in the text and performance is based on selected US datasets." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563857__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563857__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "monthly global solar-radiation forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563857__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Used monthly mean global solar radiation and 12 meteorological variables from four US sites (1998–2010). Pearson correlations and Apriori association rules selected inputs" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563857__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "radial-basis-function networks were converted to linear regression with hard-ridge node pruning and optimized using Cuckoo Search and Differential Evolution." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563857__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The proposed hard-ridge RBF models optimized by Cuckoo Search and Differential Evolution produced more accurate forecasts than the comparison models." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563857__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Sparse radiation observations demand accurate solar prediction from readily available weather variables." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563857__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Introduced hard-ridge penalized and intelligently optimized RBF forecast models." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563857__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Assess larger station networks and alternative feature-selection methods." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563857__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Four US sites and monthly historical records limit generalization." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563860__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563860__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hourly solar-irradiance forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563860__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed a hybrid self-organizing-map, support-vector-regression and particle-swarm-optimization model. SOM partitions input space into characteristic regions, SVR models each region, and PSO automatically selects SVR parameters" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563860__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "tested in Colorado, USA and Singapore." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563860__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The hybrid SOM–SVR–PSO method outperformed traditional hourly solar-irradiance forecasting models." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563860__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Noise, nonstationarity and SVM parameter sensitivity reduce the reliability of statistical irradiance forecasts." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563860__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Combined SOM partitioning, regional SVR models and PSO parameter selection." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563860__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Validate with other climates and forecast horizons." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563860__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Only two locations were reported." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563863__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563863__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "monthly mean global solar-radiation prediction" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563863__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed an SVM–Firefly Algorithm hybrid model using sunshine duration, maximum temperature and minimum temperature to estimate monthly mean horizontal global solar radiation across Iseyin, Maiduguri and Jos, Nigeria" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563863__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "compared against ANN and genetic-programming models." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563863__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "SVM–FFA was more accurate than ANN and GP. It achieved test RMSE 1.8661, R2 0.7280, correlation 0.8532 and MAPE 11.5192." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563863__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Many weather stations lack solar-radiation records despite having routine meteorological data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563863__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Optimized SVM prediction using Firefly Algorithm with three simple meteorological inputs." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563863__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test the hybrid method at more climates and with further meteorological variables." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563863__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Three Nigerian sites and historical observations may limit generalizability." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563866__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563866__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "daily global solar-radiation forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563866__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed a nonlinear SVM with hard penalty function for 30-day global-radiation forecasts at four US sites. Eclat association-rule mining selected meteorological inputs" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563866__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "SVM was converted to a ridge-regularization problem, hard penalty selected radial-basis-function count, and glowworm swarm optimization tuned parameters." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563866__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The proposed nonlinear hard-penalty SVM with glowworm optimization gave the best forecasting performance versus competitors." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563866__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Grid-connected PV needs accurate daily irradiation forecasts despite sparse radiation observations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563866__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Combined Eclat data mining, hard-penalty SVM basis selection and Glowworm Swarm Optimization." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563866__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Evaluate model robustness in other climates and operational settings." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563866__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Four US sites and selected training/test partitions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563869__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563869__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hourly global solar-radiation prediction" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563869__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed a Firefly Algorithm-optimized random-forest model using hourly sunshine ratio, humidity, ambient temperature, month/day/hour inputs from Subang Meteorological Station in Klang Valley, Malaysia. The algorithm optimized tree and leaf counts" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563869__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "compared with conventional RF, ANN and Firefly-optimized ANN." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563869__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Optimal forest contained 493 trees and one leaf per tree. The proposed model achieved RMSE 18.98%, MAPE 6.38% and MBE 2.86%, outperforming the comparator models." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563869__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Reliable hourly solar-radiation data are needed for designing, sizing and controlling solar-energy systems." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563869__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Optimized random-forest complexity with Firefly Algorithm for hourly global-radiation prediction." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563869__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Validate optimized random forest at other climates and longer records." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563869__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "One-year single-site dataset." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563872__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563872__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "five-day global-horizontal-radiation forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563872__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed a multi-stage ensemble approach for five-day global horizontal radiation forecasts at four Indian locations. The approach uses two-way interaction modeling, Divide-and-Conquer ensembles, LASSO feature selection selected through cross-validation, and Glowworm Swarm Optimization for individual-model weights." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563872__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Training/test experiments at four locations demonstrated the proposed multi-stage ensemble was effective and outperformed competitors." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563872__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Grid-connected PV requires accurate and stable medium-term global-horizontal-radiation forecasts." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563872__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Combined interaction modeling, sparse feature selection and optimized ensemble weighting." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563872__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test additional sites and operational horizons." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563872__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Four locations and selected training/test splits limit generalizability." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563875__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563875__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "yearly mean daily global solar-radiation estimation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563875__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Applied fuzzy regression functions with support vector machines (FRF-SVM) and several kernels to yearly mean daily horizontal global solar-radiation data from Turkey" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563875__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "compared against adaptive neuro-fuzzy and coplot-supported genetic-programming approaches." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563875__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "FRF-SVM with a Gaussian kernel was robust to outliers and overfitting and gave the most accurate estimates among the compared approaches." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563875__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Solar-radiation investment decisions require robust long-term estimates in complex terrain and climate, including data with outliers." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563875__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Combined fuzzy regression functions and SVM kernels for robust global-radiation estimation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563875__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test fuzzy-SVM generalization in more climates and data regimes." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563875__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Results are based on one Turkey regional dataset." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563878__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563878__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "monthly global solar-radiation forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563878__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed a combined artificial-neural-network model whose weights are optimized using a nondominated sorting-based multiobjective bat algorithm (NSMOBA). Statistical and frequent-pattern-growth data-mining methods selected inputs" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563878__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "assessed with monthly solar-radiation and meteorological variables from six US datasets in four experiments." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563878__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The combined model was more accurate and stable than individual models. NSMOBA improved both forecasting accuracy and stability compared with a single bat algorithm." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563878__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Solar-radiation forecasting needs simultaneous accuracy and stability improvement, not accuracy alone." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563878__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Combined multiple ANN models with NSMOBA weight optimization and data-mined input selection." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563878__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Assess the approach in other regions and operational settings." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563878__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Experiments used six US datasets and selected model configurations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563881__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563881__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "daily horizontal solar-radiation prediction" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563881__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed an ANN/simulated-annealing hybrid using SA temperature cycling to improve ANN calibration. Models used thousands of daily observations and meteorological parameters from Mashhad, Iran (1995–2014), with validation phases and sensitivity analysis." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563881__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "ANN/SA accurately predicted daily horizontal solar radiation and outperformed standalone ANN, SVM, existing regression and other machine-learning models." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563881__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Daily solar-radiation prediction models need improved calibration and a practical form for solar-system design." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563881__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Used simulated-annealing temperature cycling to calibrate ANN and derived a practical design equation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563881__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test the practical design equation and hybrid calibration across climates." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563881__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Data are from one Iranian city." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563884__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563884__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "neighboring-station solar-radiation estimation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563884__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Estimated solar radiation at eight Iranian target synoptic stations (1974–2014) with support vector regression coupled to Krill-Herd Algorithm optimization and neighboring-station data" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563884__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "compared against classical SVR." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563884__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "SVR-KHA improved testing accuracy at all target stations. SVR-KHA3 at Isfahan performed best with RMSE 1.98 MJ m-2 day-1, MAPE 7.4%, and R2 0.93." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563884__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Low density, uneven distribution, cost and errors in solar-radiation station data limit accurate estimation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563884__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Integrated neighboring-station data with Krill-Herd-optimized SVR." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563884__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test other regions, station densities and climate regimes." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563884__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Station-network conditions and historical Iranian data may limit transferability." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563887__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "temperature-only global solar-radiation prediction" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed ANFIS-muSG by hybridizing ANFIS with Salp Swarm Algorithm and Grasshopper Optimization Algorithm for global solar-radiation prediction across North Dakota locations. Used nine years (2010–2018) of maximum, mean and minimum air temperatures and compared seven ANFIS and metaheuristic variants." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "ANFIS-muSG improved RMSE-based accuracy by 25.7–54.8% over other models at the study locations, demonstrating effective temperature-only solar-radiation prediction." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Accurate solar-radiation prediction is needed from readily available temperature observations where radiation data are sparse." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Jointly optimized ANFIS using Salp Swarm and Grasshopper Optimization algorithms." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test hybrid metaheuristics across climates and additional predictors." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563887__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "North Dakota data and temperature-only predictors constrain transferability." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563890__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563890__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "global horizontal irradiance forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563890__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed SVR-GOA-BAK by combining support vector regression, Boruta feature selection and Grasshopper Optimization Algorithm hyperparameter tuning for GHI forecasting at Saudi Arabian sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563890__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The hybrid model outperformed standalone SVR by 32.15–39.69% in MAPE across sites" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563890__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "GOA tuning outperformed popular optimizers and reduced manual tuning/overfitting risks." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563890__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Solar-radiation variability and uncertainty challenge generalizable GHI forecasts" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563890__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "manual SVR tuning risks overfitting." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563890__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Automated Boruta feature selection and GOA hyperparameter optimization in an SVR framework." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563890__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test online feature selection and additional climates." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563890__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Specific Saudi study sites and simulation conditions may limit transferability." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563893__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563893__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "robust solar-radiation time-series prediction" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563893__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Proposed a hybrid model combining wavelet-transform denoising, CEEMDAN decomposition into intrinsic mode functions, improved Atom Search Optimization and outlier-robust extreme learning machine. IASO uses PWLCM mapping and Lévy flight to optimize ORELM weights and thresholds" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563893__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "compared against ten benchmarks." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563893__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Benchmark comparisons verified the proposed WT–CEEMDAN–IASO–ORELM model’s robustness and accuracy for solar-radiation prediction." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563893__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Solar-radiation sequence volatility and outliers challenge reliable prediction models." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563893__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Denoised/decomposed the series and robustly optimized ORELM using an improved metaheuristic." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563893__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test real-time deployment and wider climatic datasets." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563893__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Detailed transferability depends on data settings and benchmark selection." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563896__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563896__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "daily global solar-radiation prediction" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563896__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed CNN-REGST, integrating a CNN with dual-stage stacked regression and a level-1 SVM optimized using HyperOpt. Metaheuristic feature selection chose inputs from global climate models and observations, derived using a marine predator algorithm, for six Queensland solar farms" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563896__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "evaluated year-round and compared with deep, machine-learning and persistence models." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563896__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "CNN-REGST was significantly more accurate than CNN, LSTM, DNN, ELM, REGST, random forest, gradient boosting, MARS and persistence benchmarks for daily GSR." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563896__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Efficient high-accuracy GSR forecasts are needed for grid-integrated solar-energy operations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563896__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Combined deep convolution, stacked regression, SVM, HyperOpt and metaheuristic feature selection." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563896__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Validate broader regions and real-time solar-monitoring implementation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563896__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Study evaluated six Queensland solar farms and available climate/observational predictors." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563899__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563899__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "daily global solar-radiation prediction" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563899__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed hybrid computational-intelligence models coupling Covariance Matrix Adaptive Evolution Strategy (CMA-ES) with Extreme Gradient Boosting and Multivariate Adaptive Regression Splines for daily solar radiation. Evaluated using climate parameters at Boromo, Dori, Gaoua and Po stations in Burkina Faso." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563899__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Hybrid frameworks improved testing RMSE accuracy by 17.2%, 4.9%, 39.8% and 44.5% at Boromo, Dori, Gaoua and Po, respectively, and showed strong predictive performance." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563899__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Solar-system design and management require accurate robust daily radiation predictions from climate data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563899__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Hybridized CMA-ES with XGB and MARS to construct a robust daily solar-radiation surrogate." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563899__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Evaluate the hybrid models across more climates and operational datasets." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563899__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Four stations in one sub-Saharan region." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563902__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563902__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "monthly average daily global solar-radiation prediction" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563902__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Compared feed-forward neural network, three Angstrom-type empirical models, Holt-Winters time series and response surface methodology using pressure, relative humidity, wind speed, ambient temperature and sunshine data for Ankara, Karaman, Kilis and Şırnak, Turkey." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563902__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "All models achieved R2 0.952–0.993, MAPE below 10%, and RMSE below 2 MJ m-2 day-1. ANN was best overall (mean R2 0.9911" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563902__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "MBE 0.1323 MJ m-2 day-1" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563902__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "RMSE 0.78 MJ m-2 day-1" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563902__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "MAPE 4.9263%" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563902__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "t-stat 0.582), followed by Holt-Winters, RSM and empirical models." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563902__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Solar-radiation measurements are unavailable at many weather stations, requiring accurate model selection." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563902__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Compared representative machine-learning, empirical, time-series and mathematical modeling classes." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563902__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Extend comparison to other climates and real-time forecasting." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563902__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Four province case study and monthly inputs." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563911__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "inclined-surface solar-irradiance forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Trained ANN models for solar irradiance on an inclined surface in metropolitan Douala using 30-minute data from the IUT Douala meteorological station (17 January 2019–30 October 2020). Tested variable combinations of temperature, wind speed, humidity and air pressure" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "data were preprocessed in Excel and modeled in MATLAB with 80/15/5 train/validation/test split." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "A logistic sigmoid ANN with 50 hidden neurons achieved a 98.883% correlation coefficient between observed and estimated solar irradiation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Erratic irradiance driven by climatic fluctuations makes solar prediction difficult in Central Africa." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Optimized ANN input combinations and hidden-layer activation/size for inclined-surface irradiance." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Validate across Central African sites and seasons." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563911__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "A single station and about two years of data limit spatial and temporal generalization." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563914__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563914__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "short-range solar-irradiance numerical weather prediction" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563914__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Tested 3D-Var assimilation of SEVIRI radiances from Meteosat Second Generation into WRF-ARW Solar v3.8.1. Compared hourly GHI with ARPA ground data and MSG shortwave irradiance estimates, and cloud coverage with MSG Cloud Mask, in two Italian case studies." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563914__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Under clear sky, WRF Solar achieved correlation 0.995. Under cloudy conditions, SEVIRI assimilation improved irradiance/cloud forecasts, reducing one-hour cloud-cover MBE from 41.62 to 20.29 W m-2 and improving the first three forecast hours." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563914__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Variable solar generation requires reliable high-resolution short-term irradiance forecasts for operations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563914__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Assimilated MSG/SEVIRI radiances in WRF Solar with 3D-Var to improve short-range forecasts." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563914__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Extend assimilation evaluation across seasons and more forecast cases." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563914__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Only two preliminary case studies." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563917__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563917__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "day-ahead solar-radiation forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563917__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed a hybrid WRF numerical-weather-prediction and clearness-index-based Kalman filter model. Evaluated on one-year photovoltaic-plant solar-radiation data at Maizuru, Japan and Qinghai, China under different sky conditions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563917__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The hybrid method surpassed WRF alone. Under clear skies, MBE accuracy improved 95.7% in Maizuru and 90.9% in Qinghai" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563917__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "RMSE accuracy improved 42.2% and 26.8%, respectively." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563917__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Day-ahead solar forecasts are essential for grid balancing, dispatch, scheduling and trading, but standard Kalman filters miss sudden error changes." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563917__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Corrected WRF forecasts with a clearness-index Kalman filter." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563917__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test more climates and sudden-error-change conditions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563917__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Two PV plant sites and one-year datasets." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563920__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563920__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "photovoltaic maximum power point tracking" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563920__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Modeled a PV panel with a boost converter and MPPT controller in PSIM. Implemented incremental conductance and Kalman-filter algorithms in C/PSIM C blocks, then simulated under stable and variable environmental conditions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563920__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Kalman-filter MPPT outperformed incremental conductance in response time, efficiency and steady-state oscillations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563920__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "PV systems require fast and stable maximum-power tracking under variable irradiance and temperature." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563920__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Compared Kalman filtering with incremental conductance in a simulated boost-converter PV system." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563920__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Validate both algorithms on physical PV hardware." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563920__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Simulation study" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563920__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "performance depends on modeled system and test conditions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563923__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563923__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "solar-wind data assimilation and space-weather forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563923__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Conducted twin experiments applying Local Ensemble Transform Kalman Filter (LETKF) data assimilation to the ENLIL solar-wind model. Wang-Sheeley-Arge supplied boundary conditions" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563923__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "synthetic density, temperature and momentum observations were generated every 4.5 hours at 0.6 AU." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563923__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "LETKF improved modeled state at the observation point and forecast skill near Earth for observed and unobserved variables, but assimilating a single spatial observation created artificial wave-like gradients that propagated Earthward." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563923__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Data assimilation is underused in solar-wind prediction because of limited observations and technical challenges." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563923__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "First in-depth application of advanced NWP-style data assimilation to solar-wind forecasting." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563923__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Use remote solar-wind observations and address spurious gradients for operational assimilation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563923__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Synthetic data and a single-observation configuration limit operational conclusions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563927__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563927__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "intraday satellite-based solar-irradiance forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563927__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Described and validated a satellite-image intraday solar forecast over three years in Paris for horizons up to six hours. Assessed clear-sky index, solar zenith angle, 10 km surrounding cloud patterns and North Atlantic weather regimes as predictors of forecast uncertainty." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563927__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Forecast skill was positive versus persistence (up to 15%) and NWP (20–40%). Error increased as solar zenith angle and clear-sky index decreased" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563927__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Atlantic Ridge had highest and Scandinavian Blocking lowest errors, with relative RMSE gaps of 8–10% in summer and 18–30% by horizon." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563927__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "PV penetration needs accurate intraday forecasts and advance knowledge of uncertainty driven by evolving clouds." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563927__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Identified weather, cloud and irradiance predictors of satellite-forecast reliability." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563927__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Extend reliability predictors to other regions and integrate them with operational forecast systems." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563927__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Validation is specific to Paris and satellite coverage." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563930__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563930__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "ultra-short-term photovoltaic power prediction" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563930__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Proposed a Kalman-filter PV-power prediction model based on forecasting experience. Hourly solar-irradiance forecasting, NWP data and a photoelectric conversion model generate ground-irradiance/PV-power forecast experience" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563930__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "fitted Kalman dynamics and measured power iteratively correct prediction error. Evaluated using DKASC data simulation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563930__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The proposed model reduced error variability and provided more accurate ultra-short-term PV-power predictions than comparison approaches in DKASC simulations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563930__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Historical-experience PV forecasts lose accuracy during anomalous conditions, and photoelectric conversion equations are difficult to model directly." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563930__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Fused NWP-driven forecast experience with Kalman error correction using measured power." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563930__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Validate in real PV energy-storage power stations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563930__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Evidence is simulation-based and depends on forecast-experience/model assumptions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563933__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563933__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "solar energy potential and solar-electric-vehicle planning" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563933__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Trained LSTM networks to predict solar irradiation and temperature over 24 hours from MERRA-2 hourly temperature, relative humidity, pressure, wind speed/direction, irradiation and rainfall data for 20 northern Cameroon locations, 2000–2022" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563933__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "tested at Makary and Banyo." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563933__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "LSTM prediction achieved 92.45% accuracy and RMSE 20.9. Average solar-energy potential was 2.193 MWh m-2 year-1 at Makary and 1.949 at Banyo, supporting solar-plant, PV/EV fleet and charging-station site selection." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563933__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Northern Cameroon needs solar-resource forecasts and potential estimates to support PV and solar-EV development." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563933__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Used 23 years of MERRA-2 data and LSTM predictions to map resource potential across 20 locations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563933__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Validate predictions against local measurements and expand EV deployment analysis." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563933__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Reanalysis-based analysis and testing at two highlighted localities." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563937__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563937__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "theoretical incident solar-radiation modeling" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563937__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Applied the Capderou theoretical method with Klein day calculations to determine hourly global, direct and diffuse solar-radiation components on horizontal and inclined surfaces across all months in N’Djamena, Chad." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563937__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Hourly component estimates across January–December agreed satisfactorily with comparable literature values, supporting Capderou-method application outside a desert climate." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563937__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Chad lacks meteorological stations to measure solar radiation throughout the country." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563937__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Provided a theoretical Capderou correlation model for global, direct and diffuse radiation on horizontal and tilted planes." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563937__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Establish ground monitoring and validate the model across Chad." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563937__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "No countrywide solar-radiation measurement network was available for direct validation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563974__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563974__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "concentrated solar power site suitability and potential assessment" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563974__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Applied a hybrid multi-criteria decision-making Analytic Hierarchy Process and GIS to assess wet-cooled grid-connected CSP suitability across Cameroon. Criteria included DNI, temperature, slope, elevation, distances to grid/roads/railways/homes/watercourses and land use" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563974__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "evaluated technical, socio-economic and equal-weight scenarios." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563974__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "42.35% of land was unsuitable" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563974__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "44% suitable, 13.46% highly suitable and 0.01% most suitable. Far North contained highly suitable areas. Standard-scenario theoretical potential was 37,917.005 TWh/year, varying across sensitivity scenarios." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563974__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Cameroon needs transparent, spatially explicit CSP site-selection and potential estimates for grid-connected projects." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563974__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Integrated AHP weighting and GIS mapping to rank CSP site suitability and theoretical potential." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563974__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Incorporate refined population density, security indicators and minimum surface-area constraints." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563974__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Results depend on criteria weights, spatial datasets and CSP technical assumptions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563977__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563977__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "solar irradiance and photovoltaic-power estimation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563977__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Compared physical and machine-learning models at each solar-power modeling step—global horizontal irradiance, direct normal irradiance, global tilted irradiance and PV power—using hourly Seoul data from April 2011 to December 2017." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563977__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "With suitable inputs, ML models generally outperformed physical models and substantially reduced mean bias difference: GHI MBD 0.96% and PV-power MBD 0.03%. LSTM and GRU were recommended ML models, while physical PV-power models reduced RMSD more efficiently." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563977__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "No prior study had compared machine-learning accuracy with physical models at every stage of solar-power modeling." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563977__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Systematically compared physical and ML approaches from irradiance components through PV power." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563977__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test other climates and assess hybrid physical/ML model combinations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563977__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Results use a Seoul dataset and model performance depended on selected inputs." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563980__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563980__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "global solar-radiation estimation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563980__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Evaluated six empirical models for global solar radiation on a horizontal surface at Abeche, Chad using data from the General Directorate of National Meteorology of Chad" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563980__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "used statistical indicators and NASA data validation to identify the most accurate model." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563980__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The Sabbagh model performed best, estimating an average 6.354 kWh m-2 with average deviation −3.704%, and was validated against NASA data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563980__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Reliable local solar-radiation estimates are needed to support renewable-energy planning in Chad." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563980__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Benchmarked six empirical models against meteorological and NASA data for Abeche." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563980__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Extend testing to more Chadian sites and compare modern ML models." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563980__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "One site and empirical models only." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563984__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563984__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "real-time solar irradiance estimation for photovoltaic systems" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563984__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed and simulated an Environmental Sensor-less Hybrid Analytical-Machine Learning (ESHAML) framework combining a PV analytical model, Bayesian-regularized neural network temperature approximation, synthetic data generation, and fractional-area MPPT" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563984__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "experimentally validated it with an IoT Trio-PV Monitor in Dschang, Cameroon." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563984__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "ESHAML achieved 2.668–3.561% simulated MAPE and 4.9355% experimental MAPE, with MPPT convergence below 20 ms" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563984__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "its experimental MAPE outperformed Moshksar & Ghanbari (34.96%) and Abe et al. (7%)." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563984__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Costly environmental-sensor dependence, data scarcity, integration complexity, and insufficient real-time accuracy hinder solar-irradiance estimation in resource-constrained regions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563984__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Provides a sensorless hybrid PV/ML estimator with synthetic-data training and fast MPPT for real-time operation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563984__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Validate at additional sites and PV configurations and deploy the framework for wider real-time PV applications." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563984__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Validation was conducted at one Cameroon site for three consecutive days" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563984__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "reported results depend on the studied PV setup and atmospheric conditions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563987__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563987__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "direct solar radiation resource assessment for concentrating solar power" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563987__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Used 2015 HelioClim-3 satellite-derived global horizontal irradiation and the Liu–Jordan isotropic model to calculate direct solar radiation on horizontal and south-facing 15° inclined planes for Abeche, Aozou, Faya-Largeau, Moundou, and N’Djamena, Chad." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563987__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Northern Chad had higher direct solar radiation than the south" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563987__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Moundou had the lowest values. Peak irradiance reached 800 W/m² around 11:00–13:00. Reported annual average direct solar radiation was at least 1800 kWh/m²/year, indicating favorable concentrating-solar resource." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563987__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Sparse radiometric and meteorological stations leave Chad’s solar climate and direct radiation poorly characterized." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563987__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Estimates direct radiation for five representative Chad locations from satellite data and a geometric radiation model." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563987__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Use the estimated resource to support thermo-solar plant siting and incorporate additional measured data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563987__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Results are modelled satellite-data estimates for 2015 rather than direct radiometric-station observations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563991__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563991__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "short-term solar irradiation forecasting for photovoltaic energy planning" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563991__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Used Weka to select mean solar irradiation, maximum temperature, and measurement time" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563991__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "trained a feed-forward multilayer perceptron ANN using Levenberg–Marquardt on 70% of measured Gandon meteorological data and tested it across twelve 30–360 minute horizons." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563991__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Forecast performance declined modestly as the horizon increased. The 360-minute horizon achieved R=0.961 and RMSE=0.075" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563991__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "the authors conclude six-hour forecasting is feasible." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563991__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Existing Senegal solar forecasts generally use a single short horizon, limiting investors’ ability to select forecasting windows that match demand and available data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563991__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Provides and compares twelve ANN forecasts from 30 minutes to six hours." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563991__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Extend the multi-horizon approach to Senegal’s other regions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563991__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The model was evaluated at one north-west Senegal site and with the reported meteorological measurements." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563995__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563995__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "photovoltaic power-output prediction" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563995__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Compared three-, four-, and five-parameter PV equivalent-circuit models with NOCT and Sandia cell-temperature models. Calibrated models from manufacturer datasheets and experimental I–V data, then tested monocrystalline and polycrystalline 245 Wp modules with actual weather measurements at SolarTechLab, Politecnico di Milano." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563995__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Hourly forecast errors were usually below 15 Wh. No clear advantage of greater circuit complexity was found" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563995__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "calibration data and thermal model mattered more. Sandia with experimental calibration was most accurate for monocrystalline cells, while NOCT with manufacturer data performed better for polycrystalline cells. Errors could be below 1% NMAE and 2% WMAE." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563995__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "PV power-model accuracy depends on circuit complexity, temperature estimation, and calibration data, but their comparative effects across cell types were unclear." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563995__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Compares physical circuit and thermal models using both datasheet and measured calibration for mono- and polycrystalline modules." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563995__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Compare the physical models with neural-network methods and account for PV ageing through recalibration every one or two years." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563995__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Predictions used actual weather measurements, excluding weather-forecast error, and evaluations concerned the tested module types and site." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563998__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563998__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "next-day solar irradiance forecasting with numerical weather prediction" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563998__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Ran WRF at 27-, 9-, and 3-km nested resolution over Singapore for 2015–2016" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563998__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "compared WRF-only, 3DVAR, and 4DVAR initialisations using ground, satellite, and GPS observations. Post-processed forecasts with a 500-tree random forest trained in 2015 and tested in 2016." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563998__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Raw 4DVAR had the lowest RMSE (216 W/m², 46% relative RMSE) versus 3DVAR (237 W/m²) and WRF-only (263 W/m²). After random-forest post-processing, 4DVAR remained best (173 W/m², 37% relative RMSE) and all NWP methods outperformed climatology and persistence ensemble." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563998__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Initial-condition errors limit tropical NWP solar forecasts" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563998__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Singapore WRF forecasts had not compared 3DVAR and 4DVAR assimilation for next-day irradiance." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563998__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Assimilates ground, satellite, and GPS observations into WRF with 3DVAR and 4DVAR, then compares their next-day irradiance forecasts." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563998__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Assess ensemble or hybrid 3DVAR/EnKF/EMOS methods and examine high-error overcast events." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563998__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Overcast conditions had very large errors" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563998__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "4DVAR was computationally costlier than 3DVAR and the comparison was evaluated in Singapore." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564001__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564001__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "photovoltaic state estimation and maximum power point tracking" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564001__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed an Extended Kalman Filter (EKF) that combines a dynamic PV thermal model and sinusoidal irradiation-state model to estimate module temperature and effective irradiation from PV measurements. Used its state estimates in a state-based MPPT controller and simulated 250 W PV performance with one-minute National Wind Technology Center weather data for clear, partly cloudy, and severely cloudy days." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564001__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "EKF temperature estimates were generally within 2 K and irradiation estimates within 10 W/m² of true values. The state-based MPPT stayed within 2 W of maximum power and increased daily energy by approximately 1%, 5%, and 8.5% over incremental conductance for clear, partly cloudy, and severely cloudy cases respectively." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564001__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Temperature and irradiation estimation and MPPT have usually been treated separately, with many methods requiring costly sensors or lacking observer feedback." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564001__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Uses a feedback EKF to estimate both PV states and supplies them to a state-based MPPT controller." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564001__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Validate the estimator/controller experimentally and consider additional PV model effects." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564001__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Validation was simulation-based using a simplified lumped PV thermal model" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564001__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "long-wave radiation was neglected." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564008__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564008__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "very-short-term solar irradiance nowcasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564008__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed a hybrid nowcaster that fuses a time-varying Kalman-filter predictor and multiple regressor. A support-vector-machine ramp-down classifier uses all-sky-image features and irradiance history" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564008__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "three local-RMSE fusion alternatives were evaluated with four-fold cross-validation on 2014 Taiwan data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564008__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Fusion alternative 2, which selects the Kalman prediction only when its local RMSE is below a threshold, was more stable and generally outperformed alternatives 1 and 3, standalone regressor, fixed/time-varying Kalman filter, and compared neural network. Accuracy degraded only slightly between 10- and 20-minute horizons." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564008__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Cloud movement and ramp-down events make high-resolution irradiance nowcasting difficult" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564008__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "individual Kalman or regression predictors excel under different irradiance variability." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564008__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Combines adaptive Kalman and regression predictions according to recent local RMSE and anticipated ramp-down events." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564008__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Apply the hybrid mechanism to other sites and nowcasting conditions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564008__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Evaluated at one marine-climate site" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564008__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "numerical chart values were not tabulated in the paper text." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564076__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564076__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "daily global solar irradiance forecasting for energy harvesting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564076__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Compared FoBa, leapForward, spikeslab, Cubist, and bagEarthGCV endogenous machine-learning models using minute-resolution NREL solar irradiance data from 2010–2015. Used 70/30 training/testing, same-month historical samples, seasonal 2016 test days, and 1-, 24-, and 48-hour forecast horizons." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564076__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Spikeslab and Cubist were most promising and stable across seasons and horizons. Best 48-hour result was spikeslab on 30 August (91.67% accuracy, R=0.92, RMSE=22.73)" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564076__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "unstable June weather had lower accuracy and higher error." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564076__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Solar-resource seasonal variability and uncertain selection of historical days/time slots make reliable multi-horizon irradiance prediction difficult." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564076__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Systematically compares five machine-learning methods and historical-data configurations across seasonal 1–48 hour forecasts." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564076__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Extend the machine-learning forecasting approach with additional inputs and locations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564076__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "One NREL site and historical irradiance-only endogenous modelling" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564076__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "effectiveness depends on weather and input-data selection." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564084__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564084__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "daily global solar radiation estimation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564084__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Trained a four-dense-layer deep neural network with one dropout layer, mean-square-error loss, Adadelta optimisation, and five-fold cross-validation. Tested 16 input combinations of extraterrestrial radiation, sunshine duration, cloud cover, minimum temperature, and maximum temperature using daily data from 34 Turkish stations (2001–2007)." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564084__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The all-input C16 model was best overall: R²=0.980, RMSE=0.78 MJ/m²/day, and MAE=0.61 MJ/m²/day. Sunshine duration was the strongest input" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564084__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "cloud cover was second, while temperature added smaller gains. The best station result was Kirikkale (R²=0.992, MAE=0.40, RMSE=0.52)." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564084__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Sparse or unreliable solar-radiation measurements require accurate estimation from routinely available meteorological and astronomical variables." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564084__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Evaluates deep learning across a nationally distributed 34-station dataset and input combinations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564084__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Apply the model to similar regions and additional solar-radiation estimation settings." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564084__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Performance is based on Turkish station data and selected daily meteorological/astronomical inputs." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564088__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564088__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hourly solar irradiance forecasting for photovoltaic grid stability" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564088__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Compared time-series LSTM, ConvLSTM, CNN, random forest, support vector regression, and XGBoost models using hourly Johannesburg temperature, solar irradiance, and sunshine-duration data. Cleaned 2009–2018 Meteoblue records, removed nighttime zeros, used 80/20 training/testing, and varied training data from four months to ten years." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564088__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "ConvLSTM was best: nRMSE=4.05% for 80% of one year at 500 epochs and 1.51% using ten years. With a one-year dataset, LSTM, XGBoost, SVR, RF, and CNN nRMSE values were 4.72%, 6.63%, 7.8%, 19.8%, and 12.61%, respectively." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564088__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "ConvLSTM had not been compared with LSTM, CNN, and conventional machine-learning models for hourly solar irradiance forecasting using Johannesburg data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564088__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Benchmarks ConvLSTM alongside five AI methods using historical city weather data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564088__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Deploy ConvLSTM forecasts in solar farms to support stable PV-grid operation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564088__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Performance depends on local weather, training data size, and model parameters" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564088__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "evaluation used historical Johannesburg data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564093__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564093__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "daily global solar radiation prediction" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564093__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Compared support vector machine, feed-forward back-propagation ANN, kernel nearest neighbor, and deep learning using daily minimum/maximum temperature, cloud cover, extraterrestrial radiation, and day length for Kırklareli, Tokat, Nevşehir, and Karaman. Turkish State Meteorological Service data from 2018–2019 were randomly split 70%/30% for training/testing and evaluated with seven metrics." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564093__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "ANN was best overall, followed by deep learning, SVM, and k-NN. Overall best ANN metrics were R²=0.932, RMSE=2.157 MJ/m², rRMSE=14.10%, MABE=1.597 MJ/m², MBE=0.195 MJ/m², t-stat=1.280, and MAPE=15.92%. k-NN was generally worst" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564093__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Nevşehir was most predictable and Tokat least predictable." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564093__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Most solar-radiation stations lack measurement equipment, while different machine-learning models can have close and region-dependent results that require multi-metric comparison." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564093__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Benchmarks four algorithms with seven metrics across four provinces spanning Turkey’s solar-radiation range." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564093__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Evaluate additional attributes and regions to refine algorithm selection." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564093__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Four Turkish provinces and two years of data" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564093__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "performance varied with province and metric." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564100__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564100__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hourly solar radiation prediction for photovoltaic installations" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564100__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Built two single-hidden-layer feed-forward ANN models in MATLAB Simulink with 1–15 neurons and Levenberg–Marquardt, resilient back-propagation, and scaled conjugate gradient training. Used NREL hourly direct/global irradiation, weather, and location attributes for six Tamil Nadu districts" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564100__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Model 1 trained on five districts and tested on Vellore, while Model 2 used an 80/20 split across all districts." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564100__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Model 1 with Levenberg–Marquardt and 12 hidden neurons was best, with R=0.9376 training and R=0.9340 testing. Its testing MAD, MSE, RMSE, and MAPE were 0.045632, 0.005781, 0.076342, and 0.484634, respectively. Model 1 was more stable than Model 2." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564100__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "High acquisition and maintenance cost of meteorological instruments leave many locations without solar-radiation records for PV design." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564100__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Develops and selects an ANN configuration that estimates hourly direct and global radiation from readily available meteorological and locational inputs." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564100__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Apply the ANN model to estimate hourly radiation at comparable locations without monitoring facilities." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564100__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Study covered six hot-area Tamil Nadu locations, one year of data, and the selected inputs/models." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564524__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564524__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "monthly global solar radiation prediction" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564524__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Trained and tested standalone ANFIS and hybrid ANFIS-PSO, ANFIS-GA, and ANFIS-DE models on monthly sunshine duration, maximum/minimum temperature, rainfall, and clearness index. Used 108 Kuala Terengganu months (2006–2014) with an 80/20 split and applied the models to Penang Island." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564524__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "ANFIS-PSO was best. At Kuala Terengganu it achieved test RMSE=0.3065, RRMSE=1.7933%, r=0.9963, R²=0.9921, MABE=0.2482, and MAPE=1.4097%. All models had RRMSE below 10%" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564524__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "ANFIS-GA had longest execution time while standalone ANFIS was fastest." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564524__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Malaysia has missing or scarce solar-radiation records due to costly, complex measurement equipment, and comprehensive high-accuracy hybrid ANFIS monthly models for tropical settings were lacking." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564524__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Uses routine meteorological variables with ANFIS and three optimisation hybrids, then validates at a second Malaysian site." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564524__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Expand the monthly solar-radiation database, calibrate models in other regions, and optimise execution time." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1564524__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Model performance requires the specified meteorological inputs and was evaluated for two Malaysian sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565340__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565340__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "photovoltaic generation potential and economics" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565340__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Compared satellite-derived GHI datasets with ground measurements from 22 cities in six countries, selected SolarGIS based on lowest error, and used pvPlanner to assess optimally tilted crystalline silicon, amorphous silicon, and CIS PV at 33 Cameroon locations. Calculated energy output, performance ratio, capacity factor, simple payback, and LCOE under cost, discount-rate, and generation scenarios." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565340__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "SolarGIS had the lowest RMSE (7.9%). a-Si produced the highest energy output, PR, and CF across Cameroon. Adjusted annual output ranged 1053–1764 kWh/kWp. At 1500 €/kWp, 5% discount and 1764 kWh/kWp/year, payback was 5.6 years and LCOE was 6.79 €c/kWh" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565340__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "at 2500 €/kWp, 10%, and 1053 kWh/kWp/year, they were 15.7 years and 28.82 €c/kWh." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565340__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Cameroon lacks reliable weather observations and PV performance data, limiting resource assessment and investment confidence." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565340__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Validates satellite datasets using neighbouring-country observations and quantifies location-specific PV energy performance and investment economics in Cameroon." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565340__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Facilitate PV deployment in commercial buildings and adopt policies such as duty exemptions, low-interest loans, and tax breaks." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565340__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "SolarGIS data had 7.9% average GHI overestimation and no reliable Cameroon surface-observation network" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565340__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "economics rely on assumed costs, tariffs, degradation, and demand profile." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565343__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565343__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "short-term solar photovoltaic power forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565343__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Downloaded four years of hourly PVGIS/ERA5 data for a 20 kW Bamenda PV system, preprocessed 35,064 records to 33,000, split 80/20 for training/testing, and trained/validated/tested 24 MATLAB Regression Learner models from six technique families. Compared hold-out (25% of training held out) and re-substitution validation using RMSE and R²." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565343__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Wide neural network was best on hold-out testing with RMSE=9.377 W and R²=0.999" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565343__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Matérn 5/2 GPR (9.452 W) and exponential GPR (10.299 W) followed. Fine Gaussian SVM was least accurate (RMSE=458.97 W, R²=0.990). Hold-out validation was more accurate for 62% of models." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565343__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Cameroon has little machine-learning solar-PV forecasting research and lacks ground measurements with all required inputs/outputs for Bamenda." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565343__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Compares 24 ML models and validation methods on PVGIS data to choose a dependable Bamenda SPVP forecaster." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565343__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Deploy the selected model to the cloud for real-time forecasting and evaluate at additional locations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565343__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Data are PVGIS satellite/reanalysis estimates for a single location" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565343__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "findings cannot be generalised and the model was only used within MATLAB." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565347__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565347__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "diffuse solar radiation estimation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565347__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed location-specific quadratic relations between diffuse-to-global radiation ratio and clearness index using 1985–2005 HelioClim-1 monthly mean daily horizontal-surface data for Ngaoundéré, Garoua-Boulai, Bafoussam, and Nkambé. Compared results with Page, Liu–Jordan, Iqbal, and Erbs models using MBE, RMSE, and t-statistic." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565347__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The proposed quadratic models achieved diffuse-fraction R² of 0.983–0.989 and t-statistics within the 95% critical range, giving closest agreement with observations. Existing models consistently underestimated diffuse radiation and had t-statistics outside the critical range." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565347__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Global and diffuse solar radiation are not measured by Cameroon meteorological stations, and existing general diffuse-radiation models may not represent local conditions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565347__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Derives and validates four local clearness-index quadratic models for diffuse-radiation estimation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565347__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Use the location-specific model as a diffuse solar-radiation data-generation scheme where observations are absent." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565347__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Analysis relies on satellite-derived monthly mean data and four cities between 5°N and 10°N." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565351__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565351__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "photovoltaic resource and energy-output estimation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565351__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Estimated Bambili hourly irradiance with Angstrom–Prescott, Kaplanis, Duffie and Beckman, and Collares-Pereira and Rabl models" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565351__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "estimated temperature with WAVE, Parton and Logan, and SOYGRO" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565351__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "then computed PV-module energy output and compared results with NASA data, PVGIS, and PVsyst." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565351__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Collares-Pereira and Rabl gave the lowest irradiance RMSE (6.71%). Parton and Logan performed best from 6 a.m. to noon (7.17% RMSE), while SOYGRO was preferred from 1 to 6 p.m. (9.86% RMSE). Estimated annual module energy ranged from 193.29 to 345.87 kWh." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565351__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Irradiance and temperature data are scarce in Bambili because meteorological stations are unavailable." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565351__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Applies day-of-year mathematical models to estimate irradiance, temperature, and PV energy output." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565351__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Incorporate environmental disturbances such as sudden cloudiness and rain to improve estimates." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565351__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Bambili has no meteorological station" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565351__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "NASA data are satellite-derived rather than local ground measurements." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565354__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565354__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "solar resource assessment" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565354__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Evaluated Hargreaves and Samani, Annandale, Bristow and Campbell, and Goodin temperature-based regressions for daily global solar radiation at two Cameroon and two Senegal localities. Used RMSE, MBE, t-statistic, coefficient of determination, and Willmott concordance index." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565354__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Annandale performed best in Yaounde" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565354__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Goodin performed best in Garoua, Dakar, and Gandon. Annandale and Goodin estimates were statistically significant at the 99% confidence level where their calculated t values were below 2.5758." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565354__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Observed global solar-radiation data and records are unavailable at many developing-country localities." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565354__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Compares four empirical temperature-based regressions across representative Cameroon and Senegal locations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565354__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Apply the simple temperature-based models for solar-system design where only air-temperature data are available." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565354__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Ground radiation measurements were unavailable for Garoua and Dakar" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1565354__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "satellite-based NASA data were used for validation at those sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1566035__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1566035__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "solar resource climatology" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1566035__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Analysed HelioClim3-v5 satellite global, diffuse, and direct solar-radiation data" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1566035__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "in-situ meteorological observations" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1566035__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "and SAFNWC cloud classes for Douala. Applied hierarchical clustering with Euclidean distance and Ward aggregation to hourly global-solar-radiation diurnal cycles." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1566035__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Douala has a bright dry DJF season (~5000 Wh/m²/day), a dark rainy JJAS season (<3500 Wh/m²/day), and two semi-illuminated transition seasons. Five diurnal radiation-cycle types represent 42%, 14%, 18%, 16%, and 10% of the 4017 analysed days." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1566035__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Douala requires a local characterization of annual and diurnal solar-radiation variability and its meteorological drivers." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1566035__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Characterizes seasonal and daily solar-radiation profiles and their cloud-cover associations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1566035__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Quantify cloudiness and aerosol effects and analyse regional climate response." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1566035__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Further work is needed to quantify cloudiness and aerosol effects on the solar-irradiation balance." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567953__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567953__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind-concentrated-solar power operation optimization" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567953__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Proposed a wind-CSP-electric-heater hybrid, formulated day-ahead scheduling as a MILP with energy-flow, TES, power-block, electric-heater and curtailment constraints, and tested clear-sky, partial-cloudy and annual cases." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567953__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The electric heater reduced generation-plan deviation and wind curtailment: clear-sky deviation fell to 0%, partial-cloudy deviation fell from 47.49% to 31.74%, and annual wind curtailment was reduced by more than 90% for 151 days." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567953__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Existing wind-CSP studies operate the subsystems independently and lack additional measures when wind curtailment occurs." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567953__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Curtailed wind power is converted by an electric heater into heat stored in CSP thermal energy storage for later generation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567953__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Study optimal ratios among wind power capacity CSP capacity and TES capacity considering performance and economy." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567953__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The case uses scaled BPA wind data, NSRDB irradiation data and steady-state component models" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567953__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "dynamic CSP processes are ignored." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567974__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567974__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "residential solar wind and hybrid system comparison" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567974__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Used SAM PVsyst HOMER and RETScreen to model and validate grid-connected residential PV wind and PV-wind systems in Thailand using solar irradiance wind speed demand and financial inputs." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567974__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "PV model annual-yield errors were 3.6% SAM 6.9% PVsyst 5.5% HOMER and -3.9% RETScreen. A 6.6 kW PV system was best in Chaiyaphum" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567974__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "6.05 kW PV plus 1 kW wind was best in Sa Kaeo" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567974__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "only Chanthaburi supported an economic hybrid among seven sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567974__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Thai PV wind and hybrid applications lacked validated multi-tool comparisons across regions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567974__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Validated four tools and compared PV WTS and hybrid options across nine Thai locations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567974__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Use local measurements and broader real-system validation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567974__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Model results depend on database weather and limited reference-system data" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567974__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "actual output can diverge from modeled annual values." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568004__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568004__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "wind-concentrated-solar thermal-storage hybrid optimization" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568004__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed and validated wind farm CSP thermal energy storage electric-heater and power-block submodels" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568004__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "used PSO to optimize capacity ratio TES duration solar multiple and heater capacity for an 80 MWe Zhangbei case." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568004__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The optimal configuration had wind-to-CSP ratio 1.91 TES capacity 13 h solar multiple 2.9 and heater capacity 6 MW, giving NPV USD 27.67 million and 15470 tCO2/year reduction." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568004__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Wind curtailment and intermittency reduce the economic performance and stability of high-wind systems." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568004__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Stores curtailed wind electricity as heat in CSP thermal energy storage and optimizes configuration with PSO." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568004__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test alternative weather pricing and dispatch cases." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568004__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "CSP validation used SEGS VI output in California and the case relies on assumed pricing dispatch and design parameters." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568024__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568024__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "grid-connected hybrid solar-wind power control" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568024__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Modelled a 2 MW DFIG wind turbine and 50 kW PV system connected through back-to-back converters in MATLAB Simulink" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568024__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "applied vector control P&O and PSO solar MPPT and indirect-speed wind MPPT." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568024__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The control strategy maintained DC-link voltage under step-up and step-down wind changes and produced rated 2 MW at 11 m/s" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568024__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "PV MPPT tracked maximum power under constant and real-time irradiance." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568024__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Efficient stable grid integration and maximum power extraction from combined PV and DFIG wind systems require coordinated control." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568024__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Integrated PV at the DFIG converter DC link with independent solar and hybrid wind MPPT." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568024__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Validate the controller experimentally and test broader grid and weather scenarios." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568024__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Simulation-only evaluation without hardware experiments or a detailed numerical comparison of P&O and PSO tracking performance." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568778__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568778__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "Ethiopian renewable-energy-sector review" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568778__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Reviewed national electricity statistics, wind-resource assessments, energy policy, and ongoing or planned wind, geothermal, and hydropower projects" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568778__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "compared CESEN, SWERA, meteorological, and project-site evidence." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568778__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Ethiopia had an estimated 10000 MW wind resource but only 52 MW operating wind capacity by December 2012. Eight wind farms totaling 1116 MW were planned, while hydropower supplied 92.7% of electricity in 2010/2011" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568778__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "dry-season winds could complement drought-sensitive hydro." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568778__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Sparse reliable wind data and extreme reliance on hydropower limited Ethiopian wind-energy development and exposed supply to rainfall and drought risk." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568778__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Synthesized resource maps site measurements policies and the 1116 MW wind-project pipeline to show wind's diversification value." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568778__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Collect standardized site measurements" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568778__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "formulate a long-term diversified-energy plan" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568778__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "improve incentives and financing" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568778__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "revise policy to enable more private investment." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568778__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "National wind maps relied on sparse, nonstandard-height observations and 10 km mesoscale modeling that omitted local effects" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568778__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "reported projects and plans reflect the review's 2012–2013 evidence base." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582661__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hydropower potential assessment" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "DEM and stream-network GIS analysis screened sites by stream order, bed slope, and spacing. SWAT2000 simulated flows for 60 subwatersheds" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "flow-duration curves at 50%, 75%, and 90% dependability supported theoretical run-of-river potential estimates." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "107 sites on nine streams were identified. At 50% dependability, the estimated theoretical potential was 132.67 MW" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "68 micro sites below 0.5 MW provided 10.8% of that capacity. Developing half the potential could reduce emissions by about 125 thousand t CO2." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Traditional outlet-based gauged-data assessments can miss potential sites and provide limited spatial coverage." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Integrated GIS site identification and calibrated SWAT simulation to provide spatially distributed hydropower potential." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Undertake geologic, population, demand-center, and site-feasibility studies" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "assess hybrid solar, biomass, and hydropower supply options." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Rainfall and temperature data were sparse for the watershed" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "soil mapping at 10 km² grid resolution could miss finer variation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582661__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "sites are theoretical and require practical feasibility investigation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1594719__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1594719__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "renewable energy adoption strategy prioritization" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1594719__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Identified barriers through literature review, refined them with 12 experts, linked barriers to strategies using adapted QFD, weighted seven criteria with AHP, ranked 38 strategies with Fuzzy ARASKOR, and compared rankings with nine fuzzy MCDM methods." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1594719__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Seventy-five barriers and 38 strategies were identified. Policy stability and long-term commitment ranked first, followed by promoting renewable energy as a climate solution and developing training and certification programs." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1594719__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Barrier research is fragmented and generally does not link comprehensive barriers to feasible, prioritized mitigation strategies." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1594719__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Developed and tested an integrated QFD, AHP, and Fuzzy ARASKOR framework in Iran." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1594719__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test alternative MCDM methods, add evaluation criteria, and use advanced fuzzy representations such as type-2 fuzzy sets." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1594719__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Results rely on a limited expert panel and Iran-specific contextual data" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1594719__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "alternative strategies, criteria, or perspectives may change outcomes." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1637917__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1637917__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "municipal renewable-energy decision-making" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1637917__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Province-wide survey of Alberta municipal decision-makers, analyzed with descriptive statistics and a theory-informed binary logistic regression that combines the Theory of Planned Behaviour and transition theory." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1637917__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Economic value was the leading motivation. Key constraints were access to grants and loans, limited provincial support, and concern that projects diminish natural vistas. Visual impact (odds ratio 1.81) and external challenges (odds ratio 0.63) were significant predictors of adoption intention." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1637917__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Municipal community-energy development and direct insights from municipal leaders have received limited empirical attention." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1637917__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Surveyed decision-makers across Alberta and applied a blended behavioural and transition-theory framework." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1637917__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Conduct in-depth municipal case studies and examine how broader landscape-level factors incentivize local renewable development." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1637917__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The unknown survey reach prevents a response-rate calculation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1637917__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "renewable-energy labelling may cause selection bias, and results cover 101 respondents from 74 Alberta municipalities." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638041__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638041__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "UK renewable-energy innovation policy" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638041__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "A UK Department of Trade and Industry study (March–June 2003) applied a National Systems of Innovation framework, technology-maturity stages, and system maps to six technology sectors." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638041__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "System failures occur chiefly from demonstration to pre-commercial deployment and from pre-commercial to supported commercialisation. Stable policy, niche-market support, stronger risk/reward ratios, knowledge sharing, and skills development are needed." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638041__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Innovation-systems approaches had not been widely applied to UK renewable technologies or systematically related system failures to technology-maturity stages." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638041__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Mapped actors, knowledge, influence and funding flows and characterized failures along the innovation chain." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638041__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Develop stronger and more detailed recommendations for overcoming specific system failures and barriers to long-term UK renewable options." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638041__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "A policy-focused, time-limited snapshot underemphasises learning processes and does not provide a full international comparison." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638049__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "European renewable-electricity policy" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Conceptual specification of carbon lock-in barriers in renewable generation, transmission and distribution grids, storage, and demand response, followed by a policy review of existing instruments and reform needs." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Generation policies are widespread but grid, storage, and demand-response measures remain immature. Carbon lock-out requires simultaneous barrier removal, integrated EU-wide planning, coordinated scenarios, and partly harmonised policy rules." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Existing renewable-electricity support is fragmented across Member States and insufficiently addresses non-generation components of the electricity system." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Reviewed policies across generation, grid, storage, and demand barriers and specified an integrated EU policy portfolio." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Develop coordinated, transparent European electricity scenarios and continue research on policy challenges of renewable deployment." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Conceptual policy review" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638049__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "it does not rank barriers or policy responses and recognizes that many areas require further research." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638054__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638054__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "renewable-energy investment barriers" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638054__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Online questionnaire of renewable project representatives used a five-point barrier-importance scale and quota sampling. Sixty responses were complemented by five face-to-face semi-structured interviews." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638054__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Grid connection constraints and lack of capacity were the highest-rated barrier (4.35/5), followed by lengthy permitting (4.16), land/water lease securement (3.90), and limited project finance (3.71)." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638054__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "No prior study had examined renewable-deployment barriers in Chile from investors’ perspectives, including Chile-specific mining-concession and grid-regulation issues." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638054__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Prioritized 18 barriers with investor/developer survey data and follow-up interviews." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638054__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Examine barriers by technology and investigate government and financial-institution perspectives, including project-risk assessment under differing regulations and procedures." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638054__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Barrier relevance varies by technology" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1638054__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "quota sampling is non-probabilistic and cannot provide generalisable population estimates or robust sampling-error estimates." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1639011__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1639011__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "Sub-Saharan African renewable-energy adoption" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1639011__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Stakeholder-centred synthesis of literature and real-world case studies of South Africa’s REIPPPP, Kenya’s Olkaria geothermal project, Rwanda’s Gigawatt Global solar project, and Tanzanian solar mini-grids." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1639011__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Technical, financial, policy, and socio-cultural barriers are intertwined. Successful initiatives combine stable policy support, innovative financing, capacity building, and broad stakeholder/community engagement." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1639011__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Renewable-energy barriers in Sub-Saharan Africa require an integrated stakeholder perspective spanning governments, private entities, financial institutions, and communities." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1639011__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Synthesized barriers and case-study lessons into coordinated strategies for policy reform, finance, capacity building, and public engagement." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1639011__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Develop context-specific regional assessments, support localized research and pilot projects, and strengthen knowledge transfer between research and market deployment." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1639011__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The synthesis emphasises diverse regional contexts" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1639011__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "strategies and barriers vary by country, technology, and stakeholder group." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567645__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567645__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hydrological data assimilation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567645__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Applied dual state-parameter Ensemble Kalman Filter (EnKF) to extended SAC-SMA, assimilating streamflow only, soil moisture only, or both" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567645__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Hydrus supplied areal soil-moisture observations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567645__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Combined assimilation gave more accurate soil-moisture and streamflow forecasts, especially at 1–14-day lead times. Streamflow-only assimilation distorted soil moisture" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567645__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "soil-moisture-only assimilation gave inaccurate flow." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567645__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Hydrological DA can update streamflow while producing unvalidated and distorted soil-moisture states." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567645__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Compared three dual-EnKF observation-assimilation strategies for state and forecast variation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567645__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Assess remotely sensed soil-moisture products and particle-filter/Markov-chain Monte Carlo approaches." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567645__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Only point soil-moisture observations were available, so Hydrus-simulated sub-basin averages were used as observations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567665__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "flood forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Calibrated WRF-Hydro at four USGS gauges then used evolutionary particle-filter Markov-chain Monte Carlo data assimilation to independently and jointly assimilate USGS streamflow and SMAP soil moisture at 36 km 9 km and 1 km." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Joint streamflow and 1-km SMAP assimilation improved streamflow across regimes. During normal flow 1-km SMAP outperformed coarser products" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "during Hurricane Harvey soil-moisture resolutions had similar effects." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Hyper-resolution hydrologic forecasts have uncertainty in states parameters forcing and observations, while the value of multivariate remote-sensing assimilation was insufficiently tested." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Evaluated independent and joint assimilation of satellite soil moisture and in-situ streamflow in a distributed WRF-Hydro model." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Improve observation quality over water bodies and extend high-resolution multivariate assimilation studies." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "SMAP retrievals are degraded over water bodies such as Lake Livingston" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "point stream gauges provide limited spatial soil-moisture correction." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567682__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567682__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hydropower decision support and hydraulic data assimilation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567682__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed sequential three-phase multi-metric tuning for control-theory-based data assimilation. A 1D DiffW1D river hydraulic model of the Iron Gate 1 Danube reach is continuously updated by PID-controller correction flows derived from water-level discrepancies." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567682__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The PI configuration Kp=10 and Ki=10 substantially improved assimilation: RMSE was 0.02 m at assimilation points and 0.07 m at the validation point. Adding derivative gain offered no benefit up to Kd=1000 and extreme derivative gain caused instability." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567682__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Uncertain initial and boundary conditions degrade model-driven near-future hydropower forecasting, while standard data-assimilation methods can be slow or difficult to apply operationally." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567682__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Uses PID controllers as a simple, control-theory-based data-assimilation method with sequential multi-metric initial tuning." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567682__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Test numerical-model complexity effects and perform individual-controller fine tuning with multi-objective optimization." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567682__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The study uses a synthetic test scenario and identical controller gains across all assimilation points." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567698__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567698__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hydrological data assimilation for hydropower forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567698__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Applied ensemble Kalman filtering to an E-HYPE sub-model for the Umeälven catchment. Assimilated in-situ discharge and reservoir inflow plus satellite fractional snow cover, snow water equivalent, actual evapotranspiration, and potential evapotranspiration" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567698__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "assessed ensemble size and 63 single and combined assimilation experiments using KGE gains." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567698__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Ensembles of 25 members sufficed for most products, while discharge and reservoir inflow required 100. Thirteen combinations improved both target variables" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567698__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "in-situ observations outperformed satellite products except fractional snow cover, and MODIS potential evapotranspiration did not generally improve target forecasts." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567698__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "The value of assimilating multiple satellite and in-situ products at distinct spatial and temporal scales for hydrological target predictions had not been established." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567698__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Objectively selects EnKF ensemble size and tests single and multi-product assimilation combinations for discharge and reservoir-inflow prediction." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567698__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Assess other evapotranspiration products and translate reservoir-inflow prediction gains into economic gains." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567698__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Passive-microwave snow-water-equivalent data were unreliable in highland and coastal areas, and MODIS potential evapotranspiration may be biased." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567729__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567729__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hydropower inflow forecasting and snow data assimilation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567729__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Assimilated early-April snow-water-equivalent observations at three Refsdal sites into a distributed conceptual Shyft hydrological model using a stochastic EnKF. For 15 snowmelt seasons, forecasts were run for 120 days and benchmarked against an unassimilated base case." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567729__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Assimilation improved seasonal inflow forecasts in 7 of 15 years, with large improvements in 2001 and 2010 and only small degradation in 3 years. The lowest forecast MAE (6%) was achieved with Grønebotn and Katledalane observations" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567729__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Ovridsfjell alone produced the worst MAE (15%)." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567729__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Manual snow-observation updates in Norwegian hydropower forecasts are labor-intensive, non-reproducible, and lack an objective systematic method." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567729__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Tests objective EnKF assimilation of peak-accumulation SWE observations to improve long-lead inflow forecasts." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567729__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Develop snow-sampling designs tailored to gridded ensemble updating and improve meteorological forcing and snowmelt modelling." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567729__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The sampling scheme was not designed for ensemble updating" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567729__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "precipitation forcing may underestimate solid precipitation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567735__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567735__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "basin-scale hydrological data assimilation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567735__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed SWAT-HDAS by coupling the gridded parallel SWATGP distributed hydrological model with PDAF. Conducted synthetic OSSEs assimilating soil moisture, snow water equivalent, and discharge with an EnKF in the Babaohe River Basin." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567735__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Assimilation improved soil-moisture, SWE, and streamflow estimates. More and more-downstream discharge observations improved outlet streamflow estimation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567735__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "an 18-site configuration was best. Assimilating discharge alone was as good as multivariable assimilation for streamflow in the synthetic experiments." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567735__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Basin-scale hydrological studies need a flexible system that can assimilate multi-source observations into a physically based distributed model at high spatial resolution." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567735__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Integrates SWATGP and PDAF into SWAT-HDAS and demonstrates multiscale synthetic soil-moisture, snow, and discharge assimilation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567735__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Extend observation operators for microwave and cosmic-ray soil-moisture observations and assess localization, smoothing, scaling, and observation-error effects." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567735__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Experiments used synthetic observations and assumed model and observation error statistics" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567735__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "real applications require realistic error settings and suitable observation scaling." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567757__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567757__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "satellite hydrological data assimilation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567757__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Compared dynamics-driven Square Root Analysis (SQRA) and data-driven Kalman–Takens filtering in W3RA. Assimilated GRACE terrestrial water storage and AMSR-E/SMOS soil moisture separately and jointly at 5-day resolution over the Murray–Darling and Mississippi basins." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567757__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Joint GRACE-plus-soil-moisture assimilation gave the largest improvements. SQRA case 3 was best in Murray–Darling (groundwater RMSE 24.85 mm, correlation 0.80)" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567757__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Kalman–Takens case 6 was best in Mississippi (27.11 mm, 0.84). Kalman–Takens was about six times faster and performed comparably to SQRA." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567757__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "The comparative value of dynamics-driven and data-driven assimilation frameworks for different combinations of satellite water-storage and soil-moisture products was unclear." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567757__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Assesses SQRA and Kalman–Takens using separate and joint GRACE and satellite soil-moisture assimilations against independent in-situ measurements." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567757__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Assess further data-driven assimilation applications where physical-model error is large." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567757__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Physical-model errors can reduce performance of model-driven assimilation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567757__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "satellite soil moisture mainly updates shallow layers, and data required bias correction." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567776__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567776__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hydropower reservoir energy-generation forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567776__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Trained separate feed-forward multilayer-perceptron networks with sigmoid activation functions on monthly Kainji and Jebba reservoir data. Inputs were inflow, storage, elevation, turbine release, net head, plant-use coefficient, tailrace level, and evaporation loss" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567776__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "output was energy generation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567776__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The 8–7–1 networks produced test-set correlations of 0.89 for Kainji and 0.77 for Jebba, indicating reliable energy-generation forecasts from reservoir variables." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567776__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Hydropower reservoir management requires understanding complex relationships between reservoir variables and energy generation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567776__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Uses MLP neural networks to model monthly energy generation as a function of eight reservoir variables." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567776__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Use reservoir-variable forecasts to support hydropower operation and energy prediction." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567776__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The study evaluates historical monthly data from only Kainji and Jebba reservoirs." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567813__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567813__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "small-scale hydropower potential assessment" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567813__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Measured monthly river discharge with the velocity-area method, estimated gross hydropower potential with a UNIDO model, and used flow-duration curves to assess flow dependability." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567813__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Ovia had the highest annual power yield (61.6189 MW)" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567813__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Ikpoba, Orlie, and Edion yielded 14.7868 MW, 9.819 MW, and 5.4956 MW." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567813__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Hydrological characteristics and small-hydropower potential of most Edo State rivers are not fully understood because reliable discharge data are scarce." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567813__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Generated monthly discharge and hydropower-potential evidence for four Edo State rivers." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567813__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Conduct a comprehensive technical and socioeconomic viability appraisal of small-scale hydropower development." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567813__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The study was limited to streamflow analysis." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567836__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567836__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hydropower environmental-impact decision support" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567836__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Applied output-oriented variable-returns-to-scale DEA with an inverted frontier to derive three partial indices and a scaled Hydropower IPAT Index for 53 proposed Brazilian projects. Trained 7–4–1 ANN impact-prediction and 3–3–2 SHP/LHP classification models in SPSS." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567836__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "All top-10 low-impact projects were SHPs, while 7 of the 10 worst-ranked projects were LHPs. Selected ANN prediction model 5 achieved R²=0.963, test MSE=0.0001, and MAD=0.026" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567836__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "selected classification model achieved 99.0% accuracy." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567836__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Brazil lacks standardized, specific criteria to compare and classify hydropower projects by local environmental impact across different production scales." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567836__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Combines DEA-derived IPAT impact indexing with ANN prediction and SHP/LHP classification for 53 projects." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567836__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Include other indicators and theoretical models and compare alternative machine-learning methods." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567836__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The index uses a selected set of local IPAT indicators and does not constitute a definitive energy-policy assessment." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567855__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567855__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "micro-hydropower resource and financial feasibility assessment" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567855__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Measured Sombriero River surface velocity with a weighted wooden float over a 22 m reach, estimated mean velocity with a 0.6 tolerance factor, calculated cross-sectional area using the trapezoidal rule, calculated power from discharge, head, and efficiency, and performed RETScreen financial simulation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567855__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Measured discharge was 1.99 m³/s. At 3.5 m head and 0.75 efficiency, potential output was 51.25 kW. A run-of-river micro-hydropower scheme was viable at a US$127.61/MWh tariff, with US$920 NPV, 22.6% equity IRR, 19.5% asset IRR, benefit–cost ratio 1.01, and 4 years 6 months equity payback." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567855__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "The Sombriero River’s discharge, micro-hydropower potential, and financial feasibility had not been quantified for decentralized electricity supply." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567855__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Combines float-method flow measurement, power calculation, and RETScreen financial analysis for a run-of-river micro-hydropower scheme." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567855__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Use a standard current meter and 1–2 years of hydrological data, and prepare detailed civil, electro-mechanical, and transmission cost estimates." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567855__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Wooden-float measurement and short April–July record limit flow-estimation accuracy" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567855__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "civil works, turbine-generator, hydraulic, and transmission costs need real-time detailed costing." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567877__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567877__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "small-hydropower dam site suitability modelling" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567877__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Integrated ten hydro-physical thematic layers with GIS and AHP to create an upper Benue SHP dam-suitability map. Used a semi-automatic ArcGIS contour–stream-order–suitability intersection and SQL query to identify narrow valleys, then evaluated five sites by field survey." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567877__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Very high suitability covers 11,111.2 km² (7.5%) of the watershed and high suitability covers 40,327.2 km² (27.4%). Map validation achieved ROC AUC 79.67%" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567877__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "18 suitable dam sites were selected from 636 narrow valleys. Field/model valley widths correlated at 0.71, though the semi-automatic approach underestimated field widths by 7.1–33.1%." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567877__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Previous dam-suitability mapping studies often do not explicitly explain how potential sites are spatially identified and selected across large watersheds." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567877__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Combines GIS–AHP suitability mapping with semi-automatic narrow-valley identification and field validation for upper Benue SHP dam sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567877__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Use very high-resolution data, especially DEM data, to improve semi-automatic valley-width estimation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567877__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Thematic inputs have varied spatial and temporal resolution" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567877__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "five of 18 sites were field surveyed because other sites were remote or inaccessible." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567889__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567889__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "regional theoretical hydropower-potential and climate-impact assessment" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567889__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "An annual Choudhury-Budyko water-balance model was regionally calibrated with discharge data from 410 gauges to simulate annual discharge across more than 500,000 river reaches. The model was driven with 15 CORDEX-Africa regional climate models under RCP4.5 and RCP8.5 using a delta-change method, then theoretical line and specific hydropower potential were calculated from discharge, reach head, and length." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567889__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The most promising theoretical potential is in Guinea, Sierra Leone, Liberia, and south-eastern Nigeria. The ensemble median does not indicate a considerable West Africa-wide decrease in annual discharge over the next decades, though warming increases evapotranspiration and regional rainfall signals are mixed." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567889__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Hydro-meteorological data and spatially complete discharge and hydropower-potential evidence are inadequate across much of West Africa." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567889__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Provides a region-wide, reach-scale theoretical-potential and climate-impact screening framework." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567889__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Publish interactive ECOWREX map layers and use the results to target sub-basin studies and discharge-measurement campaigns." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567889__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Observed discharge records contain gaps, biases, and georeferencing errors" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567889__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "precipitation products also introduce uncertainty. The theoretical potential is an upper limit because it assumes full discharge and head are turbinated and excludes spillway losses and environmental-flow constraints." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567909__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567909__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "groundwater potential assessment" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567909__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Integrated vertical electrical sounding (VES), Landsat 8 imagery, SRTM DEM, geological mapping, and GIS thematic layers using analytic hierarchy process (AHP) weighted overlay." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567909__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The Ogun basin was delineated into high (21%), moderate (31%), low (6%), and very-low (42%) groundwater-potential zones" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567909__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "AHP consistency ratio was 0.04." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567909__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Groundwater occurrence and storage potential in the Ogun drainage basin require spatially integrated assessment." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567909__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Combined hydrogeophysical observations with remote sensing and GIS multi-criteria mapping and validated against resistivity surveys." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567909__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Add detailed VES data, well data, and pumping-test results to improve and validate the groundwater-potential map." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567909__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "VES validation was limited to 20 soundings at Abeokuta and Ewekoro" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1567909__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "the RS/GIS map can be pessimistic relative to VES-derived potential." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568509__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568509__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "small-hydropower feasibility assessment" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568509__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Used SRTM DEM ArcHydro GIS PERSIANN-CDR rainfall NIMET validation and NRCS-CN runoff modelling" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568509__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "constructed Q92 flow-duration curves and screened 58 points for slope and head." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568509__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Rainfall and discharge correlations were 65% and 63%. Eleven points met 2% slope and 10 m head criteria, with 393.849–16038.194 kW potential at 92% annual exceedance." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568509__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Poorly gauged Nigerian rivers lack hydrological information for small-hydropower planning." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568509__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Combined GIS RS and NRCS-CN modeling to assess Oyanmi SHP potential." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568509__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Conduct detailed site feasibility and longer-term hydrological monitoring." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568509__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Rainfall and flow validation covered only 2018 and site screening remains preliminary." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568525__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568525__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hydrokinetic energy potential assessment" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568525__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "SWAT, interfaced with MapWindow GIS, simulated watershed hydrology" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568525__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "calibrated flow and hydraulic head derived from a digital elevation model were used to calculate theoretical river hydrokinetic potential." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568525__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Awun River had the highest estimated potential (154.82 MW)" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568525__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Oyun and Asa were estimated at 98.39 MW and 41.63 MW." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568525__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Hydrokinetic potential of Nigerian river currents is largely unexplored." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568525__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Applied SWAT in a GIS environment to estimate potential for selected Asa watershed rivers." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568525__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Harness assessed river potential with appropriate technology for nearby communities." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568525__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Potential estimates may be affected by turbine design, turbine type, efficiency, deployment mode, and river use." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568565__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568565__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "small run-of-river hydropower potential assessment" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568565__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Constructed a flow-duration curve from seven years of daily flow, subtracted residual flow, modeled turbine efficiency and power-duration curves, integrated annual energy, and compared turbine and head alternatives." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568565__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "At 46.5 m net head and average flow, a single Kaplan turbine was projected at 8.774 MW, 50018 MWh/year, and 65.1% capacity factor with 148 days at rated output. Minimum-flow configurations could operate for 365 days at 97.8% capacity factor." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568565__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Nigeria lacks relevant small-hydropower data and a comprehensive inventory of potential sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568565__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Quantified flow-dependent turbine performance and energy production for a proposed Opeki River plant." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568565__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Only seven years of flow records were available" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568565__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "the average-flow configuration was not highly dependable and required standby capacity during dry periods." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568577__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568577__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "Nigerian small-hydropower spatial screening" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568577__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Used ArcGIS overlay of UN-FAO water areas waterline shapefiles and administrative boundaries across six geopolitical zones" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568577__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "used 200 m–5 km buffers and IDW suitability interpolation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568577__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Mapped high SHP potential in Borno Niger Edo Anambra and Jigawa. The north-east had 151 potential small-dam sites and Yobe 55 inland-water sites" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568577__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "north-west had 95 potential small-dam sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568577__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Nigeria lacks a comprehensive nationwide ArcGIS assessment of small-hydropower sites and supporting hydrological data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568577__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Produced national zonal maps and statistics to guide preliminary SHP site prioritization." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568577__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Conduct field flow head environmental social and feasibility studies at mapped locations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568577__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The assessment lacks site-level elevation head and flow information and is constrained by data availability GIS expertise and missing environmental and stakeholder data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568594__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568594__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "small-hydropower resource assessment" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568594__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Applied ArcHydro remote sensing GIS and NRCS Curve Number rainfall-runoff modelling to 148 drainage-network points" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568594__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "derived flow-duration design discharges and heads" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568594__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "then used SHPRASA for turbine cost and emission screening." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568594__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Eighteen of 148 points could yield 677.485–7622.877 kW at 92% flow exceedance, avoid 555.8–6543.0 tCO2/year, and cost GBP 937167.48–4048733.99." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568594__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Data-scarce river basins lack an efficient basin-wide method to identify technically economically and environmentally viable SHP sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568594__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Established SHPRASA as a GIS and NRCS-CN based SHP screening and sustainability workflow." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568594__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Undertake detailed field and feasibility studies at promising sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568594__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Screening-level assessment based largely on modeled peak discharge and limited gauge data" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568594__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "detailed engineering and field feasibility remain required." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568609__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568609__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "ungauged-basin hydropower potential assessment" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568609__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Transferred recent flow from the similar Gumera catchment using an area-ratio approach" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568609__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "simulated daily Beshilo flows with SWAT" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568609__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "calibrated with SUFI-2" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568609__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "screened GIS and field-survey sites using flow, head, spacing, construction, and sediment criteria" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568609__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "built Weibull flow-duration curves" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568609__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "and calculated power at three dependability levels." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568609__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Nine run-of-river sites were identified. Total potential was 9.866 MW at 90% dependable flow, 37.765 MW at 75%, and 184.098 MW at 50%. Site 1 was strongest at every level, reaching 2.320, 8.900, and 42.750 MW." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568609__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Recent observed Beshilo flows are unavailable despite the need to identify hydropower resources for rural electrification and regional power deficits." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568609__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Combined catchment-similarity flow transfer, SWAT simulation, GIS screening, and field observations to quantify nine sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568609__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Conduct detailed engineering and economic feasibility assessment of the proposed sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568609__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The Beshilo River lacked recent gauge records, requiring regionalized Gumera flows. Results require detailed technical and economic feasibility studies before development." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568654__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568654__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "GERD hydropower-design evaluation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568654__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Applied a satellite-driven 0.1 degree VIC hydrological model with routing and a reservoir-operation optimization model to simulate 37 years of GERD inflow storage releases turbine use and generation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568654__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Upper Blue Nile hydrology could support 13629 GWh/year at capacity factor 0.30" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568654__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "in the current configuration eight of 14 turbines would likely be idle annually. The 5150 MW design was judged more reasonable than 6000 and 6450 MW alternatives." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568654__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "GERD's ability to meet declared design generation and whether its capacity is oversized had not been evaluated from Upper Blue Nile hydrology." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568654__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Linked long-term hydrologic simulation to reservoir operation and turbine-capacity scenarios." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568654__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Assess climate and sedimentation impacts and peak-versus-base load operations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568654__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Operational optimization used assumed downstream-damage penalties and did not assess future climate-change or sedimentation effects in detail." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568665__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hydro-kinetic turbine resource assessment" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Converted 25 years of discharge records into velocity and power density using SRTM DEM ArcGIS HEC-GeoRAS HEC-RAS and field velocity depth and width measurements." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Maximum extractable power density was 1.4 kW/m2 in Gumara 3.4 kW/m2 in Gilgel-Abay and 2.6 kW/m2 in Bahirdar-Abay" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "24.5% 31.7% and 29% of their reaches respectively met velocity thresholds." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "River velocity records required for hydro-kinetic turbine assessment are generally unavailable although discharge records exist." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Coupled public GIS hydraulic modeling and low-cost field validation to estimate velocity and power density." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Obtain better spatial velocity and turbine-power-curve data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Historical discharge is not velocity data" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "bathymetry was limited and HKT power-curve averaging lacks a standardized convention." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568768__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568768__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "pumped hydro-energy storage site selection" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568768__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Integrated ALOS PALSAR terrain data, Sentinel-2 land cover, geology, rainfall and infrastructure layers in ArcGIS Pro" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568768__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "applied AHP weighting and weighted GIS overlay within 10 km of seven existing reservoirs." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568768__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Head was the highest-weighted criterion (29.8%), followed by head-to-distance ratio (17.9%), slope (15.9%), TWI (11.7%), lineaments (6.9%), grid proximity (6.3%), river proximity (5.8%), and road proximity (5.6%). Very-high suitability covered 2.6 km2 (0.17%)." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568768__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Selecting viable pumped-storage locations around Ethiopian reservoirs requires integrating topographic hydrologic geological and infrastructure constraints." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568768__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Produced a national PHES suitability map using GIS-based MCDA and AHP." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568768__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Conduct detailed reservoir-pair design capacity environmental and economic evaluations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568768__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "A screening study without detailed engineering, economic, environmental, social, or reservoir-pair feasibility" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568768__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "criteria weights are subjective." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568773__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568773__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "run-of-river hydropower potential assessment" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568773__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Used ArcSWAT with 30 m DEM land cover soil weather and streamflow inputs" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568773__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "calibrated and validated flow" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568773__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "screened fourth-order streams by head and spacing" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568773__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "and used flow-duration curves to estimate theoretical power." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568773__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Reported 33 sites in results and 20 in the conclusion. Results reported 3039, 1127, and 805 kW at 90%, 75%, and 50% dependability" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568773__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "the conclusion instead reported 12744, 2538, and 603.1 kW at 50%, 75%, and 90%." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568773__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Limited integrated spatial and hydrological evidence for screening hydropower sites in the Temcha watershed." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568773__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Applied GIS and SWAT to screen sites and simulate flows along the watershed." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568773__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Assess land-cover change river morphology and hydrology and optimize head and spacing criteria." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568773__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Site-count criteria and aggregate outputs are internally inconsistent" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568773__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "geological and other nonhydrological feasibility criteria were not assessed." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568785__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568785__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "climate-change impacts on hydropower" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568785__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Calibrated Poli-Hydro for the Blue Nile and Omo basins, downscaled 21 CMIP5/CMIP6 climate projections, and used Poli-Power and Poli-Price to optimize GERD and GIBE III operation under no-release and environmental-release scenarios through 2100." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568785__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "GERD production generally increases by mid-century and then moderates by end-century" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568785__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "GIBE III production generally increases. Constrained and unconstrained GERD operation produced similar results, and an approximately five-year GERD filling period performed best." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568785__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Prospective climate change may alter water availability, reservoir management, and Ethiopian hydropower production." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568785__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Coupled hydrological, climate, price, and reservoir-operation models to project GERD and GIBE III production through 2100." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568785__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Use longer and more recent streamflow series, obtain plant energy-production data, and investigate a larger climate-scenario ensemble." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568785__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Hydrological, production, and price observations were sparse" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568785__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "only calibration was possible" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568785__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "future GCM, RCP, and SSP projections embed uncertainty." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568790__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568790__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "run-of-river hydropower potential assessment" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568790__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Combined 12.5 m DEM-based GIS screening, daily SWAT simulation and SUFI-2 calibration, inverse-distance parameter regionalization, flow-duration curves, the hydropower equation, and AHP-weighted GIS multicriteria ranking." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568790__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Identified 103 sites with heads of 20–81 m. Total theoretical potential was 183.16, 125.96, and 33.03 MW at 50%, 75%, and 90% flow exceedance" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568790__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "regionalized SWAT performance was satisfactory at two verification gauges." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568790__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Data scarcity and costly field surveys impede comprehensive multi-site run-of-river assessment in Ethiopian basins." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568790__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Transferred calibrated SWAT parameters to ungauged sites and integrated GIS-derived head with dependable flow and multicriteria ranking." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568790__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Assess run-of-river potential at sub-basin scale and undertake detailed implementation studies for prioritized sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568790__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Sparse and potentially inaccurate inputs increased hydrological uncertainty, and SWAT reproduced peak flows poorly" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568790__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "the assessment remained a screening-level theoretical analysis." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568806__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568806__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "watershed surface-water potential and small-hydropower site selection" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568806__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "ArcSWAT, driven by terrain, land-use, soil, daily meteorological, and observed-flow data, delineated 15 sub-basins and 66 HRUs, calibrated and validated streamflow, and simulated flows at three candidate sites. Q90 flow-duration analysis, DEM-derived gross head, the hydropower equation, and AHP/MCDM were used to estimate and rank theoretical candidates." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568806__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Calibration R², NSE, and PBIAS were 0.84, 0.78, and −4.6%" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568806__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "validation values were 0.81, 0.72, and −4.8%. Q90 was 0.37, 0.45, and 0.48 m³/s at sites 1–3" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568806__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "corresponding gross heads were 15, 25, and 20 m and theoretical power was 54.45, 110.36, and 94.18 kW. Site 2 was selected as best." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568806__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "The Megecha watershed lacked integrated surface-water modelling and technically ranked hydropower-site evidence." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568806__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Integrates calibrated ArcSWAT, geospatial gross-head assessment, dependable-flow analysis, and MCDM site ranking." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568806__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Conduct detailed river-flow field surveys and update hydrological and meteorological data systems." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568806__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Detailed field verification of the full river flow was constrained by budget" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568806__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "authors note the need for improved hydro-meteorological data collection and field survey." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568816__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568816__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "geospatial gross-head assessment for hydropower site screening" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568816__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "A 12.5 m DEM and ArcGIS derived the Furfuro watershed, flow accumulation, Strahler stream order, and potential head. Fourth- and fifth-order streams were screened for at least 8 m head and 1,000 m spacing, and Google Earth Pro head drops were compared with handheld GPS readings at four accessible locations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568816__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Four potential hydropower sites were identified on fourth- and fifth-order streams. Google Earth Pro versus GPS head drops produced R² 0.994 and NSE 0.997, supporting use of DEM, Google Earth, and GPS for head screening." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568816__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Accurate head data and hydropower-potential information are lacking for many Ethiopian perennial rivers." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568816__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Provides validated, low-cost geospatial screening of potential head and candidate reaches on the Furfuro River." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568816__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Assess Furfuro River discharge and undertake technical and economic feasibility studies for hydropower development." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568816__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The study estimates head only" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568816__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "it does not report discharge, power capacity, technical feasibility, or economic feasibility for the candidate sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568828__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568828__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "micro-hydropower site identification, potential assessment, and rural microgrid supply" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568828__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "ArcGIS, Arc Hydro, HEC-GeoHMS, and Global Mapper derived terrain, river profiles, head, and contributing area. GPS measurements corrected river-profile head" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568828__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "an area-ratio method transferred flow to ungauged sites, Weibull FDCs supplied Q90, technical power and annual energy were calculated, HOMER modeled Alefa Kacha supply at site 8, and AHP ranked nine sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568828__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Nine run-of-river sites total 660.01 kW technical potential and 5,608.222 MWh/year. Hp site 8 has 151 m corrected head, 0.30 m³/s design flow, 305.87 kW technical potential, and 2,599.04 MWh/year" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568828__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "it ranks first. HOMER reports 4,018,758 kWh/year hydro output versus 483,123 kWh/year load, or 88% excess." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568828__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Remote Gilgel-Beles communities lack cost-effective grid access and lack a prioritized micro-hydropower resource and site assessment." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568828__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Combines geospatial site selection, corrected head, dependable flow, technical potential, rural load simulation, and ranking for nine candidate sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568828__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Use the ranking to prioritize detailed micro-hydropower feasibility and development, including surveys and assessments at the selected sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568828__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Field GPS head validation covered only three sites" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568828__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "flow was transferred to ungauged sites and feasibility relies on available DEM, flow, and assumed efficiency inputs. Detailed field, engineering, environmental, and economic investigation remains needed." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568843__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568843__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "theoretical hydropower potential comparison of three Ethiopian rivers" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568843__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "The study used ten years of daily flow data from MoWE, converted it to mean flow and Weibull FDCs, used QGIS and GPS Visualizer to analyse topography, calculated net head, and estimated theoretical output with a cross-flow turbine at 80% efficiency and an assumed 20 m net head." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568843__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Chemoga has the highest theoretical output in high, moist, and mid-range flow at 4,729.20, 3,495.49, and 2,133.08 kW. Wabe has the highest dry and low-flow output at 1,023.37 and 673.35 kW" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568843__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Wabe also has the largest elevation change, 333.34 m per 11.1 km. Huluka is lower in every condition." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568843__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Many Ethiopian rivers suitable for small-scale hydropower have insufficient flow and topographic potential assessment." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568843__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Provides a scalable FDC-plus-topography framework that compares theoretical hydropower potential under five flow conditions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568843__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Identify specific small, mini, and micro-hydropower sites along the rivers and assess detailed technical, economic, and environmental feasibility." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568843__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Topographic information was not supplied by MoWE, and a 20 m head and 80% cross-flow efficiency were assumed" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1568843__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "actual head, efficiency, economics, environmental impacts, and site feasibility require further assessment." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569160__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569160__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hydropower-dam impacts on water availability and riverine hydrology" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569160__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Mapped 2000, 2010, and 2020 LULC from Landsat, modelled Bui water yield with InVEST using climate, soil, terrain and LULC data, validated yields against Bui-gauge discharge, and compared pre/post daily Black Volta flow with IHA/RVA." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569160__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Water yield increased from 3.25 MCM in 2000 to 4.75 MCM in 2020. Forest cover fell from 81.42% to 35.80% while urban cover rose from 10.76% to 41.45%. Bui Dam altered timing and pulses: dry conditions extended 92.43 days, peaks arrived at least 10 days earlier, and low-pulse duration fell from 44.98 to 2.33 days." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569160__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Dam planning insufficiently quantifies trade-offs between hydropower operation, water provisioning, natural flow regimes, and riverine ecosystems." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569160__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Integrates land-cover change, InVEST water yield, and IHA/RVA evidence to quantify Bui Dam hydrological effects." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569160__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Adopt adaptive dam management and integrated water-resource planning that protects environmental flows and ecosystem services." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569160__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "InVEST is pixel-based and does not explicitly represent baseflow" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569160__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "three benchmark years limit validation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569160__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "water-yield changes reflect interacting climate, land-use, and dam-operation effects." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569361__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569361__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "small-hydropower site assessment and cascade design" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569361__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "SWAT simulated flow from remote-sensing, soil, weather, and gauge inputs, calibrated with SUFI-2. Nine sites were screened by head and spacing" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569361__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "FDC/PDC analysis determined firm flow, power and energy, and storage/turbine options were evaluated for a cascade." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569361__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Nine sites have combined 7.89 MW firm power. HP1, HP4, and HP7 have annual energy of 28.68, 12.68, and 14.36 GWh and form a recommended 55.72 GWh/year cascade." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569361__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Densu small-hydropower investment is constrained by limited hydrological information." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569361__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Provides SWAT-based siting, energy estimates, and a storage-cascade recommendation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569361__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Government agencies should explore Densu energy potential and undertake detailed cascade feasibility." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569361__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Site data are modelling-based and require detailed technical, environmental, and economic feasibility assessment." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569504__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569504__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "small hydropower potential and techno-economic assessment" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569504__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Used 30 m SRTM DEM and GIS criteria to locate sites" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569504__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "simulated monthly streamflow with SWAT using climate, land-cover, soil, and donor-catchment gauge data" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569504__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "calibrated and validated the model" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569504__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "constructed flow- and power-duration curves at 90% dependability" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569504__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "and assessed run-of-river and dam projects with RETScreen." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569504__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Six dam and three run-of-river sites provide 117.72–2356.2 kW firm power and 0.60–12.07 GWh firm energy per site. Dam site 1, run-of-river site 1, and dam site 6 were recommended as a cascade totaling 21.65 GWh annually. Both RETScreen cases were financially viable." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569504__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Few Ghanaian studies assess both dam and run-of-river small-hydropower siting together with economic feasibility." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569504__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Identified and quantified nine Pumpum River sites and evaluated dam and run-of-river financial cases." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569504__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Assess climate-change flows, flood risk, and detailed engineering, geological, and hydrological conditions at the proposed sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569504__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Daily streamflow was unavailable, so monthly modeled flow and regionalization from the Bamboi donor catchment were used. SWAT may have difficulty resolving localized small-project effects." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569514__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569514__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "small hydropower potential assessment" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569514__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "GIS screened Lower Pra sites" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569514__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "calibrated SWAT generated flows" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569514__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "FDC/PDC analysis calculated firm power and energy" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569514__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "storage and Francis-turbine cascade options were assessed." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569514__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Ten sites were identified. HP1, HP3 and HP7 provide 12.22, 10.00 and 9.00 MW firm power and 183.77, 157.67 and 141.91 GWh annual energy" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569514__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "their proposed cascade totals 483.4 GWh/year." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569514__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Ghanaian small-hydropower potential has not been assessed in depth." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569514__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Provides SWAT/GIS-based site and cascade evidence." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569514__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Explore Densu Basin potential through detailed feasibility studies." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1569514__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Potential sites require detailed technical, economic and environmental feasibility assessment." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1580088__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1580088__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hydropower reliability and hydroclimatology" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1580088__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Satellite and in-situ hydroclimatic observations were combined with random-forest models to reconstruct Lake Malawi levels and Shire River discharge. Beta regression quantified discharge-extreme effects on hydropower capacity factor" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1580088__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "log-linear OLS related extremes to urban nighttime-light radiance." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1580088__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "A dry discharge extreme reduced total hydropower capacity factor by 9.4 percentage points and monthly urban nighttime lights by 31 percentage points. Random-forest discharge reconstructions had KGE 0.96–0.99 and NSE 0.94–0.99 across gauges." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1580088__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Reliable continuous monitoring of hydropower performance is difficult where hydrological and generation data are sparse." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1580088__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Used publicly available satellite data and machine learning to fill discharge-record gaps and assess reliability impacts." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1580088__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Integrate hydropower-operation optimization and examine diversified generation and transboundary transmission options." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1580088__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Satellite-data calibration and interpolation can introduce error" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1580088__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "thresholds for extremes are arbitrary" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1580088__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "no hydropower-operation or optimization model was used." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581270__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581270__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hydropower production forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581270__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Monthly production and precipitation data were normalized, split chronologically into 75% training and 25% testing data, and used in grid-searched MLP, LSTM, and sequence-to-sequence LSTM models. Walk-forward validation assessed one-step and twelve-step forecasts." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581270__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The differentiated univariate MLP was best in both scenarios: RMSE 4.09 GWh for one-step and 123.84 GWh for twelve-step forecasting. ANN forecasts outperformed ARIMA and ARIMAX in the 2015 comparison." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581270__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "There were no comparable recurrent-neural-network studies for a medium-size region with a long period of changing installed hydropower capacity." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581270__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Evaluated MLP, LSTM, and seq2seq LSTM forecasting designs for Ecuador over 2000–2015." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581270__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Use more observations, latent recurrent neural networks, transformers, and super-resolution methods." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581270__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The dataset had limited observations" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581270__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "exhaustive grid search is computationally costly for larger datasets." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581274__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581274__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hydroelectricity generation forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581274__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Hourly generation from Aslantaş and upstream Ceyhan River HPPs, meteorological reanalysis, market prices, and calendar variables were cleaned and used to train/test CatBoost, XGBoost, and LightGBM regressors with 80/20 random sampling. Tree count and learning rate were tuned." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581274__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "LightGBM was best, with R² 97.07%, RMSSE 0.1217, and 1.240 s runtime at 1,000 trees and learning rate 0.10." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581274__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Direct head-to-head benchmarks of CatBoost, LightGBM, and XGBoost for hydroelectricity generation under identical constraints are lacking." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581274__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Introduced basin-aware predictors using upstream HPP generation and benchmarked three tree-based models." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581274__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Develop hybrid hydrological-ML approaches, real-time rolling retraining and drift monitoring, and cross-basin testing." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581274__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Results are specific to the Ceyhan basin" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581274__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "transferring the framework requires basin-specific retraining and independent validation. ML-only dispatch could be unreliable during extreme inflows." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581530__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581530__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hydroturbine power prediction" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581530__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Developed an improved multilayer neural network with ReLU activation, L2 regularization, Adam optimization, and adaptive inverse normalization" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581530__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "optimized LSSVM hyperparameters with an improved grey wolf algorithm" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581530__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "evaluated both on axial-flow propeller and Francis turbine operating data." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581530__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "IGWO-LSSVM achieved the best reported relative errors: 1.61% for axial-flow propeller data and 0.41% for Francis data. Adaptive inverse normalization improved neural-network prediction and produced 3.06% and 1.73% best-scenario relative errors, respectively." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581530__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Conventional 3D hydrodynamic turbine models have long design cycles and complex solutions, while manual LSSVM parameter selection is uncertain and empirical." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581530__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Provided fast data-driven turbine-power predictors for both small- and large-sample operating conditions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581530__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Reduce subjectivity in selecting the IGWO optimization range." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581530__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The IGWO multi-parameter optimization range still depends on subjective experience and may bias turbine-power predictions" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581530__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "the operational data are confidential." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581536__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581536__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "power-generation mix forecasting and low-carbon transition" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581536__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "ANFIS models forecast monthly shares of thermal, hydropower, nuclear, and non-hydropower renewable generation. Single-factor sensitivity analysis and 59,049 multi-factor scenario combinations assess influence mechanisms." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581536__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Under the standard scenario in 2025, thermal, hydropower, nuclear, and non-hydropower renewables account for 60.46%, 20.43%, 6.43%, and 12.68%. EHV/UHV transmission primarily benefits hydropower, while rapid urbanization, industrial upgrading, and demand growth increase thermal-power share." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581536__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Direct quantitative forecasts of China’s generation structure and systematic evidence on its macro drivers are scarce." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581536__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Modeled generation shares directly rather than using installed-capacity shares as a proxy." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581536__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Develop large-scale energy storage, more flexible market mechanisms for peak/frequency regulation, and policy measures beyond UHV projects." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581536__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Future indicator scenarios are based on assumptions" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581536__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "energy storage was omitted because samples were insufficient for machine learning." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581542__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "short-term hydropower production prediction" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Split 2005–2017 Karun-III data 80/20 for training/testing" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "used binary salp swarm optimization for lag selection and continuous SSA for hyperparameters" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "benchmarked nine standalone and serial hybrid neural/Bayesian models at 1-, 2-, and 3-day horizons" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "evaluated predictive accuracy and 95% interval uncertainty." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "CNNE-MUPE-GPRE was most accurate and least uncertain, with test RMSE of 595, 600, and 612 kW and NSE of 0.93, 0.91, and 0.90 at 1-, 2-, and 3-day horizons. Accuracy declined with horizon. Its 1-day PICP/PINW were 0.99/0.05." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Existing ANN approaches do not automatically extract time-series features, robustly select inputs and parameters, or quantify predictive uncertainty." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Integrated convolutional feature extraction, multilayer nonlinear learning, Gaussian-process uncertainty, and salp-based automated selection." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Combine CNNE with BI-LSTM or LSTM for spatiotemporal learning and extend the approach to energy monitoring and early-warning applications." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Forecast skill and uncertainty deteriorated at longer horizons" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1581542__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "the study used a single dam and two physical predictors with lagged inputs." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582665__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "run-of-river hydropower potential assessment" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Calibrated and validated SWAT with observed discharge, generated ten years of spatially distributed flow, ranked dependable years, and combined modeled flow with digital-elevation-model-derived head in GIS to identify candidate sites and calculate theoretical power." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Thirty-three candidate sites were identified" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "total potential was 3039 kW at 50% dependability, 1127 kW at 75%, and 805 kW at 90%." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Reliable site assessment in remote hilly terrain is constrained by costly surveys and sparse flow observations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Demonstrated a GIS, remote-sensing, and calibrated SWAT workflow for hydrological screening of hydropower sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Examine candidate sites using geological, environmental, access, demand, and economic criteria and optimize head and spacing thresholds." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Only one river gauging station was available" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582665__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "geological suitability, accessibility, demand, and ability to pay were not evaluated." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582683__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582683__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "small-hydropower potential zoning and site screening" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582683__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Prepared DEM, land-cover, soil, slope, drainage, flow-direction, rainfall, evapotranspiration, and water-yield raster layers" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582683__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "simulated daily hydrology with SWAT using 17 years of data" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582683__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "calibrated and tested parameter sensitivity with SUFI-2" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582683__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "reclassified equal-resolution 5 km2 grids" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582683__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "and applied weighted-sum overlay analysis." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582683__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Four hydropower-potential zones and ten tentative SHP sites were identified: seven in the upper catchment and three near the outlet, where optimum suitability occurred. Rainfall and water yield were most important for potential strength, while slope and streams guided site location." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582683__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Ground-intensive hydropower surveys are slow and ineffective for initial catchment-scale identification of small-hydropower zones and sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582683__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Provided an integrated raster-based hydrological and multicriteria screening workflow for a rainfall-dependent inland catchment." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582683__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Improve input quality, conduct ground and structural surveys, use climate-scenario data, and add reservoir-operation and dynamic hydrological optimization." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582683__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The ten sites are tentative" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582683__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "exact turbine heads, discharges, turbine types, technical feasibility, and structural surveys were not assessed. Model outputs depend on structure and data quality." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582734__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582734__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "small hydropower site identification using remote sensing" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582734__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "A Visual Basic expert system applied fuzzy C-means clustering to RGB intensity values in IRS-1D LISS III geocoded false-color imagery, then interpreted water bodies, forest/vegetation, habitation, settlements, and snow to screen probable sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582734__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "The remote-sensing method provided a systematic way to extract water-resource and surrounding-feature information for small-hydropower site selection in plains and inaccessible mountains. It was demonstrated for the Ganga and Alaknanda rivers and compared with Survey of India topographic sheets." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582734__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Few studies clearly integrate satellite-image interpretation with water-resource and site-selection information for hydropower development in inaccessible hilly terrain." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582734__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Developed a VB-based image-classification and expert-system workflow for hydropower resource screening." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582734__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Develop a regional flow-duration model and extend the method to water-conveyance facilities such as canal heads and canal drops." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582734__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The work did not provide a cost comparison with conventional surveys. Remotely sensed imagery needs interpretation and supporting field data" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582734__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "a regional flow-duration model remains to be developed." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582754__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582754__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "small hydropower carbon-finance potential" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582754__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "State technical capacity, regional grid emission factors, and a 35% plant load factor were used to estimate annual electricity and certified emission reduction potential. A logistic diffusion model projected standard and optimistic capacity, electricity, and CER scenarios to 2020." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582754__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "India’s technically feasible 10.27 GW small-hydropower potential could generate 31.49 TWh/year and 23.65 million CERs/year at 35% load factor. Projected annual CERs are 7/20 million in standard/optimistic scenarios by 2012 and 13/24 million by 2020." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582754__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "The CDM potential of Indian small hydropower had not been estimated comprehensively despite its potential to reduce emissions and support rural development." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582754__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Estimated national and state-level small-hydropower CER potential and modeled its diffusion under standard and optimistic conditions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582754__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Introduce supportive policies and use CDM bundling to lower transaction costs and accelerate small-hydropower diffusion." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582754__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The assessment is preliminary and macro-level" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582754__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "project additionality, hydrological/geological risk, policy conditions, and plant load factor determine realizable CERs." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582764__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582764__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "run-of-river hydropower sustainability and development barriers" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582764__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Policies, project reports, environmental documents, and secondary data were reviewed. Field visits, interviews with technical experts and developers, and group discussions with local residents assessed project impacts and barriers, using the 48 MW Lower Kalnai project as a case." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582764__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Jammu and Kashmir has 20,000 MW hydro potential, but administrative clearances, Indus Treaty constraints, difficult terrain, severe climate, social acceptance, security, and high costs slow development. A 4,000 MW development could meet the state power shortfall" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582764__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Lower Kalnai’s carbon-credit benefit lowers estimated generation cost from Rs 3.90 to Rs 3.36/kWh." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582764__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Most large-hydropower sustainability research concerns reservoir projects, with little evidence on without-reservoir run-of-river projects in the western Himalayan region." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582764__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Identified RoR-specific sustainability indicators and project-development barriers through field investigation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582764__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Conduct mandatory social-impact assessment for projects above 25 MW" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582764__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "use multi-criteria/AHP ranking" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582764__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "establish single-window clearance and improve local participation, monitoring, and benefit sharing." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582764__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Impacts and sustainability-factor intensity vary between projects" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1582764__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "field evidence is case-specific and needs longer-term social-impact assessment." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1583336__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1583336__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "rainfall-based regional hydropower potential assessment" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1583336__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Compiled Indian rainfall records for 1931–2022, calculated state/subdivision descriptive statistics, compared rainfall with installed hydro capacity, visualized rainfall series, examined basin-area distributions, and assigned qualitative regional hydropower-potential classes from annual-rainfall ranges." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1583336__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Arunachal Pradesh, Coastal Karnataka, Lakshadweep, Kerala, and Konkan-Goa had the highest rainfall. The Western Ghats, Northeast India, and Himalayan region were classified as high potential" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1583336__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "large-basin states were also considered favorable for hydropower development." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1583336__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "India requires regionally resolved analysis linking long-term rainfall and basin characteristics to hydropower-development suitability." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1583336__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Combined long-term rainfall statistics, basin distributions, and installed capacity information to screen favorable Indian regions." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1583336__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Refine rainfall-based analysis with detailed local topographical and hydrological data and integrated water-cycle variables." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1583336__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Rainfall alone cannot predict hydropower performance" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1583336__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "site-specific topography, water availability, flow, storage, infrastructure, snowmelt, and glacial runoff are also required. The reported potential classes are broad regional observations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586317__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586317__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hydropower generation-capacity prediction" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586317__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Applied SVR and XGBoost to Hawaii reservoir-resource data, optimized each with Aquila, slime mould, and grey wolf algorithms, analyzed input correlations and Delta Moment-Independent sensitivities, and compared test predictions using six statistical metrics." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586317__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Standalone XGBoost outperformed SVR. XGBoost-SMA was the best test model with R2=0.9713, RMSE=18.73, and MAE=6.19. System water volume was the most influential input, followed by transmission spurline cost and total dollar per kW." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586317__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Traditional regression and autoregressive methods struggle with nonlinear and nonstationary hydropower relationships, while optimized XGBoost hybrids remain underexplored." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586317__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Benchmarked standalone and metaheuristically optimized SVR and XGBoost models for Hawaii hydropower capacity." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586317__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Incorporate additional datasets and algorithms, including deep learning, and develop real-time prediction systems." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586317__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Results depend strongly on input-data quality" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586317__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "only SVR and XGBoost families and one geographic case were tested" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586317__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "hybrid optimization adds computational cost that can hinder real-time use." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586335__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586335__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "daily hydropower generation forecasting" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586335__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Daily precipitation, streamflow, temperature, and energy production were split 70%/30% for training/testing, with 20% of training for validation. AdaBoost, autoencoder regression, DNN, ESN, LightGBM, and ResNet models were compared" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586335__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "LightGBM feature importance ranked predictors." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586335__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "LightGBM was the best model: RMSE 98.27, MAE 73.93, AIC 17,100, NSE 0.69, KGE 0.77, R² 0.69, MBE −5.23, bias factor 1.02, and PBIAS 1.51. Streamflow was most important, followed by temperature and precipitation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586335__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Few studies jointly compare AdaBoost, autoencoder regression, DNN, ESN, LightGBM, and ResNet for daily hydropower prediction while explaining hydro-meteorological feature importance." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586335__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Delivered a multi-model daily benchmark with LightGBM-based feature importance." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586335__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Integrate the approach in operational planning, load balancing, and reservoir operation and expand data/model testing." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586335__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Results use a limited four-year record at one plant" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586335__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "model generalization under changed climate and operational conditions requires additional testing." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586400__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586400__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hydropower generation prediction and optimization" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586400__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "A 1,819-record hydropower dataset was split 80%/20%. CatBoost and histogram gradient boosting were run independently and optimized with Hunger Games Search, Chaos Game Optimization, and Archimedes Optimization Algorithm." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586400__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "CatBoost-HGS was best in testing, with R² 0.90751273, RMSE 45.21301314, MAE 8.89683593, MBE −2.16463953, Willmott index 0.97262189, and Jensen-Shannon divergence 105.508137." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586400__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Standalone prediction methods have difficulty representing complex nonlinear relations among physical, economic, and geographic hydropower variables." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586400__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Integrated CatBoost and HGBoost with three metaheuristic optimizers to improve prediction accuracy and efficiency." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586400__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Extend to real-time and regional/global predictions" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586400__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "include climate, economic and environmental information, deep reinforcement learning, and decision-support systems." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586400__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Data incompleteness and variable hydropower conditions, especially at under-monitored small plants, complicate model calibration and generalizability." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586415__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586415__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "hydropower generation prediction" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586415__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Monthly and quarterly 1993–2019 data were modelled with Gaussian process regression, support vector regression, multiple linear regression, and power regression. Three quarterly seasonal groupings and rainfall-only or multi-weather inputs were evaluated." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586415__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Quarterly data outperformed monthly data. Gaussian process regression was best" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586415__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "for quarterly climatic-data Option 1 it achieved R 0.92, MAPE 4.5%, BIAS −0.4, Nash number 0.9, and RSR 0.3." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586415__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Regression-based prediction using the full set of relevant weather indices at Samanalawewa had been limited." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586415__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Compared four regression techniques across monthly and quarterly meteorological input formulations." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586415__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Apply the selected model with forecast rainfall to predict future power generation at the plant." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586415__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The analysis is confined to one hydropower plant and historical meteorological observations" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1586415__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "rainfall forecasts and unreported operational reservoir variables may affect practical forecasting." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1594693__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1594693__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "rural renewable-energy adoption policy" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1594693__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Conducted a SALSA-structured Web of Science literature review with snowballing" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1594693__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "synthesized rural renewable-energy transition problems, prosumption and cooperative options, barriers and motives, policy responses linked to technology-adoption theory, and success factors." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1594693__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Socio-political and regulatory barriers now dominate as renewable-energy costs decline. Effective initiatives depend on locally specific strategic, institutional, and physical capacities. Regulatory reform, prosumer participation, fair competition, information, training, privacy protection, and tailored economic and non-economic policy packages are needed." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1594693__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Existing research emphasizes urban renewable adoption and lacks an integrated rural-community analysis of barriers, drivers, success factors, and policies." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1594693__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Produced rural-specific barrier, motive, policy, and success-factor frameworks for community renewable-energy initiatives." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1594693__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Tailor policy packages to local adoption stages, community capacities, and adopter characteristics" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1594693__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "phase instruments as technology diffusion advances." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1594693__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "The review is qualitative and the same policies can perform differently across communities because local capacities and conditions vary." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563316__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563316__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "solar radiation estimation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563316__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Compared 105 literature sunshine-duration models and calibrated seven new regression models using Kipp and Zonen pyranometer data from Mugla University (2007-2015)." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563316__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "\"Only models 24 and 35 met ±10% error limits" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563316__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "new models reduced errors below 0.8 and semester-specific cubic/quadratic models performed best.\"" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563316__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "No prior empirical correlation was available for Mugla despite high solar potential." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563316__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Developed calibrated annual and semester regression correlations for Mugla." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563316__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyFutureWorks> "Use semester-specific models and extend calibration to other Turkish sites." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563316__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyLimits> "Solar measurements are difficult to obtain and model validity declines in winter." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563319__study_001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#Study> .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563319__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyDomain> "diffuse solar radiation estimation" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563319__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "Evaluated 72 empirical models in nine categories using diffuse and global radiation and meteorological data from 10 Chinese stations" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563319__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyMethodsSummary> "calibrated 1966-2000 and validated 2001-2015." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563319__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "Best daily models were VIII-3 in NWC, IV-3 in QTP NEC NC, and III-2 in CSC" .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563319__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyKeyFindings> "best monthly models were IV-3, VIII-3, VII-7, VIII-5, and IV-5 respectively." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563319__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapIdentified> "Only 17 of 726 Chinese stations record diffuse radiation." .
<https://w3id.org/thirdwave/data/R1563319__study_001> <https://w3id.org/thirdwave/ontology#studyResearchGapAddressed> "Compared model categories and identified climate- and timescale-specific best models." .
